# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""ProbeStand_OneBoom_Combined.FCMacro - THE probe stand macro (replaces ProbeStand_OneBoom and ProbeStand_OneBoom_Test): a flat 20 mm base (open underneath, ballast of your choice) with the wire tensioner standing on TOP of it (the tip end, upside down),
ball links (M0 .. M5 with the default two booms; M0 .. M3 with one), double-cup connectors (DC, DC2, DC3), NBOOM booms (default 2: a second arm) and a straight TIP TENSIONER END at the free end (TIP_PROBE = True: a scope probe holder instead). No probe head, no carriage, no lead screw.

PRINCIPLE  ONE wire (WIRE_THICK = 2.5 mm) runs through the centre of every ball. When it is tensioned (WIRE_T = 400 N at full size) it presses every ball into its conical
  seat and the friction locks all joints at once; slackening it frees them. Poses are set with the panel and the rotation gizmo (wire_harness.py), which refuse a move that creates a collision.

SCALE  BALL_D is the ball diameter of the finished model and the reference for the scale of EVERYTHING (parts, wire, thread, fits; the wire channel WIRE_HOLE is the exception, see WIRE CHANNEL): 26 = full size (RB = 13, the default),
  8 = the miniature (scale 0.3077). The model is built at the design size and scaled once at the end. Forces scale with the cross-section (wire tension 400 N -> 37.9 N, test weight 100 g -> 9.5 g), masses with the volume.
  At BALL_D = 8 the base is 40 mm square and 6.2 mm high; the two wire drums are printed with the base (radius 1.2 mm there, wire 1.04 mm).

THE BASE (tensioning from the TOP, 20 mm high, open underneath, rounded for printing)
  A flat SQUARE box, 130 x 130 mm with rounded corners (BASE_R = 65 = half the width, BASE_CORNER = 12) and 20 mm high (BASE_H = 20), open at the bottom: there is NO bottom plate. It stands on its 4 mm wall and on a stiffening ring (r 40-43). The deck (4 mm) carries the stand cup, a conical
  hole whose rim is flush with the deck top (MAST_TOP = BASE_H + ZG = 24.5 mm above the table: the ball sits 4.5 mm above the deck, its lower pole hangs 4.5 mm below the deck underside), a collar under it (R 18, 3.5 mm: stiffens the deck
  and the top of the rib that guides the wire), a round hole for the wire (4 mm, STAND_HOLE_R) at XT = 44 mm from the mast (on the side AWAY from the head), beside the end of the rib.
  SCOPE PROBE HOLDER (TIP_PROBE = True, replaces the tip tensioner; PROBE_D = 13, PROBE_CLR, PROBE_LEN, PROBE_OUT, PH_OFF = 26, PH_H, PH_WALL, PH_GAP, PH_TAB, PH_ARM, PH_THREAD_D, PH_THREAD_P, PH_THREAD_DEPTH, PH_SCREW_L, PH_SOCK, PH_KNOB_R): the last link M3 ends in a holder instead of the tip end, slider and screw. The wire is tensioned at the stand end only (the stand end,
  slider and screw are unchanged); at the tip it ends in a crimped ferrule that sits in a pocket under the cup block (open to the bed, 45 deg lead-in) and pulls up into the cup, so the cup carries the 400 N. The probe does NOT run along the wire axis (its cable end would run into the wire and the cup): it lies PH_OFF = 26 mm beside it, parallel to the tip side axis, on the side away from the boom
  (+x of the tip side frame), the tip PROBE_OUT = 45 mm below the clamp. Clamp: a C ring (bore PROBE_D + 2 * PROBE_CLR, wall 3 mm, 18 mm high, opening PH_GAP = 10.5 mm towards +x so the probe snaps in from the side) with two 6 mm tabs (they reach 45 mm from the wire axis, so that both screw holes are full, closed holes with material all round) and a PRINTED plastic clamp screw across them (6 mm, pitch 1.5, 45 deg flanks like the tension screw, fluted knob, 25 mm stub that goes right through the +y tab and sticks out 2.5 mm; Clamp_screw_x1.stl, printed standing on its knob; the thread is printed in the +y tab as a full THROUGH hole, a full teardrop clearance hole in the -y tab): the screw closes the C
  and clamps the probe by hand, no nut, no metal. The holder is printed standing on its bed face, cup up, without supports (cup block, skirt, hollow cavity and windows as the end piece): the only flat roof is the pocket ceiling (4.4 mm bridge). A stand-in of the probe (Tip_Probe, PROBE_LEN = 120 mm, not printed) moves with the holder and
  takes part in the collision tests. The margins use the 100 g test weight 10 mm below the clamp, on the probe axis. Checked at BALL_D = 26: valid single solids (holder 18.4 cm3 / 23.4 g, clamp screw 1.2 cm3 / 1.5 g, through the +y tab, the screw clears the threaded hole: 0 mm3 common), neutral pose without overlaps, wire 0 of 1385 sample points in material, holding margins as in the status line of the panel (J0a 0.8 ... J2d 2.9). Not checked: the miniature (the probe does not scale), the clamp in a real print.
  LENGTH OF THE M LINKS (M_LEN, M_LEN_TIP; in the panel: "M length" box + Rebuild, 36 .. 120 mm, it sets all four M links and rebuilds the model in about 20 s, closing the old one; the pose is carried over if it is still free of collisions): M_LEN = ball-centre distance of M0, M1, M2 and M3 (default 55 mm); M_LEN_TIP > 0 gives the tip side links M2, M3 their own length (then print M0 + M1 and M2 + M3 as two different parts). Limited to 36 .. 120 mm (the range checked in FreeCAD at
  BALL_D = 26: 36, 45, 55, 80, 120 and 70 / 40: valid solids, neutral pose without overlaps, the rounded rod follows). The wire is cut to the new length (45: 544 mm, 55: 584 mm, 80: 684 mm, 120: 844 mm), the probe tip height and the reach follow from the lengths, and the holding margins change:
  longer links are lighter on the margin the wrong way (M_LEN 80: J0a 0.6 ... J2a 0.5; 120: J0a 0.4 ... J2a 0.4), shorter ones better (36: J0a 0.9). M link 16.0 g at 36, 18.1 g at 55, 21.8 g at 80, 27.7 g at 120.
  LIGHTENING WINDOWS (WIN_ON): 8 openings through the 4 mm deck, 3 mm webs (WIN_WEB) left round the wall, the stiffening ring (r 40-43), the collar, the end of the stand, the rib strip and the connector housings, corners rounded R 3 (WIN_R). The collar is held by 3 spokes
  8 mm wide (WIN_SPOKES: -x, +y, -y; +x is the rib) that join it to the ring and the wall; the ring is held by the same spokes and by the webs at the connector housings. 30.1 cm3 / 38 g less at 100 % fill (base 147.6 -> 109.6 g). They are vertical cuts through the deck: nothing overhangs when it is printed upside down, no new overhang (base: the ledge under the ball 16.8 mm2
  and 3 mm2 at the ring notch as before). WIN_ON = False gives the plain deck.
  PRINTABLE BOOM ROD (v45, ROD_FLANGE_R = 10.5): the rod (Boom1_Rod, printed 3 x) was a 3 mm flange disc (R 12.5) with a flat step to the round spigot, so standing on its spigot it needed support under the disc (484 mm2 of overhang). Now the spigot grows into the flange along a 45 deg FILLET CONE (radius 5 -> 10.5 over 5.5 mm height) with no flat rim at all, and the small end face of each cone is extruded into a round STUB (ROD_STUB = 3 mm, radius 5, like a plain spigot) that centres the rod in a pocket of the end piece (round below, 45 deg teardrop roof, 0.5 mm deeper than the stub), the flange is a 3 mm cylinder of radius 10.5, and the socket of the end piece is the matching cone (0.2 mm radial clearance, 0.5 mm deeper, wall at its mouth 1.8 mm). Standing on a spigot end every surface of the rod is within 45 deg of the vertical: 0 mm2 of overhang, no supports; the socket in the end piece adds no overhang either (0.06 mm2). The rod now seats on the two cones (like the balls in their seats) and no longer on a flat flange face: the wire tension closes the 0.14 mm gaps (0.2 mm axial on each side) and centres the rod. A longer rod (BOOM_L > 35) gets 45 deg cones from the flange down to the core and a hollow core with cone ends. ROD_FLANGE_R = 0 gives the old stepped spigot (ROD_STUB = 0: no stub) (also used automatically on a small model where the cone would not fit, and for BOOM_L = 32). Rod 3.5 cm3 / 4.5 g (before 2.0 / 2.5 g), end piece 22.3 cm3 (before 23.3), printed total 324.2 g (the pocket in the end piece adds 0.1 mm2 of overhang), valid solids, no overlaps, wire clear.
  HOLLOW BOOM END PIECES (v46, EP_VOID, EP_WIN): the two end pieces of the boom (Boom1_EPn / Boom1_EPf, the same part printed twice) were solid apart from the wire channel (22.3 cm3, 28.3 g each). Now each has a cavity: in the cup block the same shape as the tensioner end (roof = the seat cone offset by EP_VOID_W = 3 mm, 30 deg from vertical, vertical outer wall), continued down as an annulus round a column of radius 5.5 mm that carries the wire, widened to the wall of the block by a 45 deg cone, and following the elbow for EP_VOID_TILT = 45 deg of its bend (a tube at most 45 deg from the vertical has no roof steeper than 45 deg). The lower end of the cavity is a floor. The wire tube, the wall of the elbow (3 mm) and the lower half of the elbow with the rod socket stay solid. Open windows (EP_WIN: hexagons with vertical sides and a 45 deg roof, so no bridges): six radial ones through the wall of the cup block at EP_WIN_ANG (half width EP_WIN_B = 4 mm) and one through each side wall of the elbow (half width EP_WIN_A = 3.5 mm). 15.6 cm3 / 19.8 g each (-8.5 g, -30 %), printed total 324.2 -> 307.3 g; overhang steeper than 45 deg 425 mm2 (before 433 mm2: nothing new), valid single solids, no overlaps, wire clear, holding margins a little better (J0a 0.77, J2a 0.71, J2d 2.84). EP_VOID = False gives the solid end piece again (also used automatically on a small model, where the wire channel is too wide). A trap met on the way: the boolean operations of the windows with a quarter torus whose seam lies in the plane of the bend fail silently (volume 0), hence bend_tube with a seam turned by 30 deg.
  SECOND ARM (v47, NBOOM = 2 = default, ARM_LINKS = 2): after M3 comes a second boom (Boom2_EPn, Boom2_Rod, Boom2_EPf, the same parts as boom 1), then M4 -> DC3 -> M5 -> tip end. So the chain is
  base -> M0 -> DC -> M1 -> BOOM 1 -> M2 -> DC2 -> M3 -> BOOM 2 -> M4 -> DC3 -> M5 -> tip end: 6 M links, 3 connectors, 4 end pieces, 2 rods; 14 joints (J0a, J0b, J1a, J1b, T1, J2a .. J2d, T2, J3a .. J3d). ONE wire still runs through all balls
  (858 mm cut instead of 594 mm). The stack between the booms hangs from the far cup of boom 1 where that cup opens (ELBOW_ANG[0], default 90 = sideways towards -y); boom 2 starts at its lower ball (the near cup opens back towards the stack), and the tip side
  hangs from the far cup of boom 2 (TIP_ANG, default 90): the arm is stretched out, the tip end at y = -492 mm (TIP_ANG = 270 folds it back into a Z, the tip then ends near the first stack). ARM_LINKS = 0 gives the old loose ball between two booms (J2).
  BALLAST: the 0.4 kg named under THE BASE was worked out for one boom (100 g at 267 mm). With the arm stretched out (tip at y = -492 mm, about 360 g of printed arm and probe) a rough estimate gives 1.5 .. 2 kg (not verified; a folded pose or the start pose needs far less): or clamp the base to the table.
  PRICE: the holding margins fall. The wire loses exp(-0.25 * pi / 2) = 0.675 of its tension in each of the two bends of every boom (0.456 per boom), and the lever arm of the 100 g test weight grows from 267 to 492 mm: worst-case margin x0.29 at J2a
  (before: x0.71). Remedies: less friction in the bends (MU_W: PTFE tube in the end pieces, lubricated wire: 0.10 gives 0.73 per boom), TPU seats, a lighter probe, a shorter M_LEN, a folded pose.
  COLLISION TEST SPEED AND SAFETY (v47): the pose panel tests every move for new overlaps with boolean operations. (1) The three parts of one boom (end pieces and rod) are never tested against each other: a twist only turns them about their common
  axis, and the boolean operation between their coaxial faces never returned at some twist angles (FreeCAD froze while boom 2 was dragged). (2) A move stops at the first new overlap, the pair that blocked the last move is tried first, and while the mouse stays in a blocked
  zone nothing is recomputed (a blocked drag step: 11 s -> 0.01 s). (3) The end pieces and the probe holder are tested with simpler stand-ins (PROXY: solid inside, the holder without the helical socket of the clamp screw). (4) The slow threaded parts, the base, the tip end and the holder
  are kept on disk (BREP in the temp folder, ProbeStandCache; the key is the text of this macro, so a changed macro rebuilds them): a run takes 6.5 s instead of about 16 s.
  LIGHTER TENSIONER (TE_VOID, KNOB_DISH): the cup block of the end piece is hollow: a closed cavity between the seat cone and the outer wall (walls TE_VOID_W = 3 mm square to the seat and at the outside, floor flat, roof 30 deg from vertical, so nothing new overhangs when it is printed
  standing on its end wall; the wire tube round the bore stays 3.5 mm thick), 3.0 cm3 / 3.8 g less per end (28.3 -> 24.5 g); the knob of the tension screw has a 45 deg conical dish (radius 8 mm) in its outer face, which stands on the bed (-0.7 g each, 6.25 -> 5.57 g). The slider is unchanged (its thread takes the
  400 N and its sides are the bearing faces in the trough); the tail of the end (trough walls 3 mm, end wall 4 mm) was already thin. Printed total 346.9 -> 337.8 g with TE_VOID and KNOB_DISH alone (332.1 g with the windows below), valid, neutral pose without overlaps, holding margins as before (J0a 0.7 ... J2d 2.4). All three switches are for 100 % fill; with sparse infill the saving is smaller.
  OPEN WINDOWS IN THE END PIECE (TE_WIN): the walls of the tail (side walls 3 mm, back wall 3.5 mm) have two hexagonal windows each (11 mm wide, vertical sides, 45 deg roof and sill: no bridge when it stands on its end wall), one above the other, 4 mm strut between them; they start 3 mm above the floor
  of the trough and end 3 mm below its eaves, so the end wall, the vault and the corner columns stay. Six hexagonal windows (8 mm wide, flat sill at the cavity floor, 45 deg roof) open the cavity of the cup block to the outside at 0, 45, 135, 180, 225 and 315 deg (the ears at 90 and 270 deg and the column behind them stay). The load-bearing
  section of the tail is at least 110 mm2 (was 186) for the 400 N of the wire (3.6 MPa), that of the cup block at least 224 mm2. The end piece is now 17.0 cm3 / 21.6 g (28.3 g without TE_VOID and TE_WIN), the overhangs are unchanged (only the 9.4 mm bridge over the trough). The slider stays solid: the thread takes the 400 N, its sides are the guide in the trough (the windows
  in the side walls leave the struts between them and the corner columns as guides). The knob keeps its dish (through holes do not fit between its flutes).
  THE STAND TENSIONER IS THE TIP END, UPSIDE DOWN ON THE DECK, COMPLETELY EXPOSED: Stand_TE + Stand_Slider + Stand_Screw are the tip end, the tip slider and the tension screw, the same parts as at the tip (TIP_SLOT = 1 for both).
  Its cup (not used, it opens onto the deck) is at the bottom, the tail with the trough, the end wall and the knob point UP: the rim plane of the cup lies on the deck (TZ0 = BASE_H + TD - ZG = 27.5 mm is the origin of the screw axis),
  the outer face of the end wall is at z = 83.5 mm (ZEW), the knob reaches 95.7 mm. The trough is OPEN OUTWARD (away from the mast) and so is the slot of the slider: wire hole, ferrule pocket, slider, thread and knob can all be seen and reached.
  It is THE SAME PART as the tip end (SAME_END = True; print two of them, Tip_end_x2.stl). Two small EARS on the outside of the cup block (6 mm long, 2.5 mm out of the block, 1.5 mm above the rim plane, 45 deg underside) drop into two through slots of the deck (0.3 mm clearance, at +-y of the end axis, about 17 mm out): they locate the end and take the turning torque of the knob
  (about 1.7 N*m at 400 N, as much as the friction of the rim on the deck can give). They stay outside the stop ring of the ball above them (ring 14.75 mm in radius; at 25 deg of tilt it comes down to 1.4 mm over the rim plane at r = 14.8), so the tip end loses no tilt (J2d at 25 deg in 8 azimuths: no interference; keys on the flat of the rim itself did touch the ring). The slots go right through the deck, so the base has no bridge.
  SAME_END = False gives the old stand end with a round column in the cup (PLUG_R = 6 mm, 2.5 mm out of the rim plane, bore PLUG_BORE = 2.4 mm) and the 12.6 mm hole.
  The deck has only a 4 mm hole for the wire (STAND_HOLE_R = 2, 45 deg lead-in); the end is held down by the 400 N of the wire alone (the screw pulls the end wall down, the rim of the cup, a 3 mm wide ring of 265 mm2, presses on
  the deck: 1.5 MPa), so nothing is screwed or glued. The ring of the base is interrupted by a rounded notch (x 36 .. 47, y +-7.5) where the wire and the lugs of drum B cross it; the rest of the ring (|y| > 7.5) supports the deck under the end.
  WIRE PATH (OPEN, nothing hides it, no bearings, no axles; v33: ONE RIB instead of two drums with four lugs): cup centre -> straight down out of the lower pole of the ball (no pillar, no bore) -> 90 deg round the left corner of the RIB (radius RP = 4 mm) -> along the floor at 1.7 mm -> 90 deg round its right corner -> straight up through the hole of the deck
  (4 mm) into the end, through the open cup, the vault and the front wall of the slider. The RIB (make_rib, RIB_W = 6.2 mm thick, RIB = True) is a single plate under the deck, in the plane of the wire: its lower edge runs along the wire axis (RIB_S = 0) and carries a round CHANNEL of radius 1.4 mm (RIB_G), a half circle 1.4 mm deep in which the wire lies half sunk and cannot slip sideways, its upper edge is the deck. Left side: a 45 deg line starting where the wire leaves the ball
  (the wire axis at z = 6.95 mm: 1.35 mm clear of the ball, ZB_DROP = 0.75 lower than the ball allows; the line starts at the wire axis), so nothing leans out more than 45 deg when the base is printed upside down; right side: a vertical wall up to the deck beside the hole. No lugs, no drums, no webs: the channel (one sweep of a circle along the path) keeps the wire on the rib, also while it is slack. RIB_G = 0 leaves the edge plain.
  RIB = False gives the old drums and lugs back (drum A 45 deg teardrop DRUM_FLANK, two 3 mm lugs per drum, 5.2 mm gap).
  ROUNDED FOR PRINTING: the table side of the wall and of the ring (r 1 / 0.8), the underside of the collar (r 1), the inner corner of wall and deck (r 1.5); 45 deg chamfer (0.8 mm) on the outer edge of the deck,
  45 deg lead-ins (0.5 mm) round the hole of the end and the cup rim (they are on the bed); the rib has no overhang but the ledge below.
  and nothing hangs in the air. The end is the rounded, support-free tip end (see THE TIP END), the ears have 0.4 mm chamfers.
  The base is printed UPSIDE DOWN (deck on the bed: the cup rim and the deck are flat). The open underside is a pocket of 170 cm3 (16 mm deep): it takes the BALLAST. Without ballast the base (117 g + stand end 30 g + hardware)
  tips over towards the tip side with the 100 g test weight (overturning 24 kg*mm, the empty base holds 10 kg*mm; the stand end 44 mm behind the mast adds about 3 kg*mm of counter-moment): put in at least 0.4 kg (1.5 x safety; steel shot set in epoxy fills the pocket with about 0.8 kg, or steel discs, a lead sheet), or clamp / stick the base to the table.
  FRICTION ON THE DRUMS (the price of having no bearings): a wire sliding round a fixed drum keeps exp(-mu * angle) of its tension: with mu = 0.25 (MU_CH, bare printed drum) the two 90 deg bends leave 0.456 of the tension at the cup (the 693ZZ pulleys left 0.96); with
  a strip of PTFE tape along the edge of the rib, or a lubricated wire, mu = 0.10 gives 0.73. The holding margins below are computed with BASE_EFF = exp(-MU_CH * pi). The wire presses on the drum with about T / (RW * d) = 400 / (5.25 * 2.5) = 30 MPa at 400 N: bare PETG
  creeps under that, the tape / sleeve protects the drum too. The deck is a 4 mm plate: with 100 g at the tip the arm tips the stand cup by about 1 degree (plate estimate, ring taken as clamped; about 4 mm at the tip end): if that is too soft, add radial ribs between the collar and the ring.

THE ARM (one boom; with NBOOM = 2 see SECOND ARM)  The shoulder and the tip side are the same stack: base cup -> M0 -> DC -> M1 -> BOOM -> M2 -> DC2 -> M3 -> tip end (8 ball joints J0a, J0b, J1a, J1b, J2a, J2b, J2c, J2d + the boom twist T1).
  The tip side (M2, DC2, M3, tip end) is 159 mm long and points where the far cup of the boom opens: TIP_ANG = 90 deg (default) = SIDEWAYS, towards -y, horizontal at the height of the boom (z = 223.6 mm: the 20 mm base lowered everything by 37 mm), the tip end
  at y = -267 mm. Hanging it DOWN (TIP_ANG = 180, as before) does not work any more: with the 35 mm boom it hangs into the base (M3, tip end and slider overlap the base) and its end goes about 56 mm below the table.
  TIP_ANG = 270 is the mirror image (+y), 0 = up (arm 540 mm tall), 135 = down and sideways (also free, margins a little better); any angle is possible. TIP_ANG = 90 and 270 are collision free at neutral and above the table.
  TIP_LINKS = 1 gives the old tip side (M2 only). More booms (NBOOM = 2 default, 3) with ELBOW_ANG and ARM_LINKS: see SECOND ARM. The wire path, the joint centres, the stop rings and the pose panel all follow TIP_ANG.

THE TIP END (straight tensioner)
  Cup on top = the upper cup of DC (it takes the lower ball of M3). The wire runs straight along the cup axis (bare channel, no bend) into the same trough as the base, shifted by TD = 12 mm. The trough opens towards +x
  (slider dropped in from the side: see TIP SLIDER), the end wall carries the screw, the knob is at the far end. The margins below assume a test weight of 100 g at the end wall of the tip end (267 mm from the mast axis sideways).
  Shape for printing without supports (standing on the end wall, cup up): rounded outline (r 6 at the closed back corners, r 3 at the open front corners), 1 mm 45 deg chamfer on the bed edge, rounded outer rim of the cup,
  a cone (38.7 deg from vertical) from the cup block down into the tail instead of a flat ledge, and a 45 deg vault on top of the trough: its flat top is 9.4 mm wide (the old flat roof was a 20 mm bridge).
  The top of the vault is 2 mm above the old roof (3.2 mm of material left under the floor of the cup) and leaves 3 mm of free wire above the slider at the position drawn (1 mm before).

TIP SLIDER (slot, TIP_SLOT = 1)  The slider of the tip end has a slot from its wire hole and its ferrule pocket to the face that looks out of the open side of the trough, so it can be seen and the ferrule pocket can be reached from the open side
  (crimp, check or change the ferrule there). Slot 3.0 mm wide (WIRE_D/2 + 0.25 each side) through the 1.5 mm front wall (45 deg lead-in at the mouth), ferrule slot 5.4 mm wide (the pocket width) behind it up to the thread bore.
  The wire itself is NOT laid in sideways in this orientation: at the start position only 3 mm of wire are free between the top of the vault of the trough and the front face of the slider, too little to bend it out of the axis, so it is fed through
  the front hole end-on (the hole is in line with the roof bore). TIP_SLOT = -1 turns the slot to the closed back side of the trough: the slider is then dropped in from the open side over the wire and a ferrule crimped beforehand
  (ferrule front face 4.5 mm below the top of the vault, wire cut flush with the ferrule; checked: no contact in 61 positions 0.5 mm apart, also at BALL_D = 8, where the closed hole would hit both from 10 mm on), at the price of a hidden slot.
  TIP_SLOT = 0 = closed hole. The stand tensioner uses the same slider (the trough of the stand end faces OUTWARD, away from the mast, so the slot is visible there too).
  Shape for printing without supports (standing on its front face): the four long edges rounded r 4, the front edges chamfered at 45 deg (3 mm = TIP_CH on the two long sides so that the slider clears the vault of the tip end, which it may approach up to 1 mm in front of
  the position drawn with 0.5 mm clearance; 1 mm on the two short sides), the rear edges chamfered 1 mm, and the ferrule slot with a pointed 45 deg top instead of a flat ceiling. The same slider is used at the stand end (Slider_x2.stl).

TENSIONER (the same at both ends): a SLIDER holds the wire (ferrule in its pocket) and carries a printed internal thread (M10x2.5, the thread profile of jumper_wire_pen_assembly). The printed TENSION SCREW (thread + knob
  in one piece) goes through the end wall from the outside; its knob rests on the wall. Turning the knob draws the slider towards the wall (11 mm of travel from the position drawn).
  The screw is short on purpose (SCR_END): its free end stops 0.5 mm before the bottom of the thread socket when the slider has travelled the full 11 mm (the first version ended at the bottom of the socket of the slider as drawn
  and so blocked the slider after 0.5 mm of travel). It engages 6 mm of thread (2.4 turns) at the start of the travel and 17 mm at the end.
  The thread is right-handed: turn the knob CLOCKWISE (seen from the outside, from the knob) to draw the slider towards the wall and tension the wire. In the drawn position the thread of the screw and the groove of the slider mesh
  with the full 0.2 mm clearance (THREAD_CL) all round (the groove is turned by SCR_PHASE = 100.8 deg for this; without it the real threads overlapped by up to 0.5 mm in the drawn pose).

CONNECTING STANDS (CONN_ON = True, the default)  Stands join side by side like lego bricks, in a row along y: the base carries one pair of printed vertical DOVETAILS in the middle of its +y and -y sides (CONN_X = True adds a second pair on the +x / -x sides, the side of the tensioner, giving a square grid), no screws, no glue. Every stand is complete on its own (own arm, own wire, own tensioner); the joint only fixes where the
  stands are relative to each other, so several arms can work close together. A TONGUE (trapezoid, 8 mm wide at the wall, 14.5 mm at the tip, 9 mm long, flanks 20 deg, CN_*) sits on the +y side (and +x with CONN_X), a SOCKET (recessed INTO the base: a housing block inside the wall with a through slot of the same trapezoid, 0.25 mm clearance per side, mouth on the outer face of the wall) on
  the -y side (and -x with CONN_X), so the tongue of one stand always meets the socket of the next: any stand fits any other. The dovetails are full-height prisms (20 mm): LOWER one stand onto its neighbour from above (the joint slides vertically; sideways it is locked). Only the tongues stand out of the walls, so the walls of two joined stands are 0.2 mm apart (CN_GAP): pitch between two stand centres = 2 x BASE_R + 0.2 = 130.2 mm
  (conn_pitch()), the same in x and y; a stand has two neighbours (four with CONN_X, also in the corners of a grid: all joints slide vertically). show_neighbours((1, 3)) adds copies at the clicked-in positions for a look (0 = +x, 1 = +y, 2 = -x, 3 = -y).
  NO SHARP EDGES, STIFF SLOTS: the housing of each socket is blended into the inner face of the wall with concave fillets (CN_GUS = 5 mm radius), the two bottom corners of the slot are rounded (CN_FIL_S = 0.8) and so are the two edges of its mouth (CN_FIL_M = 0.8), the tip corners of the tongue
  are rounded (CN_FIL_T = 1.5, rounder than the slot bottom so they never touch it), the slot has a 45 deg countersink at both ends (CN_LEAD = 0.8, guides the tongue in), and the ends of tongue (0.8 mm) and housing (0.4 mm) have 45 deg chamfers on the bed and the table side.
  Printing: everything is a vertical prism or a 45 deg chamfer, no new supports (the countersinks and the housing chamfer on the bed side are 45-50 deg, about 50 mm2 together). Limits: a sliding fit that locks the stands sideways, but a stand can be lifted straight out, so tipping loads and ballast are not shared (add a printed pin or a drop of glue for a rigid mat);
  the clearance scales with BALL_D (never less than 0.15 mm in the finished part); the arms of neighbours are not checked against each other.

HARDWARE (not printed)  wire or string 2.5 mm, cut 584 mm at full size (path 564 mm + 20 mm for the two crimps) | 2 crimp ferrules | no bearings, no bolts | optional: PTFE tape in the channel of the rib (friction, see FRICTION ON THE DRUMS) | ballast for the open underside of the base (at least 0.4 kg: steel shot in epoxy, steel discs).
PRINTED  PETG, 0.2 mm layers, 4 walls: M link x4 (M0 .. M3 are the same part unless M_LEN_TIP is set, 18.1 g each, bored through the middle, rounded rod), DC x2 (DC, DC2: 10.9 g each, hollowed round the middle), end piece x2, rod, STAND BASE x1 (109.6 g with the connectors, the rib and the 8 lightening windows, UPSIDE DOWN, written in that orientation), END x2 (21.6 g each, hollow cup block and open windows: the stand end and the tip end are the same part, with two ears), SLIDER x2 (tip slider, slot, rounded), TENSION SCREW x2 (5.6 g each, dished knob). Total 332.1 g with the old tip tensioner (TIP_PROBE = False); with the SCOPE PROBE HOLDER (TIP_PROBE = True, default): the tip end x1, slider x1 and screw x1 are replaced by the holder (Probe_holder_x1.stl, 23.6 g, the stand end Stand_end_x1.stl stays): total 322.4 g (328 g with CONN_ON = False; WIN_ON = False: 370.1 g; TE_VOID, TE_WIN and KNOB_DISH False as well: 384.9 g; before the DC and M links were lightened 455 g).
  The tip end and the stand end are printed on their end wall, cup up, without supports: everything is steeper than 45 deg except the flat top of the vault of the trough, a bridge of 9.4 mm (use the bridging profile of the slicer).
  The base (deck on the bed) needs no support: its only flat overhang is a narrow ledge (15 mm2: the rib, 6.2 mm wide, hangs 2.4 .. 2.9 mm out from the cone wall of the cup; the v30 drum had a flat top 4.2 mm deep, 22 mm2) at z = 12 mm, where the seat cone of the cup begins (0.5 mm under the collar): the 45 deg flank of the rib ends there against the cone. It cannot be avoided completely: the wire leaves drum A on the vertical line under the pole of the ball, and the fill above it may only lean out at 45 deg (DRUM_FLANK = False gives the v30 flat top back); all its other faces are 45 deg or steeper (the cup rim and the hole of the end have 45 deg lead-ins, the outer edge of the deck a 45 deg chamfer, lug B and the drum B web 45 deg flanks).
  Slider and screw STANDING on their ends. If a screw breaks, print it lying down with 100 % infill. If the thread binds, raise THREAD_CL.
ASSEMBLY  No glue needed: (optional: stick PTFE tape in the channel of the rib), put the stand end on the deck (the two ears into the two slots of the deck, the trough open outward), slide the slider in from the open side, drop the screw in through the end wall from above and turn it until the thread takes the slider. Thread the wire from the tip end through
  every ball and out of the lower pole of the stand ball, in the channel of the rib, up through the hole of the deck into the stand end and end-on through the front hole of the slider (3 mm of free wire above the vault, as at the tip), crimp a ferrule on each end (it sits in the pocket of the slider; at both ends the pocket is open to the open side
  of the trough: crimp it there; with TIP_SLOT = -1 the wire is laid in from the side instead, see TIP SLIDER). Leave both sliders 11 mm from their end walls and turn a knob until the joints lock.
  Put the ballast into the pocket under the deck (steel shot in epoxy, discs) or clamp the base down.

BOOM END PIECES  The outer shape is a ROUNDED ELBOW (a quarter torus, centre-line radius ELBOW_R = 15 mm, tube radius RS) instead of two cylinders that meet
  at a sharp corner; the wire channel is unchanged (bend radius BEND_R = 12 mm). Each end piece is 4 cm3 (5 g) lighter.
  The outer edge of the cup block, where the elbow leaves it, has a 2 mm 45 deg chamfer (EP_CHAMFER; 0 = none), which also removes the overhang when the end piece is printed cup up.

ROTATION STOP RING  Every link ball (M0, M1, M2: six balls) carries a raised ring on its neck side that stops the tilt mechanically. The underside of the ring is a cone that
  coincides with the plane of the cup's top face when the joint is tilted RING_LIMIT + RING_PLAY (25.2 deg): the top face of the cup comes to rest flat against the ring and the
  joint cannot tilt further, in any direction; below that angle the cup stays clear of it. The ring stands RING_H = 1.8 mm out of the ball (outer dia about 29.5 mm at design size),
  has a vertical outer wall of RING_WALL = 1.5 mm and a flat top. It sits on the neck side, where the seat contact never is (>= 95 deg from the neck axis), so the holding
  force is unchanged. Printing the link neck up, the underside of the ring is a 25 deg overhang 1.8 mm wide (support it or tilt the print). RING_ON = False builds plain balls.
  The ring has the same colour as the rest of the part in the 3D view.
  CHECKED at BALL_D = 8: valid solids, neutral clear, wire 0 hits. Every joint is clear up to 25.5 deg and its ring meets its own cup at 27 deg (that pair only, overlap 0.1 mm3);
  (with the sideways tip side every joint tilts 25 deg in every direction). The ring is 9.07 mm in diameter (0.55 mm out of the 8 mm ball); each M link is 0.51 cm3 with the 3 mm channel.

WIRE CHANNEL  No liners (checked at BALL_D = 8 and 26: hole 3 mm finished = 9.75 mm at design size in the 8 mm model; rod, spigot and socket then grow to R_NECK = R_SPIG = 7.475 mm design (wall 0.8 mm finished), R_ROD = 7.975). The wire runs in a bare printed channel WIRE_HOLE = 3 mm wide (finished size, HOLE_FINISHED = True) through every ball, neck, cup, end piece and rod;
  the wire / string is WIRE_THICK = 2.5 mm (0.25 mm clearance all round), limited by the macro to what the hole and the ball allow (full size 2.5 mm; BALL_D = 8: 1.04 mm at 25 deg tilt, or 2.5 mm with TILT_MAX = 19.5, both checked: valid, neutral clear, wire clear at full tilt, stop rings ok).
  The ferrule seats (slider hole, pocket, ferrule) are sized from the wire: hole radius = wire radius + 0.5, ferrule = wire radius + 1.0, pocket = ferrule + 0.45 (design-size mm). It bends where the balls kink it. The flare around the hole in every ball
  is computed from the hole: a cone whose edge on the ball lies FLARE_EDGE = 33 deg from the ball pole (the seat touches the ball 60 deg off the cup axis, nearest 35 deg at 25 deg tilt),
  wide enough for the wire to bend TILT_MAX at the ball centre. Where the wire needs a ferrule (the slider pockets) the hole stays small. Neck, spigot and socket grow
  with the hole so that at least R_WALL = 2.6 mm (design size) of wall is left around it. The seat friction in the bare bends is MU_W = 0.25 (was 0.12 with the liner).

USE  Macro > Execute. Pose panel and rotation gizmo as in the earlier macros (wire_harness.py must stay in the Macro folder); the wire follows the pose. The panel also has the M length box (Rebuild re-runs this macro file from the Macro folder with the new length).
  export_stl("C:/temp/probe") writes one STL per printed part in its print orientation.
STATUS (all measured in FreeCAD; full size BALL_D = 26 unless stated; default TIP_ANG = 90, one boom, two tip links)
  All solids valid (also thread parts), neutral pose without overlaps, wire clearance 0 hits (2095 sample points, 1.5 mm step), wire clear of every printed part at 25 deg tilt of each of the 8 joints in four directions
  and in 12 random poses with all joints tilted 10 .. 25 deg together.
  Base 130 mm x 20 mm, 92.1 cm3 (117 g), no plate; stand end 23.8 cm3 (30 g); knob up to z = 95.7 mm; slider travel 11 mm up to the end wall. Printed total 426 g, wire cut 582 mm.
  Stand v18 (the tip end upside down on the deck instead of the tower; tower tray, cap, window, pins and the stand slider are gone), measured at BALL_D = 26: base (one solid), stand end, slider and screw valid; stand end, real slider and real screw against the base: 0 mm3;
  slider and tip end: 0 mm3; neutral pose without overlaps; the ball (r 13) overlaps the base by 0 mm3 and drum A is 0.60 mm clear of it; the wire (2.5 mm, tangent to the drums, 0.03 mm allowed for the chords of its arcs) along its whole path, through the hole of the deck and
  the open cup: 0 hits of 2190 sample points. STL export: Stand_base_x1.stl (deck on the bed, 130 x 130 x 20), Tip_end_x2.stl (end wall on the bed, 31 x 36 x 65; the stand end and the tip end are the same part), Slider_x2.stl, Tension_screw_x2.stl; no plate file.
  TILT OF THE SHOULDER JOINT J0a: the end is 84 mm tall now (the old tower was 54 mm), so the connector DC and M0 meet its end wall and knob when the arm leans towards it: free up to 25 deg in every azimuth except around the stand end, where it is free up to 13.3 deg straight at it,
  14.8 deg 20 deg off that direction, 21.1 deg 40 deg off, 25 deg from 45 deg off and beyond (the tower allowed 22.7 deg straight at it). J0b, J1a, J1b, J2a, J2b, J2c and J2d reach 25 deg in the azimuths tested (0, 90, 270) as before; XT further out would give more reach, but the end then overhangs the 130 mm base.
  Overhangs steeper than 45 deg from vertical in the print orientation: base only the flat top of drum A (19 mm2, a 3.3 mm bridge), 6 mm2 where the seat cut meets a lug and the 45 deg lead-in cone (7 mm2, exactly 45 deg); drum B has none (before: both drums, 76 mm2 of bridges 5.2 mm long); stand end and tip end only the flat top of the vault (213 mm2, a 9.4 mm bridge) and 5 mm2 of the chamfer of the bed edge.
  Square base with connectors (v25), measured at BALL_D = 26: one valid solid, 114.5 cm3 (145 g), 130 x 139 x 20 mm with the tongue; a copy at conn_pitch() in +y and in -y overlaps by 0 mm3 (tongue 0.167 mm clear of the socket on each side, vertical insertion free); overhangs steeper than 45 deg
  from vertical: the 45 deg chamfers and countersinks only (the countersinks 45-50 deg, about 50 mm2); wire 0 hits of 2190, holding margins and neutral pose as before; printed total 454.5 g. BALL_D = 8: valid, clearance floored at 0.15 mm.
  LIGHTENED DC (v27, DC_LIGHT = True): the connectors DC and DC2 were solid cylinders (R 15.6, 23.3 cm3, 29.6 g). Now the outside follows the two cup cones: a 1.5 mm collar at each rim (rim face and tilt stop unchanged), then a 30 deg double cone, the wall staying 3 mm beside the cup, meeting in a concave FILLET in the middle (DC_FIL = 10 mm radius, tangent to both cones, neck radius 6.5 mm) that reinforces the thin part round
  the wire hole between the two cup bottoms: 8.6 cm3, 10.9 g each (-19 g each, printed total 454.5 -> 417.1 g). Printing: the cones are 30 deg from vertical in both halves, so it prints on either rim without supports (only the 5.5 mm2 flat bottom of each cup, as before). Checked at BALL_D = 26: valid single solids, neutral pose
  without overlaps, J0b, J1a and J1b at 25 deg in four azimuths without interference, holding margins J0a 0.7 | J0b 0.8 | J1a 0.9 | J1b 1.0 | J2a 0.6 | J2b 0.9 | J2c 1.3 | J2d 2.4 (the lighter arm needs less torque).
  LIGHTENED M LINKS (v29, BALL_BORE = 6.5, ROD_BORE = 5): the balls were solid spheres with a 3 mm channel and the rod a tube with 3 mm wall (20.7 cm3, 26.2 g). Now one inner void runs through both balls and the rod: a bore of radius 6.5 mm through the middle of each ball (vertical walls, the wire runs free
  in it), a 45 deg cone down to the 5 mm bore of the rod (wall 2 mm = 5 perimeters). The bore ends inside the flare of the far pole (13 x sin 33 deg = 7.1 mm), so it never reaches the contact circle of the seat; the rings, the neck and the outside of the balls are unchanged. 15.3 cm3, 19.4 g each (-6.8 g, -26 %; printed total 417.1 -> 389.9 g).
  Printing (neck up or down, the link is symmetrical): vertical walls and 45 deg cones inside, so no new supports; overhang faces steeper than 45 deg are the sphere itself, 623 mm2 against 653 mm2 before. BALL_BORE = 0 gives the solid balls again; on a small model (BALL_D below about 9) the bore is skipped because the 3 mm channel is already wider than the rod bore.
  Checked at BALL_D = 26: valid single solids, neutral pose without overlaps, wire 0 hits of 2190, J0b .. J2d at 25 deg in four azimuths each without interference, holding margins J0a 0.7 | J0b 0.8 | J1a 0.9 | J1b 1.1 | J2a 0.6 | J2b 0.9 | J2c 1.3 | J2d 2.4.
  ROUNDED ROD (v30, M_ROUND = True, M_WAIST = 5.5, M_WALL = 2, M_CAVE = 9.5): the rod of the M links is no longer a straight tube but a concave spindle like the DC. It STARTS AT THE STOP RINGS: one arc runs from the outer top edge of the ring on the lower ball (ring_top: radius about 14.75, 3.5 mm above the ball centre) through the waist (outer radius
  M_WAIST = 5.5 mm, half way between the balls) to the outer top edge of the ring on the upper ball, so there is no step, no flat ledge and no straight piece: the part has one smooth profile from ring to ring. At the rings the surface is 42 deg from the vertical (48 deg from the horizontal), so the rod itself needs no support when printed (before: the flat
  shoulder under the rings and the sphere cap). The inner void follows the outside at a constant wall M_WALL = 2 mm (5 perimeters): bore 6.5 mm in the ball, 45 deg cone out to M_CAVE = 9.5 mm, then an arc parallel to the outer one. 14.25 cm3, 18.1 g each (v29 15.3 cm3, 19.4 g; printed total 389.9 -> 384.5 g). Overhang faces steeper than 45 deg (neck up or down): 376 mm2 (v29 623 mm2), of which the underside cones of the two stop rings
  (25 deg, 1.8 mm wide: they are the stop surface, left as they are) and the spheres. Same checks as above: valid single solids, neutral pose without overlaps, wire 0 of 2190, 25 deg in eight azimuths for J0b .. J2d without interference (J0a at azimuth 180 still hits Stand_TE, the known 13 deg limit), same holding margins. M_ROUND = False gives the straight tube of v29; the profile needs the stop rings (RING_ON), without them the straight tube is used.
  (The first version of the lead-in at the cup rim was a 0.5 mm edge chamfer, 60 deg from vertical because the seat is a 30 deg cone; it is a 45 deg countersink now.) Deck stiffness: see FRICTION ON THE DRUMS.
  BALL_D = 8: base, stand end, slider and screw valid, stand end against the base 0 mm3, neutral pose without overlaps, wire 0 hits of 1030, base 40 mm x 6.15 mm, printed total 11.7 g, wire cut 179 mm; the wire run is 1.7 mm (design size, ZB_DROP = 0.75) above the table, 0.65 mm clear
  of it at that size (the macro warns): put a thin pad under the base. Ballast: the arm weighs 271 g and its centre of mass is 80 mm from the mast axis, so with 100 g at the tip the overturning moment about the edge is 24 kg*mm against 10 kg*mm held by the empty base.
  Tilt reach of the other joints (1 deg steps, 24 azimuths, tower version): all 8 joints reach 25 deg in every direction (the tip side no longer hangs beside the shoulder: the old limits toward the head side are gone). The boom twist T1 is free except
  75 .. 105 deg, where the tip side would point down into the base (the pose panel stops there). Stop rings: every joint is clear up to 25.5 deg and meets its own cup (only that pair) from 26 deg.
  Tip slider (slot on the open side, TIP_SLOT = 1): valid, slot visible from the open side of the trough. The hole is 3.0 mm instead of 3.5 mm so that the ferrule keeps its bearing area on the front wall: 6.2 mm2 (closed slider 6.3 mm2; the old 3.5 mm hole
  with the slot would leave 4.1 mm2). That bearing is the most highly loaded spot of both sliders: 65 MPa at the full 400 N on a 1.5 mm PETG wall. Print one slider and pull-test it before relying on 400 N (a thicker front wall or a steel washer under the ferrule would relieve it).
  TIP_SLOT = -1 (slot on the back side): dropped into the trough over the wire (2.5 mm) and a ferrule (4.5 x 5 mm) crimped beforehand, the slider touches neither of them nor the tip end in 61 positions 0.5 mm apart (the closed hole hits both from 10 mm on); also at BALL_D = 8.
  Tip end and tip slider reshaped for printing without supports (TIP_CH = 3): both solids valid at BALL_D = 26 and 8, neutral pose without overlaps, the real threaded slider clears the tip end at every position from 1 mm in front of the position drawn
  to the end wall (0 mm3 overlap), the screw and a 2.9 mm wire column clear it too; TIP_SLOT = -1: the drop-in over the wire and a ferrule is still free in 45 positions 1 mm apart (new vault, rounded slider); TIP_SLOT = 0 valid.
  Overhangs steeper than 45 deg from vertical in the print orientation (front / end wall on the bed): tip end only the bed face and the 9.4 mm flat top of the vault (before: also the 20 x 19 mm roof and the ledge under the cup block, 4 faces);
  tip slider only the bed face and two 1.3 mm ledges. Volumes: tip end 22.2 cm3 (was 23.1), tip slider 4.80 cm3 (was 5.30), printed total 584.3 -> 582.6 g (tip end and slider). Bearing area of the ferrule 6.2 mm2 (unchanged), holding margins unchanged.
  Tension screw (both ends, one part): it was 11 mm too long, its tip (x = 24) sat at the bottom of the thread socket of the slider as drawn, so the slider could not be drawn towards the wall by more than 0.5 mm. Now it ends at x = 35 (SCR_END):
  the core of the screw overlaps neither slider at any shift from 0 to 11 mm (0.00 mm3, also at BALL_D = 8), 0.5 mm clear of the socket bottom at the end of the travel; thread engaged 6 mm at the start, 17 mm at the end of the travel.
  Screw 4.92 cm3 (was 5.66), printed total 580.7 g, valid, neutral pose without overlaps, holding margins unchanged.
  Thread meshing (cross sections of the real shapes every 1 mm, radius of the bore minus radius of the screw round the whole circumference): before, -0.50 mm (collision) in the engaged part of the drawn pose, because the groove was 100.8 deg out of phase;
  now +0.20 mm = THREAD_CL everywhere (the same slider at both ends); it still meshes when the slider is shifted a quarter pitch (0.625 mm) and the screw is turned 90 deg clockwise (0.20 mm gap), so the groove and the screw are the same helix, same hand.
  TIP_ANG = 180 (hanging): overlaps with the base. 270 free, 45 / 60 / 135 free (zmax about 429 / 372 / 236 mm: the earlier values minus the 37 mm the base got lower).
  Holding margin (wire 400 N, seat friction 0.25, bare bends 0.25, wire on the two printed drums of the base MU_CH = 0.25 -> 0.456 of the tension left at the cup, 100 g at the end wall of the tip end, worst case of random poses):
  J0a 0.6 | J0b 0.7 | J1a 0.8 | J1b 1.0 | J2a 0.6 | J2b 0.9 | J2c 1.3 | J2d 2.4. With the 693ZZ pulleys (0.96) the same joints had 1.4 | 1.5 | 1.8 | 2.1 | 1.3 | 1.8 | 2.7 | 5.1. A margin below 1 means the joint slips under that load:
  with BARE printed drums the shoulder (J0a, J0b, J1a, J2a) does NOT hold the 100 g test weight at 400 N, and J0a (0.87) not even the arm alone. Remedy: lower the friction on the two drums (PTFE tape or sleeve, lubricated wire):
  MU_CH = 0.10 (0.730 left): J0a 1.03 | J0b 1.16 | J1a 1.33 | J1b 1.63 | J2a 1.00 | J2b 1.39 | J2c 2.03 | J2d 3.86 (MU_CH = 0.15: 0.88 | 0.99 | 1.14 | 1.39 | 0.86 | 1.19 | 1.73 | 3.30).
  Without the test weight (PROBE_G = 0): MU_CH = 0.25: J0a 0.87 | J0b 1.01 | J1a 1.18 | J1b 1.44 | J2a 0.91 | J2b 1.28 | J2c 1.91 | J2d 3.68; MU_CH = 0.10: 1.40 | 1.61 | 1.89 | 2.30 | 1.46 | 2.06 | 3.05 | 5.90.
  The margins grow in proportion to WIRE_T (600 N: x1.5), but the ferrule bearing of the sliders (65 MPa at 400 N) and the printed parts limit the tension. These are thin at the shoulder because the tip side is long and horizontal
  (the lever of the 100 g load is 270 mm; a margin of x1.3 means the joint holds with 30 % to spare in the worst pose).
  MINIATURE (BALL_D = 8): same checks, same results (valid, neutral clear, wire 0 hits of 2200, every joint 25 deg in all 8 directions tested, stop ring clear at 25.5 / meets at 26). Wire 1.04 mm (the ball limits it
  at 25 deg tilt; 2.5 mm needs TILT_MAX = 19.5), cut 170 mm, tension 37.9 N, printed total 11.2 g, holding margin (v17, bare printed drums, 9.5 g at the tip) J0a 0.8 | J0b 0.9 | J1a 1.1 | J1b 1.2 | J2a 0.7 | J2b 1.0 | J2c 1.4 | J2d 2.6.
  What shrinks below FDM accuracy at BALL_D = 8: rod spigot fit 0.06 mm, thread M3.1 x 0.77 mm (depth 0.23, fit 0.06). Resin (SLA) printing is advised; for FDM raise those fits at the design size (they are in design-size mm in the code).
  The collision tests use simple stand-ins (a box, a cylinder) for the two threaded parts: boolean operations on the helical faces are slow and once crashed FreeCAD.
"""
import math, os, json, sys, copy
import FreeCAD as App
_old = globals().get("CTRL")
if _old is not None:
    try: _old.teardown()
    except Exception as _e: print("previous panel:", _e)
CTRL = None
_OV = globals().pop("PS_OVERRIDE", None) or {}                  # values set by the panel (M length) for one rebuild of the model
import Part
from FreeCAD import Vector as V

# ============================== PARAMETERS (mm) - edit here, then run the macro again ==============================
DOC_NAME   = "ProbeStandOneBoomCombined"
BALL_D     = 26.0         # ball DIAMETER of the finished model = the reference for the scale: 26 = the full-size design (RB = 13), 8 = the miniature. EVERYTHING scales with it (wire, thread, fits included; the wire channel WIRE_HOLE is in finished mm unless HOLE_FINISHED = False)
RB         = 13           # radius of every ball and of both cups of the boom (design size; the scale pass below shrinks the finished model to BALL_D)
R1         = RB           # shoulder ball J1a (base cup <-> M1): same radius as all other balls, so M1 and M2 are the same part
BOOM_L     = 35           # cup centre to cup centre of a boom (all booms identical) = 2 x XF + rod length: 35 = a 3 mm rod; 32 = no rod (short coupler peg instead)
BOOM_A     = 40           # cup centre -> boom axis (crank height)
TIP_Z      = 35           # probe tip height in the neutral pose (only used with SHOULDER_LINKS = 1; with 2 links it follows from MAST_TOP)
NBOOM      = 2            # booms: 1 = shoulder link, one boom, tip side;  2 (default) = a SECOND ARM: boom 1 -> M2 -> DC2 -> M3 -> boom 2 -> M4 -> DC3 -> M5 -> tip end (see ARM_LINKS);  3 = a third one. All booms identical
TIP_ANG    = 90           # where the tip side (M2, DC2, M3, tip end) points = direction of the cup at the far end of the boom (deg about the rod axis): 180 = hangs down (the 159 mm long tip side then runs into the base), 90 / 270 = sideways (default), 0 = up
ARM_LINKS  = 2            # what joins one boom to the next (only NBOOM > 1): 2 = a connector stack M - DC - M (the same stack as the tip side: two links and a double cup, joints J2a .. J2d, J3a ..), 0 = one loose ball between the two end pieces (old)
TIP_LINKS  = 2            # tip side, mirror of the shoulder (M0, DC, M1): 2 = boom -> M2 -> connector DC2 -> M3 -> tip end (joints Jna .. Jnd);  1 = boom -> M2 -> tip end (Jna, Jnb)
M_LEN      = _OV.get("M_LEN", 55)   # LENGTH OF THE M LINKS (also in the panel: "M length" + Rebuild) = ball-centre distance (design-size mm): M0, M1 (shoulder) and M2, M3 (tip side) are the same part, printed four times. Allowed: 36 .. 120 (shorter: the stop rings meet, longer: the rod is too slim)
M_LEN_TIP  = _OV.get("M_LEN_TIP", 0)   # length of the tip side links M2, M3 if they should differ from M0, M1 (then they are two parts, printed twice each); 0 = the same as M_LEN. The probe tip height follows from the lengths and the stand height
_ml0 = (M_LEN, M_LEN_TIP)
M_LEN = max(36.0, min(120.0, float(M_LEN))); M_LEN_TIP = 0 if M_LEN_TIP <= 0 else max(36.0, min(120.0, float(M_LEN_TIP)))              # the range that was checked (valid solids, neutral pose without overlaps, wire 0 hits)
if (M_LEN, M_LEN_TIP) != tuple(float(x) if x else x for x in _ml0): print("WARNING: M_LEN / M_LEN_TIP limited to 36 .. 120 mm")
LINK_D     = M_LEN        # (old name) length of M0 and M1
LINK_T     = M_LEN_TIP if M_LEN_TIP > 0 else M_LEN        # length of M2 and M3
BALL_BORE  = 6.5          # M links: radius of the bore through the middle of both balls (design-size mm; the wire runs free in it, like in the hollow rod); 0 = solid balls with the 3 mm channel. At most 13 * sin(FLARE_EDGE) = 7.1: the bore must stay inside the contact circle of the seat. Ignored on a small model where the channel is wider than 4.5 mm (BALL_D below about 9)
ROD_BORE   = 5.0          # M links: radius of the bore of the rod (outer radius R_NECK = 7, so the wall is 2 mm = 5 perimeters)
M_ROUND    = True         # M links: the rod between the stop rings is a rounded concave spindle (like the DC) that starts at the outer top edge of the rings; False = straight tube of radius R_NECK
M_WAIST    = 5.5          # M links rounded: outer radius in the middle of the rod (the inner void follows it, wall M_WALL)
M_WALL     = 2.0          # M links rounded: wall of the rod and of the neck side of the balls (5 perimeters at 0.4 mm)
M_CAVE     = 9.5          # M links rounded: radius of the inner void in the neck side of the ball, between the 45 deg cone from the ball bore and the inner arc (wall to the sphere at least 3 mm)
DC_LIGHT   = True         # DC / DC2: lightened round the middle (the outer surface follows the cup cones, 30 deg, wall DC_WALL; False = solid cylinder)
DC_COLLAR  = 1.5          # DC / DC2 lightened: height of the full-size collar at each rim (rim face and tilt stop contact stay as they were)
DC_CORE    = 5.0          # DC / DC2 lightened: smallest outer radius, round the wire hole between the two cup bottoms (design-size mm); only used with DC_FIL = 0
DC_FIL     = 10.0         # DC / DC2 lightened: radius of the concave fillet in the middle (the waist) between the two cones, reinforcing the thin part between the cup bottoms (0 = a short straight core of radius DC_CORE instead)
DC_D       = 49           # ball-centre distance across the double-cup connectors DC and DC2 (two cups back to back, 40 mm between the rims; DC_LIGHT hollows the outside round the middle)
# MAST_TOP (height of the stand cup above the table) is no longer a parameter: it follows from the base (BASE_H + ZG, the rim of the cup is flush with the deck)
TE_WALL    = 56           # tensioner (both ends): screw axis origin -> outer face of the end wall that carries the tension screw (the end wall of the tip end and of the stand end)
TD         = 12           # STRAIGHT tip end: the tail (trough, slider, screw, wall, knob = the dimensions of the stand end) starts this far below the cup centre line of the tail frame
THREAD_D, THREAD_P, THREAD_DEPTH = 10.0, 2.5, 0.75   # printed tension screw: outer diameter, pitch, depth (45 deg flanks): the thread profile of jumper_wire_pen_assembly
THREAD_CL, THREAD_CH = 0.2, 0.5                       # fit clearance (socket bigger, each side) and lead-in chamfer, as in jumper_wire_pen_assembly
WIRE_T     = 400          # wire tension in N with the knob tight (set by what the printed parts take: 1.5 mm 7x7 stainless breaks above 1000 N, a 2.5 mm wire or Dyneema string far above)
PROBE_OFS  = 48           # head ball axis -> probe axis (48: with the 32 mm boom the probe stands just outside the base rim; 32 would overlap the base)
BASE_R     = 65           # half the width of the SQUARE base (130 x 130 mm); the sides face +x (the tensioner), +y, -x, -y
BASE_CORNER = 12.0        # radius of the rounded corners of the base (outer outline, design-size mm)
CONN_ON    = True         # LEGO-LIKE CONNECTORS: a vertical dovetail TONGUE (side +y; +x if CONN_X) and a SOCKET (side -y; -x if CONN_X) in the middle of the sides, printed with the base; any stand fits any other, side by side
CONN_X     = False        # also a pair of connectors on the +x / -x sides (the +x side is the side of the tensioner: leave it free for the knob and the arm); with False the stands join in a row along y
DEFAULT_JOINT = "J1b"       # the joint selected when the pose panel and gizmo open: J1b = the elbow (top ball of the shoulder link M1 in the cup of the boom end piece); any name of JOINTS (J0a, J0b, J1a, J1b, T1, J2a ... J2d); an unknown name = the first joint
START_POSE  = {"T1": (0.0, 0.0, 68.125), "T2": (0.0, 0.0, 180.0)}      # the pose the stand starts in: joint -> (tilt direction, tilt, spin) deg, twist joints (0, 0, twist). Here: boom 1 twisted by 68.125 deg and boom 2 by 180 deg (the second arm folds back over the first, the probe stands up beside the base). {} = all joints neutral. "Reset all" in the panel still goes to the neutral (stretched) pose. A start pose that collides is dropped (all joints neutral)
BASE_H     = 20.0         # height of the deck of the base above the table (the rim of the stand cup is flush with it; the tensioner of the stand stands on it, see the layout)
PLUG_R     = 6.0          # stand end: radius of the round column that fills the inner part of its (unused) cup and drops into the hole of the deck (keeps the end in place)
PLUG_OUT   = 2.5          # stand end: how far the column sticks out of the rim plane of the cup into the deck (the deck is 4 mm thick)
SAME_END   = True         # the stand end and the tip end are ONE part (printed twice): the cup block carries two small EARS beside its rim that drop into two through slots of the deck (they take the turning torque of the knob); False = the old stand end with the column (PLUG_*)
KEY_H      = 1.5          # ears: height above the rim plane of the cup = how far they go into the deck (4 mm thick; the slots go right through it, so nothing bridges when the base is printed)
KEY_OUT    = 2.5          # ears: how far they stick out of the cup block (the block is rho = 15.6 mm in radius; the stop ring of the ball above it is 14.75 mm, so the ears start outside it: at 25 deg tilt the ring comes down to 1.4 mm above the rim plane at r = 14.8)
KEY_L      = 6.0          # ears: length along the arc
KEY_CLR    = 0.3          # ears: clearance to the slot of the deck, all round
STAND_HOLE_R = 2.0        # hole of the deck for the wire under the end (SAME_END): wire 2.5 mm + 1.5 mm of play (the rib under it reaches 0.75 mm into the hole: a roof of 2 mm2 only)
PLUG_BORE  = 2.4          # stand end: radius of the bore of the column (the wire runs through it)
RP         = 4.0          # radius of the two fixed round drums of the base that the wire runs round in its two 90 deg turns (the wire centre line runs at RP + wire radius)
WIRE_THICK = 2.5           # wire / string diameter in mm of the FINISHED model (it does not shrink with BALL_D). Limited automatically to what fits: the 3 mm hole (0.25 mm clearance all round) and the ball (the flare must clear the wire at TILT_MAX); the macro prints what it used
WIRE_FINISHED = True       # True: WIRE_THICK is in finished mm;  False: WIRE_D below (design size) is used and shrinks with BALL_D
WIRE_D     = 1.5           # design-size wire diameter (only used with WIRE_FINISHED = False; otherwise it is computed from WIRE_THICK)
TILT_MAX   = 25.0         # tilt limit of one ball
ZG         = 4.5          # half gap between the two cups that hold one loose ball (sets the cup rim height)
RS         = 12.5         # boom stem radius
ELBOW_ANG  = (90, 0)       # cup direction at the far end of boom 1 and boom 2 (deg about the rod axis; any angle): 90 = the stack between the booms runs sideways towards -y (default), 270 = towards +y, 0 = up, 180 = down; only used when NBOOM > 1. With TIP_ANG = ELBOW_ANG[0] the arm is stretched out, with TIP_ANG = ELBOW_ANG[0] + 180 it is folded back (Z)
XF         = 16            # cup axis -> rod flange face (round spigot sits here)
BEND_R     = 12            # radius of the rounded wire path inside every end piece (wire turns 90 deg along this arc)
EP_CHAMFER = 2.0           # boom end pieces: 45 deg chamfer on the outer edge of the cup block, where the elbow leaves it (0 = none; max RS-side ledge: rho - RS)
ROD_FLANGE_R = 10.5         # boom rod: radius of its flange (design-size mm). The round spigot grows into the flange with a 45 deg cone (fillet) with NO flat step, and the socket of the end piece is the matching cone, so the rod seats on the cone and prints standing on a spigot end WITHOUT supports. 0 = old stepped spigot and flat 12.5 mm flange
ROD_STUB   = 3.0           # boom rod: the small end faces of the two cones are extruded into a round stub of this length (radius R_SPIG, like a plain spigot) that centres the rod in the pocket of the end piece (0 = none). Only with ROD_FLANGE_R > 0
EP_VOID    = True          # BOOM END PIECES: hollow (closed cavity round the wire tube: in the cup block, same shape as the tensioner end, and in the upper part of the elbow); False = solid
EP_VOID_W  = 3.0           # end piece: wall round the cavity (square to the seat cone, at the outer wall of block and elbow)
EP_VOID_TILT = 45.0        # end piece: how far the cavity follows the elbow (deg from the vertical; at most 45: the roof of the cavity is then never steeper than 45 deg, no bridge)
EP_WIN     = True          # end piece: open windows into the cavity (hexagonal, 45 deg roof, vertical sides: no bridge): radial ones through the wall of the cup block and one through each side wall of the elbow; False = closed walls
EP_WIN_ANG = (30.0, 90.0, 150.0, 210.0, 270.0, 330.0)   # end piece: directions of the windows of the cup block (deg about the cup axis from +x)
EP_WIN_B   = 4.0           # end piece: half width of the windows of the cup block
EP_WIN_A   = 3.5           # end piece: half width of the windows of the elbow
ELBOW_R    = 15            # outer shape of the boom end pieces: a rounded elbow, a quarter torus whose centre line has this radius (RS + 0.5 ... XF - 0.5; 15 = gently rounded)
RING_ON    = True          # raised STOP RING on every link ball (M0 .. M3 = 8 balls): the top face of the cup comes to rest against it when the joint is tilted RING_LIMIT + RING_PLAY
RING_LIMIT = TILT_MAX      # tilt (deg) at which the stop engages (default = the ball limit)
RING_PLAY  = 0.2           # extra tilt (deg) before the stop touches, so that the pose limit itself is reached without contact
RING_H     = 1.8           # how far the ring stands out of the ball where its underside leaves the sphere (design-size mm)
RING_WALL  = 1.5           # height of the vertical outer wall of the ring (mm); the top of the ring is flat (perpendicular to the neck axis)
WIRE_HOLE  = 3.0           # diameter of the wire channel through every ball, neck, cup, end piece and rod (bare printed channel, NO liner). The ferrule pockets of the sliders keep their own small hole.
HOLE_FINISHED = True       # True: WIRE_HOLE is in mm of the FINISHED model (it stays 3 mm when BALL_D is small);  False: in design-size mm (it then shrinks with BALL_D: 3 mm at BALL_D = 8 would be 0.92 mm)
TIP_SLOT   = 1             # tip slider: slot from the wire hole and the ferrule pocket to a face: 1 = the face that looks out of the open side of the trough (visible, the ferrule pocket can be reached), -1 = the face against the closed back of the trough (the wire and a pre-crimped ferrule can then be laid in from the side), 0 = no slot (closed hole, like the stand slider)
BASE_CORNER = max(6.0, float(BASE_CORNER))
NC = 4                                                                  # connector positions k = 0 .. 3 at k * 90 deg from the +x side: tongues on k = 0, 1, sockets on k = 2, 3, so the tongue of one stand meets the socket of the next
RUN_CHECKS = True
CHECK_WIRE = False
OPEN_PANEL = True          # open the pose panel and the rotation gizmo when the macro ends

NBOOM = max(1, min(3, int(round(NBOOM))))
INTER = NBOOM > 1 and int(round(ARM_LINKS)) == 2          # the booms are joined by an M - DC - M stack (False: one loose ball)
TIP_SLOT = max(-1, min(1, int(round(TIP_SLOT))))
HEAD_BALLS = 2                 # fixed: the tip end is a cup, it needs the head link M2
TIP_LINKS = 2 if int(round(TIP_LINKS)) == 2 else 1
SHOULDER_LINKS = 2        # fixed: stand cup -> M0 -> connector DC -> M1 (the mast height follows from the base, see MAST_TOP below)
MU_W = 0.25    # wire sliding friction in the bare printed bend (assumed)
MU_CH = MU_W        # friction of the wire on the two printed drums of the base (assumed like the other bare bends; about 0.10 with a PTFE sleeve or a lubricated wire)
BASE_EFF = math.exp(-MU_CH * math.pi)   # tension left at the cup after the two 90 deg turns on the drums of the base (capstan: exp(-mu * pi / 2) each): 0.456 at mu = 0.25, 0.730 at 0.10
KS = BALL_D / (2.0 * RB)          # scale factor of the finished model (1 = full size)

# ============================== HELPERS ==============================
T30 = math.tan(math.radians(30))

# ---- wire channel (no liner: the wire runs in the bare printed channel, WIRE_HOLE wide) ----
FLARE_EDGE = 60.0 - TILT_MAX - 2.0     # deg from the ball pole: the flare around the hole must stay inside the contact circle of the seat (60 deg off the cup axis, nearest 60 - TILT_MAX) with 2 deg to spare
HOLE_R = 0.5 * WIRE_HOLE / KS if HOLE_FINISHED else 0.5 * WIRE_HOLE      # radius of the wire channel in design-size mm (the scale pass shrinks it with everything else)
_hmax = RB * math.sin(math.radians(FLARE_EDGE)) - 0.5          # the largest hole the ball can take (the flare edge would meet the hole edge)
if HOLE_R > _hmax:
    print("WIRE_HOLE: %.2f mm is more than the balls can take - limited to %.2f mm (design size)" % (2 * HOLE_R, 2 * _hmax)); HOLE_R = _hmax
HOLE_UP = 1.0 + max(0.0, (HOLE_R - 2.0) / T30)                 # the bore starts this far above the cup apex (a wide bore must reach the height where the cone of the seat is as wide: no ceiling over the cone)
R_WALL = 2.6                                                   # least wall around the channel (design-size mm)
R_NECK = max(7.0, HOLE_R + R_WALL)                             # rod between the two balls of a link
R_SPIG = max(5.0, HOLE_R + R_WALL); R_SOCK = R_SPIG + 0.2      # round spigot of the boom rod and the socket of the end pieces
R_ROD  = max(7.0, R_SPIG + 0.5)                                # core of the boom rod (the 3 mm disc)
ROD_RF = float(ROD_FLANGE_R)                                  # radius of the rod flange (smaller than the end piece stem RS: the cone socket of the end piece leaves a wall of RS - ROD_RF - 0.2 at its mouth)
ROD_CH = ROD_RF - R_SPIG                                       # height of the 45 deg cone from the spigot (R_SPIG) to the flange (ROD_RF): no flat rim is left
if ROD_RF > RS - 1.5: ROD_CH = 0.0
if ROD_FLANGE_R <= 0 or ROD_CH < 1.5 or BOOM_L - 2 * XF < 1.0: ROD_CH = 0.0   # switched off, too small (small model) or no rod (coupler peg): the old stepped spigot
ROD_ST = max(0.0, float(ROD_STUB)) if ROD_CH > 0 else 0.0     # length of the round stub at the tip of each cone
if WIRE_FINISHED: WIRE_D = WIRE_THICK / KS                       # design-size diameter of the wire
_wfit  = 2.0 * (HOLE_R - 0.25 / (KS if HOLE_FINISHED else 1.0))                                 # fits the channel with 0.25 mm (finished) clearance all round
_wball = 2.0 * RB * math.sin(math.radians(max(1.0, 58.0 - 2.0 * TILT_MAX - 0.5)))               # the footprint of the tilted wire must fit between the tilt (TILT_MAX) and the flare edge (FLARE_EDGE) on the ball
if WIRE_D > min(_wfit, _wball):
    print("WIRE: %.2f mm asked, %.2f mm used (finished size). Limits: channel %.2f mm, ball at %.0f deg tilt %.2f mm. A thicker wire at this ball size needs a smaller TILT_MAX." % (WIRE_D * KS, min(_wfit, _wball) * KS, _wfit * KS, TILT_MAX, _wball * KS))
    WIRE_D = min(_wfit, _wball)
WH_R   = WIRE_D / 2 + 0.5                                    # hole for the wire in the ferrule seats (sliders, pull block, head): smaller than the ferrule, so the ferrule stays
FER_R  = WIRE_D / 2 + 1.0                                    # crimp ferrule radius (1.75 for a 1.5 mm wire)
POCK_R = FER_R + 0.45                                        # pocket for the ferrule (2.2 for a 1.5 mm wire)
SL_WH_R = WIRE_D / 2 + 0.25                                  # wire hole / slot half width of the slotted tip slider: tighter than WH_R, so that the ferrule keeps about the same bearing area on the front wall although the slot cuts into the shoulder
TIP_CH  = 3.0                                                # 45 deg chamfer of the front edges of the long sides of the tip slider (the rest of its shape: see slider_block): the trough of the tip end has a 45 deg vault on top (self-supporting roof, no 20 mm bridge) and the chamfers keep the slider clear of it
SCR_END = 35.0                                               # free end of the tension screw (both ends, x of the tail frame, the slider as drawn): the socket of the slider ends at x = 23.5, and the slider travels 11 mm towards the wall,
                                                             # so its socket bottom reaches x = 34.5: the screw has to end at or beyond that (0.5 mm spare). Engaged thread: 6 mm at the start of the travel, 17 mm at the end
SCR_PHASE = 360.0 * (((TE_WALL + 0.7) - 41.0) / THREAD_P % 1.0)   # turn (deg) of the thread groove of the sliders about the screw axis: the shoulder of the screw is 15.7 mm = 6.28 pitches from the socket mouth, so without this turn the helix of the groove is 100.8 deg out of phase with the helix of the screw in the drawn position
def cyl(r, h, p=(0, 0, 0), d=(0, 0, 1)): return Part.makeCylinder(r, h, V(*p), V(*d))
def box(x0, x1, y0, y1, z0, z1): return Part.makeBox(x1 - x0, y1 - y0, z1 - z0, V(x0, y0, z0))
def hexp(af, h, p, d=(0, 0, 1)):
    r = af / math.sqrt(3)
    pts = [V(r * math.cos(math.radians(60 * i)), r * math.sin(math.radians(60 * i)), 0) for i in range(7)]
    s = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(pts)).extrude(V(0, 0, h))
    s.Placement = App.Placement(V(*p), App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), V(*d)))
    return s
def fuse(*s):
    r = s[0]
    for x in s[1:]: r = r.fuse(x)
    return r.removeSplitter()
def seat(R, c, rb=2.0, clear=0.15):
    """conical cup (opens upward) touching the ball on a ring 60 deg off the axis; returns cone, apex z, radius at centre height"""
    Rr = R + clear; rho = Rr * math.sin(math.radians(60)); zr = c[2] - Rr * 0.5
    zb = zr - (rho - rb) / T30; rtop = rho + (c[2] - zr) * T30
    return Part.makeCone(rb, rtop, c[2] - zb, V(c[0], c[1], zb), V(0, 0, 1)), zb, rtop
def seat_depth(R): return -seat(R, (0, 0, 0))[1]
def cone_cut(R, c, dirn):
    """flare around the wire hole: a cone from the hole at the ball centre, widening so that its edge on the sphere lies FLARE_EDGE deg from the pole
    (the wire can bend TILT_MAX at the ball centre without touching the ball, and the flare stays clear of the seat contact)"""
    h = R + 1; r0 = HOLE_R + 0.05; ph = math.radians(FLARE_EDGE)
    t = max(0.0, (R * math.sin(ph) - r0) / (R * math.cos(ph)))        # tan of the flare half angle
    return Part.makeCone(r0, r0 + h * t, h, V(*c), V(0, 0, dirn))
def fluted(r, h, p, d, n=12, fr=2.4):
    body = cyl(r, h, p, d); dv = V(*d); dv.normalize()
    ref = V(1, 0, 0) if abs(dv.x) < 0.9 else V(0, 1, 0)
    u = dv.cross(ref); u.normalize(); w = dv.cross(u)
    for i in range(n):
        a = 2 * math.pi * i / n
        body = body.cut(Part.makeCylinder(fr, h, V(*p) + u * (math.cos(a) * r) + w * (math.sin(a) * r), dv))
    return body
def bend_bore(r, rb, z_top, x_end):
    """swept bore of radius r: straight down the cup axis to z = rb, quarter circle of radius rb (centre x=rb, z=rb), then straight along the rod axis to x_end"""
    parts = []
    if z_top > rb: parts.append(cyl(r, z_top - rb, (0, 0, rb)))
    f = Part.Face(Part.Wire([Part.makeCircle(r, V(0, 0, rb), V(0, 0, 1))]))
    parts.append(f.revolve(V(rb, 0, rb), V(0, -1, 0), 90))
    if x_end > rb: parts.append(cyl(r, x_end - rb, (rb, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
    return fuse(*parts)

# ============================== LAYOUT ==============================
RW = RP + WIRE_D / 2                      # wire centre-line radius on a drum
# ---- top-tensioned base: heights (design-size mm). Wire: cup centre -> straight down out of the ball -> drum A (90 deg) -> run along the floor -> drum B (90 deg) -> up into the slider ----
XT   = 44.0                               # distance of the tensioner axis (slider, screw) from the mast axis: the stand end (cup block r 15.6, back of the tail 12.5 mm towards the mast, trough open OUTWARD) stands clear of the stand ball and the first link
MAST_TOP = BASE_H + ZG                    # height of the stand cup (centre of the first ball): the rim of the cup is flush with the deck (the deck is printed face down on the bed)
ZB_DROP    = 0.75                          # the wire corners of the base (axis height zB) are this much lower than the ball allows: the 45 deg flank of the rib then meets the seat cone of the cup lower, the flat ledge under the ball gets shorter (the wire floor is 1.7 mm above the table, its underside 0.45 mm)
zB   = math.floor(10.0 * (MAST_TOP - math.sqrt((RB + RP + 0.6) ** 2 - RW ** 2))) / 10.0 - ZB_DROP      # axis height of both drums: as high as the lower pole of the stand ball allows (0.6 mm clear of the ball)
zh   = zB - RW                            # height of the horizontal wire run above the table (no bottom plate: the base stands on its wall)
if zh < WIRE_D / 2 + 0.4: print("WARNING: the wire run is only %.2f mm above the table" % zh)
TZ0  = BASE_H + (TD - ZG)                  # origin of the tensioner frame (= tail frame of the end, x up): the rim plane of the cup of the end (4.5 mm above the cup centre, 12 mm below the origin) lies on the deck
ZEW  = TZ0 + TE_WALL                      # outer face of the end wall of the stand end (the knob sits on it)
DU   = BASE_H - 4.0                       # underside of the deck
XB   = XT - RW                            # axis of drum B
L = BOOM_L; A = BOOM_A
def dvec(th): return V(0, -math.sin(math.radians(th)), math.cos(math.radians(th)))   # direction a cup opens in
def tp(v): return (v.x, v.y, v.z)
def upz(d): return d if d.z > -0.5 else d * (-1)
HD  = LINK_T if HEAD_BALLS == 2 else 0     # distance between the last boom ball and the head pivot
D1 = LINK_D
if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2:      # stand cup -> M0 -> connector DC -> M1: the stand cup stays at MAST_TOP, the probe tip height follows from the stack
    C0a = (0, 0, MAST_TOP); C0b = (0, 0, MAST_TOP + LINK_D); C1a = (0, 0, C0b[2] + DC_D)
    N1 = C1a[2] + D1; TIP_Z = N1 - 106 - HD
else:                        # stand cup -> M1: the mast height follows from the probe tip height TIP_Z
    N1 = TIP_Z + 106 + HD; MAST_TOP = N1 - D1; C0a = C0b = None; C1a = (0, 0, MAST_TOP)
C1b = (0, 0, N1); CBASE = C0a if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2 else C1a      # CBASE = centre of the ball in the stand cup
ANG_F = [ELBOW_ANG[_i] % 360 for _i in range(NBOOM - 1)] + [TIP_ANG % 360]       # cup direction at the FAR end of each boom
ANG_N = [180] + [(a + 180) % 360 for a in ANG_F[:NBOOM - 1]]        # cup direction at the NEAR end of each boom
S_ARM = LINK_T + DC_D + LINK_T                                  # length of one connector stack (M - DC - M), upper ball of the first link -> lower ball of the second one
BALL = [V(*C1b)]; AXIS = []; FARB = []                         # BALL[k] = near ball of boom k+1 (the last entry: the head ball), FARB[k] = ball in the far cup of boom k+1
for _k in range(NBOOM):
    _a0 = BALL[_k] - dvec(ANG_N[_k]) * A                    # rod axis point at the near cup
    _fb = _a0 + V(L, 0, 0) + dvec(ANG_F[_k]) * A
    AXIS.append(_a0); FARB.append(_fb)
    BALL.append(_fb + dvec(ANG_F[_k]) * S_ARM if (INTER and _k < NBOOM - 1) else _fb)       # the next boom starts at the lower ball of the stack
CB = [tp(_b) for _b in BALL]; C4b = tp(FARB[NBOOM - 1])     # ball centres; C4b = the head ball (far cup of the last boom)
XH, YH = C4b[0], C4b[1]
# the tip side (M2, DC2, M3, tip end) is built hanging straight down from the far cup of the boom, the centre of that cup is the origin (canonical frame), and placed by HEADPL:
SPL = [App.Placement(FARB[_s], App.Rotation(V(1, 0, 0), ANG_F[_s] - 180)) for _s in range(NBOOM)]       # frame of the stack that hangs from the far cup of boom s+1: turned about the rod axis so that it points where that cup opens (180 = down)
HEADPL = SPL[-1]                                                                     # the tip side is the last stack
HZ4a = -HD                                                                        # lower ball of M2
if TIP_LINKS == 2: HZ5a = HZ4a - DC_D; HZ5b = HZ5a - LINK_T; HZT = HZ5b          # M2 -> connector DC2 -> M3 -> tip end: the same stack as M0 -> DC -> M1 on the shoulder (HZ5a = upper ball of M3, HZ5b = lower ball of M3 = cup of the tip end)
else: HZ5a = HZ5b = None; HZT = HZ4a
def _hp(z): return tp(HEADPL.multVec(V(0, 0, z)))                                # point on the axis of the tip side (canonical z) -> global
C4a = _hp(HZ4a); CT = _hp(HZT); C5a = _hp(HZ5a) if TIP_LINKS == 2 else None; C5b = _hp(HZ5b) if TIP_LINKS == 2 else None
HZI5a = HZ4a - DC_D; HZI5b = HZI5a - LINK_T                                         # the same stack between two booms (always M - DC - M)
def _hps(s, z): return tp(SPL[s].multVec(V(0, 0, z)))
STK = [(tp(FARB[_s]), _hps(_s, HZ4a), _hps(_s, HZI5a), _hps(_s, HZI5b)) for _s in range(NBOOM)]      # per boom: (far cup centre, lower ball of the first link, upper ball of the second link, lower ball of the second link)
STACKS = list(range(1, NBOOM + 1)) if INTER else [NBOOM]                             # the stacks s that exist (s hangs from the far cup of boom s)
def SN(s):                                                                           # names of the parts of stack s: first link, double cup, second link (without INTER: M2, DC2, M3 as before)
    n = s if INTER else 1
    return ("M%d" % (2 * n), "DC%d" % (n + 1), "M%d" % (2 * n + 1))
def STK_FULL(s): return s < NBOOM or TIP_LINKS == 2                                   # a tip side with one link has no DC and no second link
def STACK_PARTS(s): return list(SN(s)) if STK_FULL(s) else [SN(s)[0]]
NMLINK = 2 + sum(2 if STK_FULL(_s) else 1 for _s in STACKS)                           # number of M links: M0 .. M(NMLINK-1)
CH = (0, 0, HZ4a); RH = RB
TE_XF = 20.5                               # where the wire ends in a tensioner (inside the ferrule), measured along the screw axis
BASE_PL = App.Placement(V(0, 0, 0), App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), 180))       # the base is built with the tensioner on +x and turned half a turn about the mast: the tensioner stands on the side away from the head
TE_FR = App.Placement(V(XT, 0, TZ0), App.Rotation(V(0, 1, 0), -90).multiply(App.Rotation(V(1, 0, 0), 180)))      # frame of the vertical tensioner inside the base: local x (screw axis) -> up, local z (open side of the trough) -> OUTWARD, away from the mast
STAND_TPL = BASE_PL.multiply(TE_FR)
TE_REL = App.Placement(V(0, 0, -TD), App.Rotation(V(0, 1, 0), 90))                                     # tail frame of an end relative to its cup frame (TIP_TAIL_PL = TIP_PL * TE_REL)
STAND_TE_PL = STAND_TPL.multiply(TE_REL.inverse())                                                      # the SAME end upside down on the deck: cup at the bottom (opens onto the deck), tail and knob up, trough open outward
TIP_PL = HEADPL.multiply(App.Placement(V(0, 0, HZT), App.Rotation()))                                  # straight tip end: cup centre = origin, wire and tail run straight down (-z)
TIP_TAIL_PL = HEADPL.multiply(App.Placement(V(0, 0, HZT - TD), App.Rotation(V(0, 1, 0), 90)))           # tail frame of the tip end: tail x axis -> -z, trough opens towards +x
XP, YP, ZTIP = tp(HEADPL.multVec(V(0, 0, HZT - (TD + TE_WALL))))      # load point of the margins (test weight): outer face of the end wall of the tip end, on the wire axis

PRINT = (0.76, 0.78, 0.82); STEEL = (0.42, 0.44, 0.48); TEAL = (0.10, 0.55, 0.55)
doc = App.newDocument(DOC_NAME)
OBJ = {}; ROLE = {}; NEUT = {}
def add(name, shape, color, role="printed", placement=None):
    o = doc.addObject("Part::Feature", name); o.Shape = shape
    if placement is not None: o.Placement = placement; NEUT[o.Name] = placement
    if App.GuiUp: o.ViewObject.ShapeColor = color
    OBJ[o.Name] = o; ROLE[o.Name] = role
    return o

# ============================== BASE WITH TOP TENSIONER, TIP TENSIONER END, PRINTED SLIDER AND SCREW ==============================
# ---- thread: taken over unchanged from jumper_wire_pen_assembly.FCMacro (printed there, 45 deg flanks, flat crest and root); +Z axis, rotated into place below
SOCKET_EXTRA = 0.5      # a socket is this much deeper than its stub is long
def cyl_z(r, z0, z1): return Part.makeCylinder(r, z1 - z0, V(0, 0, z0), V(0, 0, 1))
def clean(shape):
    """Merge coplanar faces, but only keep the result if it is still a valid solid of the same volume and it still survives a half cut."""
    try:
        sc = shape.copy().removeSplitter()
        if sc.isValid() and abs(sc.Volume - shape.Volume) <= 1e-3 * abs(shape.Volume):
            bb = sc.BoundBox
            probe = Part.makeBox(bb.XLength + 10.0, 120.0, 240.0, V(bb.XMin - 5.0, -120.0, -120.0))
            r = sc.cut(probe)
            if r.isValid() and r.Volume > 0.05 * sc.Volume: return sc
    except Exception: pass
    return shape
def thread_extra(pitch, depth):
    """How far the ridge reaches into the core so that it fuses cleanly."""
    flat = pitch / 2.0 - depth
    return min(0.1, max(flat / 2.0 - 0.02, 0.0))
def ridge_hw(pitch, depth):
    """Half width of the ridge at its buried inner end (45-degree flanks)."""
    return pitch / 4.0 + depth / 2.0 + thread_extra(pitch, depth)
def thread_ridge(r_crest, pitch, depth, z0, z1):
    """Helical trapezoid ridge around +Z: 45-degree flanks, flat crest and flat root of equal width (pitch/2 - depth). The centre-line runs from z0 to z1."""
    flat = pitch / 2.0 - depth; extra = thread_extra(pitch, depth)
    hw_c = flat / 2.0; hw_a = ridge_hw(pitch, depth); r_a = r_crest - depth - extra
    helix = Part.makeHelix(pitch, z1 - z0, r_a)
    pts = [V(r_a, 0, -hw_a), V(r_crest, 0, -hw_c), V(r_crest, 0, hw_c), V(r_a, 0, hw_a), V(r_a, 0, -hw_a)]
    sw = helix.makePipeShell([Part.makePolygon(pts)], True, True)
    sw.translate(V(0, 0, z0)); return sw
def make_stub_gen(R_M, P, depth, Lt, ch=0.0, rc=0.0):
    """A male thread stub (axis +Z, shoulder at z = 0). With ch > 0 the free end gets a 45-degree lead-in chamfer."""
    z0 = ridge_hw(P, depth) + 0.05
    stub = cyl_z(R_M - depth, 0.0, Lt).fuse(thread_ridge(R_M, P, depth, z0, Lt - z0))
    ch = min(ch, 0.25 * Lt)
    if ch > 0.0:
        r_end = R_M - depth - ch; r_out = R_M + 1.0; reach = r_out - r_end
        keep = Part.makeCone(r_end, r_out, reach, V(0, 0, Lt), V(0, 0, -1)).fuse(cyl_z(r_out, -1.0, Lt - reach))
        stub = stub.common(keep)
    return stub
def make_socket_tool(R_M, P, depth, Lt, clr, bore_to, ch=0.0):
    """Cutting tool for a female thread (mouth at z = 0, going to +Z), same thread phase as make_stub_gen. The plain bore goes on down to z = bore_to."""
    Ls = Lt + SOCKET_EXTRA; z0 = ridge_hw(P, depth) + 0.05; hw_a = ridge_hw(P, depth); k = 0
    while z0 - k * P > -hw_a - 0.1: k += 1
    z0s = z0 - k * P; z1s = Ls - (hw_a - thread_extra(P, depth)) - 0.05
    tool = cyl_z(R_M - depth + clr, -1.0, max(bore_to, Ls)).fuse(thread_ridge(R_M + clr, P, depth, z0s, z1s))
    if ch > 0.0:
        r_b = R_M - depth + clr; r_top = R_M + clr + ch + 0.5
        tool = tool.fuse(Part.makeCone(r_top, r_b, r_top - r_b, V(0, 0, -0.5), V(0, 0, 1)))
    return tool
ZCOL0 = 12.5                       # underside of the collar below the deck (the lugs of drum A hang from it)
R_COL = 18.0                       # radius of that collar
R_FREE = 1.0                       # rounding of the free edges (the table side of the wall and of the ring, the underside of the collar)
CH_BED = 0.8                       # 45 deg chamfer of the edges that lie on the bed (outer edge of the deck): no elephant foot, no overhang
def _circ(shp, r, z, tol=1e-3):
    """circular edges of radius r at height z"""
    return [e for e in shp.Edges if e.Curve.__class__.__name__ == "Circle" and abs(e.Curve.Radius - r) < tol and abs(e.BoundBox.ZMin - z) < tol and abs(e.BoundBox.ZMax - z) < tol]
def _soft(shp, fn, rad, edges, what):
    """fillet / chamfer that never stops the macro: if OpenCascade refuses, the edge stays sharp and the macro says so"""
    if not edges: print("WARNING: no edges to round for", what); return shp
    try:
        r = fn(shp, rad, edges)
        if r.isValid() and abs(r.Volume - shp.Volume) < 0.2 * shp.Volume: return r
    except Exception as ex: print("WARNING: rounding failed for", what, ex)
    print("WARNING: edge left sharp:", what); return shp
def _fil(shp, rad, edges, what): return _soft(shp, lambda sh, r, e: sh.makeFillet(r, e), rad, edges, what)
def _chf(shp, rad, edges, what): return _soft(shp, lambda sh, r, e: sh.makeChamfer(r, e), rad, edges, what)
def _at_z(shp, z, tol=1e-6):
    return [e for e in shp.Edges if abs(e.BoundBox.ZMin - z) < tol and abs(e.BoundBox.ZMax - z) < tol]
CN_LEN = 9.0                              # tongue: length from the wall (design-size mm)
CN_ROOT = 8.0                             # tongue: width at the wall
CN_ANG = 20.0                             # dovetail flank angle from the sliding direction: the tongue is wider at its tip (8 mm -> 14.5 mm)
CN_CLR = 0.25                             # clearance per side between tongue and socket at design size (a sliding fit; raise it if your printer is coarse); on a small model it is never less than 0.15 mm in the finished part
CN_WALL = 3.5                             # socket housing: wall beside the socket
CN_BACK = 2.0                             # socket housing: wall behind the bottom of the socket
CN_DS = CN_LEN + 0.5                      # depth of the socket (0.5 mm spare at its bottom)
CN_HF = CN_DS + CN_BACK                   # how far the socket housing reaches INTO the base from the outer face of the wall (the sockets are recessed inside the base: nothing stands out of the wall but the tongues)
CN_GUS = 5.0                              # socket housing: radius of the concave fillets that blend its root into the wall (0 = none)
CN_FIL_T = 1.5                            # tongue: radius of the two tip corners (rounder than the bottom of the socket, so they never touch it)
CN_FIL_S = 0.8                            # socket: radius of the two bottom corners of the slot
CN_FIL_M = 0.8                            # socket: radius of the two edges of the mouth
CN_LEAD = 0.8                             # lead-in of the socket: 45 deg countersink at both ends of the slot (0 = none); the tongue tips have 0.8 mm 45 deg chamfers
CN_GAP = 0.2                              # gap between the walls of two stands joined side by side (the tongue is 9 mm long and goes 8.8 mm into the socket)
def conn_pitch(k=0): return 2 * BASE_R + CN_GAP                                           # distance between the centres of two stands joined side by side, design size
RIB        = True                          # wire path of the base: ONE solid rib under the deck (its lower edge is the wire path: round the two corners, along the floor) instead of two drums with four lugs; False = the old drums and lugs
RIB_W      = 6.2                           # rib: thickness (y); the wire runs in a channel along its outer edge
RIB_S      = 0.0                           # rib: distance of its edge from the wire centre line (the wire radius is 1.25: 0 = the wire lies half (1.25 mm) in the channel)
RIB_G      = 1.4                           # rib: radius of the channel (the wire is 1.25 in radius: 0.15 mm of play); the channel is a half circle, 1.4 mm deep
WIN_ON     = True                          # LIGHTENING WINDOWS: through the deck, 3 mm webs between them and round everything that stays (windows between 3 spokes, about 25-30 cm3 less at 100 % fill); False = the plain deck
WIN_WEB    = 3.0                           # windows: web left round the wall, the ring, the collar, the end, the rib and the connector housings
WIN_R      = 3.0                           # windows: radius of the corners (smaller corners are not cut)
WIN_SPOKE  = 8.0                           # windows: width of the spokes that hold the collar (they join the collar, the ring and the wall)
WIN_SPOKES = (180.0, 90.0, 270.0)          # windows: directions of the spokes (deg from +x; the +x side is the rib): -x, +y, -y
WIN_MIN    = 150.0                         # windows: smaller openings (mm2) are left out
TE_VOID    = True                          # TENSIONER END: the cup block is hollow (a closed cavity between the conical seat and the outer wall, TE_VOID_W thick walls, no overhang steeper than 30 deg from vertical); False = solid block
TE_VOID_W  = 3.0                           # end: wall of the cup block round the cavity (measured square to the seat cone, and at the outer wall)
KNOB_DISH  = 8.0                           # tension screw: radius of the 45 deg conical dish in the outer face of the knob (it faces the bed when printed; 0 = solid knob)
TE_WIN     = True                          # TENSIONER END: open windows (hexagonal, 45 deg roof and sill, vertical sides: no bridge) through the two side walls and the back wall of the tail and through the wall of the cup block (into the cavity); False = closed walls
TE_WIN_A   = 5.5                           # end: half width of the windows of the tail (the side windows are centred at x = -1, the back windows at y = 0)
TE_WIN_S   = 4.0                           # end: strut between two windows of the tail (measured across the 45 deg ends)
TE_WIN_ANG = (0.0, 45.0, 135.0, 180.0, 225.0, 315.0)   # end: directions of the windows of the cup block (deg about the cup axis from +x; the ears are at 90 and 270)
TE_WIN_B   = 4.0                           # end: half width of the windows of the cup block
TIP_PROBE  = True                          # SCOPE PROBE HOLDER instead of the tip tensioner: the last link ends in a holder (cup, wire anchor, clamp for the probe body); the wire is tensioned at the stand end only. False = the old tip tensioner (end, slider, screw)
PROBE_D    = 13.0                          # probe body diameter (design-size mm: the whole model scales with BALL_D, use BALL_D = 26 for a real probe)
PROBE_CLR  = 0.1                           # clearance between the probe body and the bore of the clamp (per side)
PROBE_LEN  = 120.0                         # length of the probe (only the stand-in solid that is used for the collision tests and the picture)
PROBE_OUT  = 45.0                          # how far the probe sticks out below the clamp (the tip end of the stand-in)
PH_OFF     = 26.0                          # axis of the probe beside the wire axis (+x of the tip side frame, away from the boom): the probe lies beside the last link, its cable end up
PH_H       = 18.0                          # height of the clamp ring
PH_WALL    = 3.0                           # wall of the clamp ring
PH_GAP     = 10.5                          # opening of the C (smaller than the probe: it snaps in from the side); the plastic screw across the two tabs closes it
PH_TAB     = 6.0                           # thickness of each tab
PH_ARM     = 10.0                          # height of the arm between the wire anchor and the clamp (it lies on the bed)
PH_THREAD_D = 6.0                          # clamp screw (PRINTED, plastic, the thread profile of the tension screw: 45 deg flanks): outer diameter
PH_THREAD_P = 1.5                          # clamp screw: pitch
PH_THREAD_DEPTH = 0.45                     # clamp screw: depth of the thread
PH_SCREW_L  = 25.0                         # clamp screw: length of the threaded stub (it passes the -y tab and the gap, goes right through the +y tab and sticks out of it by 2.5 mm)
PH_SOCK     = 7.0                          # clamp screw: length of the threaded hole in the +y tab: right through it (the tab is 6 mm thick, the tool runs 1 mm out of it)
PH_KNOB_R   = 7.0                          # clamp screw: radius of the fluted knob
DRUM_FLANK = True                          # drum A: the fill above the wire has a 45 deg flank that starts at the point where the wire leaves the drum (no flat roof hanging in the air when the base is printed upside down); False = the old teardrop with a flat top
DRUM_BALL_CLR = 0.3                       # least gap between the filled-in top of drum A and the ball (the bare drum is 0.6 mm clear)
def base_outline(inset=0.0, z=0.0):
    """outline of the wall (inset = 0) or of its inner face (inset = 4): a square with rounded corners"""
    a = BASE_R - inset; return rr_outline(-a, a, -a, a, BASE_CORNER - inset, BASE_CORNER - inset, z)
def rounded_wire(pts, rad, z):
    """closed wire through the corner points pts (x, y) at height z, corner i rounded with radius rad[i] (0 = sharp)"""
    n = len(pts); segs = []; prev = None; first = None
    cuts = []
    for i in range(n):
        q = pts[i]; a = pts[i - 1]; b = pts[(i + 1) % n]; r = rad[i]
        u1 = (a[0] - q[0], a[1] - q[1]); l1 = math.hypot(*u1); u1 = (u1[0] / l1, u1[1] / l1)
        u2 = (b[0] - q[0], b[1] - q[1]); l2 = math.hypot(*u2); u2 = (u2[0] / l2, u2[1] / l2)
        if r <= 0: cuts.append((q, q, None)); continue
        th = math.acos(max(-1.0, min(1.0, u1[0] * u2[0] + u1[1] * u2[1]))); td = r / math.tan(th / 2.0)
        t1 = (q[0] + u1[0] * td, q[1] + u1[1] * td); t2 = (q[0] + u2[0] * td, q[1] + u2[1] * td)
        bx, by = u1[0] + u2[0], u1[1] + u2[1]; bl = math.hypot(bx, by); bx, by = bx / bl, by / bl; dc = r / math.sin(th / 2.0)
        c = (q[0] + bx * dc, q[1] + by * dc); m = (c[0] - bx * r, c[1] - by * r)
        cuts.append((t1, t2, m))
    P = lambda t: V(t[0], t[1], z); edges = []
    for i in range(n):
        t1, t2, m = cuts[i]
        if m is not None: edges.append(Part.Arc(P(t1), P(m), P(t2)).toShape())
        nxt = cuts[(i + 1) % n][0]
        if (t2[0] - nxt[0]) ** 2 + (t2[1] - nxt[1]) ** 2 > 1e-12: edges.append(Part.LineSegment(P(t2), P(nxt)).toShape())
    return Part.Wire(Part.__sortEdges__(edges))
def make_connectors():
    """vertical dovetails in the middle of the four sides (position k at k * 90 deg from the +x side, built at +x, then turned about the mast). Positions 0, 1: a TONGUE (trapezoid, 8 mm at the wall, 14.5 mm at the tip,
    9 mm long, tip corners rounded); positions 2, 3: a SOCKET, recessed INTO the base: a housing block inside the wall (blended into the wall with concave fillets) and a through slot of the same trapezoid cut through wall,
    housing and deck, mouth on the outer face of the wall, 0.25 mm clearance. So the walls of two joined stands are only CN_GAP = 0.2 mm apart. No sharp edges: concave fillets at the root of the housing, rounded bottom corners
    of the slot and rounded edges of its mouth, a 45 deg countersink at both ends of the slot, 45 deg chamfers at the ends of tongue and housing. Position k and k + 2 are opposite, so the tongue of one stand meets
    the socket of the next. They run the full height (z 0 .. BASE_H), so they slide together VERTICALLY: lower one stand onto its neighbour. Everything is a vertical prism, a fillet or a 45 deg chamfer: nothing overhangs.
    Returns (solids to fuse with the base, sockets to cut from it afterwards: [(position k, slot, countersinks, local position of the mouth edges)])."""
    t = math.tan(math.radians(CN_ANG)); H = BASE_H; R = BASE_R; adds = []; cuts = []
    def rot(shp, k): shp = shp.copy(); shp.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), k * 360.0 / NC); return shp
    for k in range(NC):
        if k % 2 == 0 and not CONN_X: continue                                                                 # the pair on the +x / -x sides is optional
        if k < NC // 2:
            w0 = CN_ROOT / 2 - 2.0 * t; wt = CN_ROOT / 2 + CN_LEN * t
            sol = Part.Face(rounded_wire([(R - 2.0, -w0), (R + CN_LEN, -wt), (R + CN_LEN, wt), (R - 2.0, w0)], [0, CN_FIL_T, CN_FIL_T, 0], 0.0)).extrude(V(0, 0, H))
            sol = _chf(sol, 0.8, _at_z(sol, H) + _at_z(sol, 0.0), "tongue ends")
            adds.append(rot(sol, k))
        else:
            clr = max(CN_CLR, 0.15 / KS); wm = CN_ROOT / 2 + clr; wh = wm + CN_DS * t; Wh = 2 * (wh + CN_WALL)
            xo = R; xi = xo - CN_DS; xb = xi - CN_BACK                                                              # outer face of the wall, bottom of the slot, back of the housing
            blk = Part.Face(rr_outline(xb, R - 1.0, -Wh / 2, Wh / 2, 3.0, 0.5, 0.0)).extrude(V(0, 0, H))            # housing inside the wall, ending 1 mm inside the wall
            blk = _chf(blk, 0.4, _at_z(blk, 0.0), "socket housing, table side")                                      # (its bed side is inside the deck: no chamfer there)
            if CN_GUS > 0:                                                                                         # concave fillets between the housing and the inner face of the wall (radius CN_GUS)
                g = CN_GUS; yh = Wh / 2; xw = R - 4.0; c45 = math.sqrt(0.5)
                for sg in (1, -1):
                    ed = [Part.LineSegment(V(xw + 1.0, sg * (yh - 0.5), 0), V(xw - g, sg * (yh - 0.5), 0)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(V(xw - g, sg * (yh - 0.5), 0), V(xw - g, sg * yh, 0)).toShape(),
                          Part.Arc(V(xw - g, sg * yh, 0), V(xw - g + c45 * g, sg * (yh + g - c45 * g), 0), V(xw, sg * (yh + g), 0)).toShape(),
                          Part.LineSegment(V(xw, sg * (yh + g), 0), V(xw + 1.0, sg * (yh + g), 0)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(V(xw + 1.0, sg * (yh + g), 0), V(xw + 1.0, sg * (yh - 0.5), 0)).toShape()]
                    blk = blk.fuse(Part.Face(Part.Wire(Part.__sortEdges__(ed))).extrude(V(0, 0, H)))
            adds.append(rot(blk, k))
            def slot_wire(d, z): return rounded_wire([(xo + 1.0 + d, -(wm + d - t)), (xi, -(wh + d)), (xi, wh + d), (xo + 1.0 + d, wm + d - t)], [0, CN_FIL_S + d, CN_FIL_S + d, 0], z)
            slot = Part.Face(slot_wire(0.0, -1.0)).extrude(V(0, 0, H + 2.0)); cs = []
            if CN_LEAD > 0:                                                                                        # countersink: the slot widens by CN_LEAD at each end, 45 deg
                dl = CN_LEAD / math.cos(math.radians(CN_ANG))                                                       # sideways offset CN_LEAD / cos(flank angle) = CN_LEAD square to the flank: exactly 45 deg
                for z0, z1 in ((H, H - CN_LEAD), (0.0, CN_LEAD)): cs.append(rot(Part.makeLoft([slot_wire(dl, z0), slot_wire(0.0, z1)], True, True), k))
            a = math.radians(k * 360.0 / NC); ca, sa = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)
            mouth = [(R * ca - y * sa, R * sa + y * ca) for y in (wm, -wm)]                                         # where the flanks of the slot meet the outer face of the wall
            cuts.append((k, rot(slot, k), cs, mouth))
    return adds, cuts
def cut_sockets(base, cuts):
    """cut the slots of the sockets through wall, housing and deck, round the edges of their mouths, then the countersinks"""
    for k, slot, cs, mouth in cuts:
        base = base.cut(slot)
        sel = [e for e in base.Edges if e.BoundBox.ZLength > BASE_H - 3.0 and e.BoundBox.XLength < 1e-6 and e.BoundBox.YLength < 1e-6
               and any(math.hypot(e.BoundBox.XMin - mx, e.BoundBox.YMin - my) < 0.2 for mx, my in mouth)]
        base = _fil(base, CN_FIL_M, sel, "mouth of the slot")
        for c in cs: base = base.cut(c)
    return base
def key_geom():
    """(inner radius, outer radius) of the part of the ears that goes into the deck: it starts 0.3 mm inside the block (rho) and ends KEY_OUT outside it"""
    zb = -seat_depth(RB); rrim = 2.0 + (-ZG - zb) * T30; rho = rrim + 3.0
    return rho - 0.3, rho + KEY_OUT, rho
def key_sector(r1, r2, half_len, z0, h):
    """annular sector r1..r2, 2 * half_len long along the arc, centred on the +x axis, from z0 up by h"""
    rm = (r1 + r2) / 2.0; a = math.degrees(half_len / rm)
    sec = Part.makeCylinder(r2, h, V(0, 0, z0), V(0, 0, 1), 2.0 * a).cut(Part.makeCylinder(r1, h + 2.0, V(0, 0, z0 - 1.0), V(0, 0, 1)))
    sec.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), -a); return sec
def end_keys():
    """the two ears of the end (local frame: cup axis z, rim plane z = -ZG, ears at +-y): profile (radius, z) = flat top KEY_H above the rim plane, vertical outer face, 45 deg underside back to the wall of the block (no overhang when it is printed standing, cup up)"""
    r1, r2, rho = key_geom(); zt = -ZG + KEY_H; zr = -ZG - 0.5
    prof = [V(rho - 1.0, 0, zr - KEY_OUT), V(rho, 0, zr - KEY_OUT), V(r2, 0, zr), V(r2, 0, zt), V(r1, 0, zt), V(r1, 0, -ZG - 0.3), V(rho - 1.0, 0, -ZG - 0.3), V(rho - 1.0, 0, zr - KEY_OUT)]
    rm = (r1 + r2) / 2.0; a = math.degrees(KEY_L / 2.0 / rm); ks = []
    for ang in (90.0, 270.0):
        k = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(prof)).revolve(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), 2.0 * a); k.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), ang - a)
        ks.append(_chf(k, 0.4, [e for e in k.Edges if abs(e.BoundBox.ZMin - zt) < 1e-6 and abs(e.BoundBox.ZMax - zt) < 1e-6 and e.BoundBox.XLength + e.BoundBox.YLength > 1.0], "top of an ear"))
    return fuse(*ks)
def key_slots():
    """the two through slots of the deck for the ears of the end (the end axis is at x = XT, the ears at +-y of it); the slot starts at the stop-ring-free radius r1 = rho - 0.3, the part of the ear inside the block is above the rim"""
    r1, r2, rho = key_geom(); ks = []
    for ang in (90.0, 270.0):
        k = key_sector(r1 - KEY_CLR, r2 + KEY_CLR, KEY_L / 2.0 + KEY_CLR, DU, BASE_H + 1.0 - DU); k.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), ang); k.translate(V(XT, 0, 0)); ks.append(k)
    return fuse(*ks)
def make_rib():
    """the wire guide of the base: one rib, a plate RIB_W thick in the plane of the wire path (y = 0), hanging from the deck. Its lower edge follows the wire path at a distance RIB_S from the wire centre line, with a round CHANNEL of radius RIB_G for the wire (swept along the path):
    left side line (45 deg, from the point where the wire leaves the ball straight down, so nothing leans out more than 45 deg when the base is printed upside down), round corner RR = RW - RIB_S (drum A), flat along the floor, round corner (drum B), vertical wall up to the deck beside the hole."""
    RR = RW - RIB_S; xl = RW - RR; zt = DU + 0.5; cA = xl - zB; xr = XB + RR; hw = RIB_W / 2.0; c = math.sqrt(0.5); P = lambda x, z: V(x, -hw, z)
    e = [Part.LineSegment(P(xl, zB), P(cA + zt, zt)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P(cA + zt, zt), P(xr, zt)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P(xr, zt), P(xr, zB)).toShape(),
         Part.Arc(P(xr, zB), P(XB + RR * c, zB - RR * c), P(XB, zB - RR)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P(XB, zB - RR), P(RW, zB - RR)).toShape(), Part.Arc(P(RW, zB - RR), P(RW - RR * c, zB - RR * c), P(xl, zB)).toShape()]
    rib = Part.Face(Part.Wire(e)).extrude(V(0, RIB_W, 0))
    if RIB_G > 0:                                                                                  # the channel: a circle of radius RIB_G swept along the wire centre line (from the left point of drum A, round both corners, up to the deck)
        Q = lambda x, z: V(x, 0, z); w = RW; ze = DU + 1.0
        pe = [Part.LineSegment(Q(0, zB + 2.0), Q(0, zB)).toShape(), Part.Arc(Q(0, zB), Q(RW - w * c, zB - w * c), Q(RW, zB - w)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(Q(RW, zB - w), Q(XB, zB - w)).toShape(), Part.Arc(Q(XB, zB - w), Q(XB + w * c, zB - w * c), Q(XB + w, zB)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(Q(XB + w, zB), Q(XB + w, ze)).toShape()]
        path = Part.Wire(Part.__sortEdges__(pe)); prof = Part.Wire(Part.makeCircle(RIB_G, V(0, 0, zB + 2.0), V(0, 0, -1)))
        rib = rib.cut(path.makePipeShell([prof], True, True))
    return rib
def make_windows():
    """the lightening windows: solid to cut through the deck (the deck is only 4 mm thick: vertical walls, nothing overhangs when it is printed upside down).
    Area = the inside of the wall (WIN_WEB from it) minus the keep-out zones (collar, stiffening ring band, end of the stand, rib strip, connector housings, spoke, each WIN_WEB bigger), the corners rounded with radius WIN_R."""
    a = BASE_R - 4.0 - WIN_WEB; rc = max(WIN_R, BASE_CORNER - 4.0 - WIN_WEB)
    free = Part.Face(rr_outline(-a, a, -a, a, rc, rc, 0.0))
    def disc(r, x=0.0): return Part.Face(Part.Wire(Part.makeCircle(r, V(x, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1))))
    def rect(x0, x1, y0, y1): return Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(x0, y0, 0), V(x1, y0, 0), V(x1, y1, 0), V(x0, y1, 0), V(x0, y0, 0)]))
    r_end = (key_geom()[1] + KEY_CLR if SAME_END else 15.6) + 0.3
    ko = [disc(R_COL + WIN_WEB), disc(43.0 + WIN_WEB).cut(disc(40.0 - WIN_WEB)), disc(r_end + WIN_WEB, XT),
          rect(0.0, XT + WIN_WEB, -(RIB_W / 2.0 + WIN_WEB), RIB_W / 2.0 + WIN_WEB)]
    for an in WIN_SPOKES:
        sp = rect(0.0, BASE_R + 5.0, -WIN_SPOKE / 2.0, WIN_SPOKE / 2.0); sp.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), an); ko.append(sp)
    if CONN_ON:
        t = math.tan(math.radians(CN_ANG)); hh = CN_ROOT / 2.0 + CN_CLR + CN_DS * t + CN_WALL + WIN_WEB; yb = 43.0 + WIN_WEB          # housing: half width, and the rect starts at the ring band (the housing, 11.5 mm deep + fillets, ends 3 mm outside it)
        for k in range(NC):
            if k % 2 == 0 and not CONN_X: continue
            r = rect(-hh, hh, yb, BASE_R + 5.0); r.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), k * 360.0 / NC - 90.0); ko.append(r)
    reg = free
    for z in ko: reg = reg.cut(z)
    out = []
    for f in reg.Faces:
        try: g = f.makeOffset2D(-WIN_R, 0, False, False, False).makeOffset2D(WIN_R, 0, False, False, False)
        except Exception as e: print("WARNING: window offset failed (%s), the sharp window is used" % e); g = f
        out += [q for q in g.Faces if q.Area > WIN_MIN]
    if not out: return None
    sol = [q.extrude(V(0, 0, BASE_H + 1.0 - (DU - 0.5))) for q in out]
    for q in sol: q.translate(V(0, 0, DU - 0.5))
    return fuse(*sol) if len(sol) > 1 else sol[0]
DECK_HOLE_R = STAND_HOLE_R if SAME_END else PLUG_R + 0.3                # hole of the deck for the column of the stand end (0.3 mm clearance)
import hashlib, tempfile
def _src_id():
    for _p in (globals().get("__file__"), os.path.join(App.getUserMacroDir(True), "ProbeStand_OneBoom_Combined.FCMacro")):
        try:
            if _p and os.path.isfile(_p) and "probestand" in os.path.basename(_p).lower(): return hashlib.md5(open(_p, "rb").read()).hexdigest() + repr(sorted((k, v) for k, v in _OV.items() if k not in ("M_LEN", "M_LEN_TIP")))
        except Exception: pass
    return None
_SRC_ID = _src_id(); _CACHE = os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), "ProbeStandCache")
def _cached(fn):
    """the threaded parts, the base, the tip end and the holder do not depend on the M length: keep them on disk (BREP) between runs; any trouble with the cache just builds the part again"""
    def w(*a, **k):
        if _SRC_ID is None: return fn(*a, **k)
        path = os.path.join(_CACHE, hashlib.md5((_SRC_ID + fn.__name__ + repr(a) + repr(sorted(k.items()))).encode()).hexdigest() + ".brep")
        try:
            if os.path.isfile(path):
                r = Part.read(path)
                if r.isValid() and r.Volume > 0: return r
        except Exception: pass
        r = fn(*a, **k)
        try: os.makedirs(_CACHE, exist_ok=True); r.exportBrep(path)
        except Exception: pass
        return r
    return w
@_cached
def make_stand_base():
    """Flat base, open at the bottom (built with the tensioner on +x, placed by BASE_PL), all edges rounded for printing.
    A shallow cylinder (BASE_R, BASE_H, wall 4 mm, open at the bottom): print it UPSIDE DOWN, deck on the bed (the rim of the stand cup is flush with the deck). The deck (4 mm) carries the stand cup as a conical hole
    (the ball sits 4.5 mm above the deck, its lower pole hangs below the deck), a collar under it (stiffens the deck, carries the lugs of drum A) and a round hole at XT for the column of the stand end
    (the tensioner: the tip end upside down, completely above the deck, it is a separate part). The lugs of drum B hang from the deck beside that hole.
    Wire (OPEN, nothing hides it): cup centre, straight down out of the ball (no pillar), 90 deg round DRUM A (a fixed rounded cylinder of radius RP between two lugs under the collar), along the floor, 90 deg round DRUM B
    (the same, between two lugs under the deck), straight up through the hole of the deck into the stand end. No bearings, no axles; the lugs are the side plates that keep the wire on the drums.
    Rounded for printing: the table side of the wall and of the ring (r 1), the underside of the collar (r 1), the lugs (r 1 / r 1.5), 45 deg chamfers (0.8 mm) on the edges on the bed (the outer edge of the deck),
    a 45 deg lead-in round the cup and round the hole of the end."""
    cz = MAST_TOP
    _c, zbs, rtop = seat(RB, (0, 0, cz))                                                  # seat cone of the cup (apex plane zbs, radius rb = 2 there)
    zs0 = ZCOL0 - 0.5; rs0 = 2.0 + (zs0 - zbs) * T30                                       # the seat is cut from zs0 up: below that nothing of the cone is needed (the ball leaves it at the contact ring 60 deg off the axis)
    seat_cut = Part.makeCone(rs0, rtop, cz - zs0, V(0, 0, zs0), V(0, 0, 1))
    shell = Part.Face(base_outline(0.0)).extrude(V(0, 0, BASE_H)).cut(Part.Face(base_outline(4.0)).extrude(V(0, 0, DU)))     # wall + deck, square with rounded corners
    shell = _fil(shell, R_FREE, _at_z(shell, 0.0), "table edge of the wall")
    shell = _fil(shell, 1.5, _at_z(shell, DU), "inner corner wall / deck")
    shell = _chf(shell, CH_BED, _at_z(shell, BASE_H), "bed edge of the deck")
    parts = [shell]
    ring = cyl(43.0, DU + 0.5).cut(cyl(40.0, DU + 2.0, (0, 0, -1.0)))                                          # stiffening ring (r 40-43): the deck rests on the table here, it takes the overturning moment of the arm
    ring = _fil(ring, 0.8, _circ(ring, 43.0, 0.0) + _circ(ring, 40.0, 0.0), "table edge of the ring")
    notch = Part.Face(rr_outline(XT - 8.0, XT + 3.0, -7.5, 7.5, 2.0, 2.0, -1.0)).extrude(V(0, 0, DU + 2.0))            # the ring is interrupted where the wire and the lugs of drum B cross it (rounded)
    parts.append(ring.cut(notch))
    col = cyl(R_COL, DU - ZCOL0, (0, 0, ZCOL0))                                                                # collar under the deck round the cup
    parts.append(_fil(col, R_FREE, _circ(col, R_COL, ZCOL0), "underside of the collar"))
    if RIB: parts.append(make_rib())
    else:
        cA = (RW - RP) - zB                                                                                                # the 45 deg line x - z = cA runs through the point where the wire leaves drum A (left point of the drum)
        if DRUM_FLANK: qa = [(RW - 5.0, zB - 3.5), (RW + 5.0, zB - 3.5), (RW + 10.25, zB + 1.7), (RW + 10.25, DU), (cA + DU, DU), (RW - 5.0, RW - 5.0 - cA)]
        else: qa = [(RW - 5.0, zB - 3.5), (RW + 5.0, zB - 3.5), (RW + 10.25, zB + 1.7), (RW + 10.25, DU), (RW + 4.5, DU), (RW - 5.0, zB - 1.2)]     # lug of drum A (x, z): hangs from the collar beside the ball, the pull of the wire (up + towards B) runs along its diagonal; the edge towards the ball is 45 deg (printed upside down: no support)
        for y0 in (2.6, -5.6):                                                                                              # lugs: 3 mm plates either side of the wire (5.2 mm between them)
            qb = [(XB - 5.0, zB - 3.5), (XB + 5.0, zB - 3.5), (XB + 5.0, zB + 1.7), (XB + 5.0 - (DU + 0.5 - (zB + 1.7)), DU + 0.5), (XB - 5.0, DU + 0.5)]            # lug of drum B (x, z): hangs from the deck beside the hole, the pull of the wire (up and towards A) runs along its diagonal; the edge towards the hole is 45 deg (printed upside down: no support)
            pb = [V(x, y0, z) for x, z in qb]; pb.append(pb[0])
            lb = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(pb)).extrude(V(0, 3.0, 0))
            parts.append(_fil(lb, 1.0, [e for e in lb.Edges if abs(e.BoundBox.YLength - 3.0) < 1e-6 and e.BoundBox.ZMax < DU - 0.01], "edges of lug B"))
            # (lug A follows)
            pts = [V(x, y0, z) for x, z in qa]; pts.append(pts[0])
            la = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(pts)).extrude(V(0, 3.0, 0))
            parts.append(_fil(la, 1.0, [e for e in la.Edges if abs(e.BoundBox.YLength - 3.0) < 1e-6 and e.BoundBox.ZMax < DU - 0.01], "edges of lug A"))
        iDA = len(parts)
        for xc in (RW, XB): parts.append(cyl(RP, 6.2, (xc, -3.1, zB), (0, 1, 0)))                                         # the two fixed round drums the wire runs round (axis along y, 0.5 mm into each lug plate: one solid with the lugs)
        # no bridges when printed upside down: the wire only touches the lower quarter of each drum, so the upper half is filled in with 45 deg flanks (a horizontal cylinder would be a 5.2 mm bridge with a drooping underside)
        c45 = math.sqrt(0.5); tx = RP * c45; tz = RP * c45
        def _prism(pts): return Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(x, -3.1, z) for x, z in pts] + [V(pts[0][0], -3.1, pts[0][1])])).extrude(V(0, 6.2, 0))
        zt = zB + tz + 0.01; bc = (0.0, MAST_TOP)                                                                                 # drum A: teardrop (flanks tangent at 45 and 135 deg), cut off flat below the ball: raise the top while the corner stays DRUM_BALL_CLR clear of the ball
        while True:
            xl = RW - tx + (zt + 0.05 - (zB + tz))
            if math.hypot(xl - bc[0], zt + 0.05 - bc[1]) < RB + DRUM_BALL_CLR or zt + 0.05 > zB + RP * math.sqrt(2.0): break
            zt += 0.05
        xl = RW - tx + (zt - (zB + tz)); xr = RW + tx - (zt - (zB + tz))
        if DRUM_FLANK:                                                                                                          # drum A: circle cut by the 45 deg line through the wire's leaving point + a triangle up to the right flank (45 deg, tangent at 45 deg); the seat cone trims the apex
            S = RW + tx + zB + tz; ax, az = (S + cA) / 2.0, (S - cA) / 2.0
            capx = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(cA + zB - 6.0, -3.2, zB - 6.0), V(cA + zB + 9.0, -3.2, zB + 9.0), V(cA + zB - 6.0, -3.2, zB + 9.0), V(cA + zB - 6.0, -3.2, zB - 6.0)])).extrude(V(0, 6.4, 0))
            parts[iDA] = parts[iDA].cut(capx)
            parts.append(_prism([(RW, zB), (RW - RP, zB), (ax, az), (RW + tx, zB + tz)]))
        else: parts.append(_prism([(RW, zB), (RW - tx, zB + tz), (xl, zt), (xr, zt), (RW + tx, zB + tz)]))
        parts.append(_prism([(XB - RP, zB), (XB + tx, zB + tz), (XB + tx - (DU + 0.5 - (zB + tz)), DU + 0.5), (XB - RP, DU + 0.5)]))      # drum B: web up to the deck (flank tangent at 45 deg, it stays 1.6 mm clear of the hole of the deck; the wire leaves the drum on the other side)
    if CONN_ON: _cn_add, _cn_cut = make_connectors(); parts += _cn_add                                                   # tongues and socket housings
    base = fuse(*parts)
    base = base.cut(seat_cut)
    if CONN_ON: base = cut_sockets(base, _cn_cut)                                                                        # slots of the sockets
    if SAME_END: base = base.cut(key_slots())
    if WIN_ON:
        _w = make_windows()
        if _w is not None: base = base.cut(_w)                                                                           # lightening windows through the deck
    base = base.cut(cyl(DECK_HOLE_R, BASE_H + 1.0 - DU, (XT, 0, DU)))                                                    # round hole of the deck under the stand end: the wire comes up through it, the column of the end drops into it
    base = base.cut(Part.makeCone(DECK_HOLE_R, DECK_HOLE_R + 0.5, 0.5, V(XT, 0, BASE_H - 0.5), V(0, 0, 1)))               # 45 deg lead-in (it is on the bed)
    ra = rtop - (cz - (BASE_H - 0.4)) * T30                                                                         # 45 deg lead-in (countersink) at the rim of the cup: starts on the 30 deg seat cone 0.4 mm below the deck, so no face is flatter than 45 deg
    base = base.cut(Part.makeCone(ra, ra + 0.5, 0.5, V(0, 0, BASE_H - 0.4), V(0, 0, 1)))
    return base.removeSplitter()
def slider_block(ch):
    """block 24 x 18 x 16 of a slider (front face x = 17, rear face x = 41). ch = 0: plain block (stand slider).
    ch > 0 (tip slider, printed standing on its front face without supports): the four long edges rounded r 4, the front edges chamfered at 45 deg (ch on the two long sides = clearance of the vault of the tip end,
    1 mm on the two short sides), the rear edges chamfered 1 mm"""
    sl = box(17, 41, -9, 9, -8, 8)
    if ch <= 0: return sl
    sl = sl.makeFillet(4.0, [e for e in sl.Edges if abs(e.BoundBox.XLength - 24.0) < 1e-6])
    r1 = Part.makePolygon([V(17, -(9 - ch), -7), V(17, 9 - ch, -7), V(17, 9 - ch, 7), V(17, -(9 - ch), 7), V(17, -(9 - ch), -7)])
    r2 = Part.makePolygon([V(17 + ch, -9, -(7 + ch)), V(17 + ch, 9, -(7 + ch)), V(17 + ch, 9, 7 + ch), V(17 + ch, -9, 7 + ch), V(17 + ch, -9, -(7 + ch))])
    sl = sl.common(Part.makeLoft([r1, r2], True, True).fuse(box(17 + ch, 42, -9.5, 9.5, -8.5, 8.5)))
    return sl.makeChamfer(1.0, [e for e in sl.Edges if abs(e.BoundBox.XMin - 41) < 1e-3 and abs(e.BoundBox.XMax - 41) < 1e-3])
def rr_outline(x0, x1, y0, y1, rb, rf, z=0.0):
    """closed wire of a rectangle x0..x1, y0..y1 at height z, the two corners at x0 rounded with rb, the two at x1 with rf"""
    c = lambda a, b: V(a, b, z)
    def arc(cx, cy, r, a0, a1):
        pt = lambda a: c(cx + r * math.cos(math.radians(a)), cy + r * math.sin(math.radians(a)))
        return Part.Arc(pt(a0), pt((a0 + a1) / 2.0), pt(a1)).toShape()
    ln = lambda p, q: Part.LineSegment(p, q).toShape()
    e = [ln(c(x0 + rb, y0), c(x1 - rf, y0)), arc(x1 - rf, y0 + rf, rf, -90, 0), ln(c(x1, y0 + rf), c(x1, y1 - rf)), arc(x1 - rf, y1 - rf, rf, 0, 90),
         ln(c(x1 - rf, y1), c(x0 + rb, y1)), arc(x0 + rb, y1 - rb, rb, 90, 180), ln(c(x0, y1 - rb), c(x0, y0 + rb)), arc(x0 + rb, y0 + rb, rb, 180, 270)]
    return Part.Wire(Part.__sortEdges__(e))
def te_windows(zb, ze, zfl, tail=True):
    """open windows of the end piece (tool solid). Tail: N hexagonal windows (vertical sides, 45 deg roof and sill) one above the other through both side walls (axis y) and through the back wall (axis x),
    between 3 mm above the floor of the trough (zfl) and 3 mm below its eaves (ze); the corner columns and the struts between the windows carry the load. Cup block: windows through its outer wall into the
    cavity (radial, flat sill at the cavity floor, 45 deg roof), at the angles TE_WIN_ANG; the ears and the column behind them stay."""
    za = zfl + 3.0; zb2 = ze - 3.0; a = TE_WIN_A; n = 2; hh = ((zb2 - za) - (n - 1) * TE_WIN_S) / n          # height of one hexagon
    hv = hh - 2.0 * a; tools = []
    def hexpts(u0, zc):
        return [(u0 - a, zc - hv / 2.0), (u0 - a, zc + hv / 2.0), (u0, zc + hv / 2.0 + a), (u0 + a, zc + hv / 2.0), (u0 + a, zc - hv / 2.0), (u0, zc - hv / 2.0 - a), (u0 - a, zc - hv / 2.0)]
    for i in (range(n) if tail else ()):
        zc = za + hh / 2.0 + i * (hh + TE_WIN_S)
        p = hexpts(-1.0, zc); tools.append(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(u, -20.0, z) for u, z in p])).extrude(V(0, 40.0, 0)))                         # both side walls
        p = hexpts(0.0, zc); tools.append(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(-20.0, u, z) for u, z in p])).extrude(V(11.5, 0, 0)))                         # back wall (stops at the trough)
    rs = 2.0 + (-ZG - zb) * T30 + 3.0 - TE_VOID_W; zf0 = zb - 0.5; b = TE_WIN_B; zt = zf0 + 2.0 * b + 1.0                                               # window of the cup block: width 2b, flat sill at the cavity floor, 45 deg roof
    if TE_VOID:
        for ang in TE_WIN_ANG:
            w = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(rs - 0.6, -b, zf0), V(rs - 0.6, b, zf0), V(rs - 0.6, b, zf0 + 1.0 + b), V(rs - 0.6, 0, zt), V(rs - 0.6, -b, zf0 + 1.0 + b), V(rs - 0.6, -b, zf0)])).extrude(V(6.0, 0, 0))
            w.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), ang); tools.append(w)
    return fuse(*tools)
@_cached
def make_te_tip(plug=0.0):
    """STRAIGHT test end for the tip: cup on top (cup centre = origin, opens up), the wire runs straight down the axis (no elbow, no liner),
    below the cup the same tail as the stand end (trough for the slider, end wall with the screw hole), shifted down by TD, trough opening towards +x.
    Made to be printed standing on its end wall, cup up, WITHOUT supports: rounded outline (the corners at the closed back r 6, at the open front r 3), 45 deg chamfer on the bed edge,
    rounded outer rim of the cup, a cone (38.7 deg from vertical) that carries the cup block down into the tail instead of a flat ledge, and a 45 deg vault on top of the trough:
    its flat top is only 9.4 mm wide (the old flat roof spanned 20 mm). The slider clears the vault with its corners chamfered by TIP_CH (45 deg, 0.5 mm clearance at the stop, 1 mm in front of the position drawn)."""
    zb = -seat_depth(RB); rrim = 2.0 + (-ZG - zb) * T30; rho = rrim + 3.0
    z0 = zb - 2.0; zbot = -(TD + TE_WALL); zr = -(TD + XF)             # underside of the cup block, bed plane, roof plane of the old flat trough (= front face of the slider at its stop)
    tail = Part.Face(rr_outline(-RS, 10.0, -13.0, 13.0, 6.0, 3.0, zbot)).extrude(V(0, 0, (zb - 1.5) - zbot))
    tail = tail.makeChamfer(1.0, [e for e in tail.Edges if abs(e.BoundBox.ZMin - zbot) < 1e-6 and abs(e.BoundBox.ZMax - zbot) < 1e-6])
    blk = cyl(rho, -ZG - z0, (0, 0, z0))
    blk = blk.makeFillet(1.2, [e for e in blk.Edges if e.Curve.__class__.__name__ == "Circle" and abs(e.Curve.Center.z + ZG) < 1e-6])         # rounded outer edge of the rim
    slope = 0.8; hs = (rho - 5.0) / slope                                                                                                  # radius shrinks 0.8 mm per mm of height: 38.7 deg from vertical
    skirt = Part.makeCone(rho - slope * hs, rho, hs, V(0, 0, z0 - hs), V(0, 0, 1))
    te = fuse(blk, skirt, tail)
    te = te.cut(seat(RB, (0, 0, 0))[0])
    if TE_VOID:                                                                                                                            # closed cavity round the seat: floor flat (faces up), roof = the seat cone offset by TE_VOID_W (30 deg from vertical), outer wall vertical
        ra = 2.0 + TE_VOID_W / math.cos(math.radians(30.0)); rc = rho - TE_VOID_W; zf = zb - 0.5; zk = zb + (rc - ra) / T30
        vp = [V(ra, 0, zf), V(rc, 0, zf), V(rc, 0, zk), V(ra, 0, zb), V(ra, 0, zf)]
        te = te.cut(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(vp)).revolve(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360))
    if SAME_END: te = te.fuse(end_keys())                                                                                                   # keys on the rim of the cup (the stand end drops them into the slots of the deck; harmless at the tip)
    if plug > 0:                                                                                                                           # STAND end (standing upside down on the deck, its cup is empty): a round column fills the inner part of the cup and sticks out of the rim plane by `plug`
        pt = -ZG + plug; pg = cyl(PLUG_R, pt - zb, (0, 0, zb)); pg = _chf(pg, 0.6, _at_z(pg, pt), "top of the column")
        te = te.fuse(pg)
    ze = zr - 0.3 - TIP_CH; zt = -26.0; w = 10.0 - (zt - ze)                                                                              # vault: 45 deg flanks from the eaves (y = +-10, z = ze) up to the flat top (z = zt, y = +-w)
    zf = -(TD + TE_WALL - 4)                                                                                                               # floor of the trough
    prof = [V(-9, -10, zf), V(-9, 10, zf), V(-9, 10, ze), V(-9, w, zt), V(-9, -w, zt), V(-9, -10, ze), V(-9, -10, zf)]
    te = te.cut(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(prof)).extrude(V(29, 0, 0)))                                                                    # trough for the slider (open on the +x side)
    te = te.cut(cyl(HOLE_R, (zb + HOLE_UP) - (zt - 1.0), (0, 0, zb + HOLE_UP), (0, 0, -1)))                                               # wire path: cup apex straight down into the trough
    if plug > 0: te = te.cut(cyl(PLUG_BORE, (-ZG + plug) - zb + 1.0, (0, 0, zb)))                                                          # bore of the column for the wire
    te = te.cut(cyl(THREAD_D / 2 + 0.6, 8, (0, 0, -(TD + TE_WALL - 5)), (0, 0, -1)))                                                       # screw hole through the end wall
    if TE_WIN: te = te.cut(te_windows(zb, ze, zf))
    return te
def ph_dims():
    """dimensions of the probe holder (local frame of the tip end: cup centre = origin, axis down): seat depth, rim radius rho, bottom of the cup block z0, foot of the skirt, bed plane, ceiling of the ferrule pocket"""
    zb = -seat_depth(RB); rho = 2.0 + (-ZG - zb) * T30 + 3.0; z0 = zb - 2.0; zsk = z0 - (rho - 6.0) / 0.8; zbot = zsk - 7.0
    return zb, rho, z0, zsk, zbot, zbot + 5.5
def tear_y(x, z, r, y0, y1):
    """horizontal hole along y (from y0 to y1) at (x, z), radius r, with a 45 deg pointed roof (no bridge)"""
    c = math.sqrt(0.5) * r
    h = cyl(r, y1 - y0, (x, y0, z), (0, 1, 0))
    roof = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(x - c, y0, z + c), V(x, y0, z + r * math.sqrt(2.0)), V(x + c, y0, z + c), V(x, y0, z), V(x - c, y0, z + c)])).extrude(V(0, y1 - y0, 0))
    return h.fuse(roof)
def ph_screw_pos():
    """axis of the clamp screw (along y): x, z of the axis and y of the outer face of the tabs"""
    zbot = ph_dims()[4]; ro = PROBE_D / 2.0 + PROBE_CLR + PH_WALL
    return PH_OFF + ro + 3.0, zbot + PH_H / 2.0, PH_GAP / 2.0 + PH_TAB
@_cached
def make_clamp_screw():
    """printed clamp screw in the local frame of the holder: fluted knob outside the -y tab, threaded stub along +y through the tab and the gap into the socket of the +y tab"""
    xs, zs, yo = ph_screw_pos()
    st = make_stub_gen(PH_THREAD_D / 2.0, PH_THREAD_P, PH_THREAD_DEPTH, PH_SCREW_L + 0.5, THREAD_CH, 0.0).copy()
    st.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0), -90.0); st.translate(V(xs, -yo - 0.5, zs))                                                            # shoulder 0.5 mm inside the knob
    return clean(st.fuse(fluted(PH_KNOB_R, 5.0, (xs, -yo - 5.0, zs), (0, 1, 0), 10, 1.5)))
@_cached
def make_probe_holder(thread=True):
    """SCOPE PROBE HOLDER (replaces the tip tensioner). Local frame of the tip end: cup centre = origin, cup opens up, the wire runs down the axis. It is printed STANDING on its bed face (z = zbot), cup up, without supports:
    the cup block with its skirt and cavity as the end piece, a neck with a ferrule pocket open to the bed (the crimped end of the wire sits in it and pulls up: the tension is carried by the cup), a flat arm on the bed
    to a clamp ring beside the wire axis (PH_OFF) whose bore (vertical, PROBE_D + 2 * PROBE_CLR) holds the probe body. The ring is a C open towards +x (snap-in from the side) with two tabs and an M3 screw across them
    (a clearance hole in the -y tab, a printed THREADED HOLE in the +y tab for the plastic clamp screw, make_clamp_screw): the screw closes the C and clamps the probe."""
    zb, rho, z0, zsk, zbot, zc = ph_dims()
    blk = cyl(rho, -ZG - z0, (0, 0, z0))
    blk = blk.makeFillet(1.2, [e for e in blk.Edges if e.Curve.__class__.__name__ == "Circle" and abs(e.Curve.Center.z + ZG) < 1e-6])
    skirt = Part.makeCone(6.0, rho, z0 - zsk, V(0, 0, zsk), V(0, 0, 1)); neck = cyl(6.0, zsk - zbot + 0.01, (0, 0, zbot))
    ro = PROBE_D / 2.0 + PROBE_CLR + PH_WALL; rbo = PROBE_D / 2.0 + PROBE_CLR; g = PH_GAP / 2.0; tl = ro + 9.5
    arm = box(0.0, PH_OFF, -6.0, 6.0, zbot, zbot + PH_ARM); ring = cyl(ro, PH_H, (PH_OFF, 0, zbot))
    tabs = [box(PH_OFF + 2.0, PH_OFF + tl, a, b, zbot, zbot + PH_H) for a, b in ((g, g + PH_TAB), (-g - PH_TAB, -g))]
    h = fuse(blk, skirt, neck, arm, ring, *tabs)
    h = h.cut(seat(RB, (0, 0, 0))[0])
    if TE_VOID:
        ra = 2.0 + TE_VOID_W / math.cos(math.radians(30.0)); rc = rho - TE_VOID_W; zf = zb - 0.5; zk = zb + (rc - ra) / T30
        h = h.cut(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(ra, 0, zf), V(rc, 0, zf), V(rc, 0, zk), V(ra, 0, zb), V(ra, 0, zf)])).revolve(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360))
        if TE_WIN: h = h.cut(te_windows(zb, 0.0, 0.0, tail=False))
    h = h.cut(cyl(HOLE_R, (zb + HOLE_UP) - (zbot - 1.0), (0, 0, zb + HOLE_UP), (0, 0, -1)))                                            # wire path down the axis
    h = h.cut(cyl(POCK_R, zc - zbot + 1.0, (0, 0, zbot - 1.0))).cut(Part.makeCone(POCK_R + 0.6, POCK_R, 0.6, V(0, 0, zbot), V(0, 0, 1)))   # ferrule pocket, open to the bed, 45 deg lead-in
    h = h.cut(cyl(rbo, PH_H + 2.0, (PH_OFF, 0, zbot - 1.0))).cut(box(PH_OFF, PH_OFF + tl + 2.0, -g, g, zbot - 1.0, zbot + PH_H + 1.0))      # bore and the opening of the C
    xs, zs, yo = ph_screw_pos(); rm = PH_THREAD_D / 2.0
    h = h.cut(tear_y(xs, zs, rm + 0.4, -yo - 1.0, -g + 0.5))                                                                               # clearance hole for the screw through the -y tab
    if thread:
        tool = make_socket_tool(rm, PH_THREAD_P, PH_THREAD_DEPTH, PH_SOCK, THREAD_CL, PH_SOCK + SOCKET_EXTRA, THREAD_CH).copy()                   # printed thread in the +y tab: mouth on its inner face, going outwards
        tool.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0), -90.0); tool.translate(V(xs, g, zs)); h = h.cut(tool)
    return h.removeSplitter()
def probe_ref():
    """stand-in of the probe (collision tests, picture): body of PROBE_D with a tapered tip, its axis at PH_OFF beside the wire axis, the tip PROBE_OUT below the bed face of the holder"""
    zb, rho, z0, zsk, zbot, zc = ph_dims(); z1 = zbot - PROBE_OUT
    return fuse(Part.makeCone(1.0, PROBE_D / 2.0, 20.0, V(PH_OFF, 0, z1), V(0, 0, 1)), cyl(PROBE_D / 2.0, PROBE_LEN - 20.0, (PH_OFF, 0, z1 + 20.0)))
@_cached
def make_slider(side_slot=False, plain=False, ch=0.0):
    """block 24 x 18 x 16: wire hole + ferrule pocket at the front, printed internal thread behind it (mouth on the +x face).
    side_slot: wire slot (width of the hole, 45 deg lead-in) through the front wall and ferrule slot (width of the pocket) behind it, up to the thread bore, opened to
      +1 = the +z face (the face that looks out of the open side of the trough: visible, the ferrule pocket can be reached from there),
      -1 = the -z face (the face that leads when the slider is dropped into the trough from its open side, against the closed back: the wire and a ferrule crimped on it beforehand are laid in from the side),
       0 = closed hole.
    plain: tests only (plain bore instead of the thread)
    ch: 0 = plain block, > 0 = rounded and chamfered block of the tip slider (see slider_block; it clears the vault of the tip end)"""
    sg = 1 if side_slot > 0 else -1
    wh = SL_WH_R if side_slot else WH_R
    sl = slider_block(ch).cut(cyl(wh, 2.5, (16.5, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0))).cut(cyl(POCK_R, 5, (18.5, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
    if side_slot:
        _z0, _z1 = (0.0, 8.5) if sg > 0 else (-8.5, 0.0)
        sl = sl.cut(box(16.5, 18.5, -wh, wh, _z0, _z1))
        _f = [V(18.5, -POCK_R, _z0), V(23.5, -POCK_R, _z0), V(23.5 + POCK_R, 0, _z0), V(23.5, POCK_R, _z0), V(18.5, POCK_R, _z0), V(18.5, -POCK_R, _z0)]      # ferrule slot with a pointed (45 deg) top: no flat ceiling when printed standing on the front face
        sl = sl.cut(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(_f)).extrude(V(0, 0, _z1 - _z0)))
        _v = [V(16.5, -wh, 5.5 * sg), V(16.5, wh, 5.5 * sg), V(16.5, wh + 2.8, 8.3 * sg), V(16.5, -wh - 2.8, 8.3 * sg), V(16.5, -wh, 5.5 * sg)]
        sl = sl.cut(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(_v)).extrude(V(2.0, 0, 0)))
    if plain: return sl.cut(cyl(THREAD_D / 2.0 - THREAD_DEPTH + THREAD_CL, 17.5, (23.5, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
    tool = make_socket_tool(THREAD_D / 2.0, THREAD_P, THREAD_DEPTH, 17.0, THREAD_CL, 17.0 + SOCKET_EXTRA, THREAD_CH).copy()
    tool.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), SCR_PHASE)                                    # the groove meets the thread of the screw (phase of the drawn position)
    tool.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 1, 0), -90.0); tool.translate(V(41, 0, 0))           # +Z -> -X, mouth at x = 41, bottom at x = 23.5
    return clean(sl.cut(tool))
@_cached
def make_screw():
    """tension screw: knob (fluted, 12 mm) just outside the end wall, thread stub running back through the wall to x = SCR_END (free end with lead-in chamfer)"""
    st = make_stub_gen(THREAD_D / 2.0, THREAD_P, THREAD_DEPTH, TE_WALL + 0.7 - SCR_END, THREAD_CH, 0.0).copy()
    st.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 1, 0), -90.0); st.translate(V(TE_WALL + 0.7, 0, 0))   # shoulder 0.5 mm inside the knob
    kn = st.fuse(fluted(11, 12, (TE_WALL + 0.2, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0), 12, 2.2))
    if KNOB_DISH > 0: kn = kn.cut(Part.makeCone(KNOB_DISH + 0.1, 0.0, KNOB_DISH + 0.1, V(TE_WALL + 12.3, 0, 0), V(-1, 0, 0)))                    # dish in the outer face of the knob (45 deg: no bridge when the knob stands on the bed)
    return clean(kn)
BASE_SHAPE = make_stand_base(); TE_TIP = make_te_tip(); PH_ZBOT, PH_ZCEIL = ph_dims()[4], ph_dims()[5]; TIP_HOLDER = make_probe_holder() if TIP_PROBE else None; CLAMP_SCREW = make_clamp_screw() if TIP_PROBE else None; CLAMP_PRINT = None; PROBE_REF = probe_ref() if TIP_PROBE else None; FER_P = cyl(FER_R, 5, (0, 0, PH_ZCEIL - 5.0)) if TIP_PROBE else None; TE_STAND = TE_TIP if SAME_END else make_te_tip(PLUG_OUT); SCREW = make_screw()
if TIP_PROBE: XP, YP, ZTIP = tp(HEADPL.multVec(V(PH_OFF, 0, HZT + PH_ZBOT - 10.0)))      # load point of the margins: on the probe, 10 mm below the clamp
TIP_SLIDER = make_slider(TIP_SLOT, ch=TIP_CH)
FERRULE = cyl(FER_R, 5, (18.5, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0))
def _upright(shp, ang):                                          # print orientation: thread axis vertical (x -> +z for ang = -90, x -> -z for ang = +90)
    c = shp.copy(); c.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 1, 0), ang); return c
TIP_SLIDER_PRINT = _upright(TIP_SLIDER, -90); SCREW_PRINT = _upright(SCREW, 90)
# simple stand-ins for the two threaded parts in the collision tests (boolean operations on helical faces are slow and once crashed FreeCAD)
_SL_HULL_TIP = slider_block(TIP_CH)
_SC_HULL = fuse(cyl(THREAD_D / 2.0, TE_WALL + 0.7 - SCR_END, (SCR_END, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)), cyl(11, 12, (TE_WALL + 0.2, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
PROXY = {"Stand_Slider": _SL_HULL_TIP, "Tip_Slider": _SL_HULL_TIP, "Stand_Screw": _SC_HULL, "Tip_Screw": _SC_HULL}
if TIP_PROBE: PROXY["Tip_Holder"] = make_probe_holder(thread=False)      # the holder without the helical socket of the clamp screw
def show_neighbours(dirs=(0,)):
    """add copies of the base joined to this one at the sides dirs (0 = +x, 1 = +y, 2 = -x, 3 = -y; e.g. (0, 1, 3)); each is a plain Part object 'Neighbour_k' placed exactly where it clicks in
    (distance conn_pitch() = 130.2 mm at full size). For looking at the grid only: no collision tests."""
    for k in dirs:
        a = math.radians(k * 90.0); d = conn_pitch(k) * KS
        o = doc.addObject("Part::Feature", "Neighbour_%d" % k); o.Shape = BASE_SHAPE
        o.Placement = BASE_PL.multiply(App.Placement(V(d * math.cos(a), d * math.sin(a), 0), App.Rotation()))
        if App.GuiUp: o.ViewObject.ShapeColor = (0.62, 0.70, 0.78)
    doc.recompute()
def _located(n):
    if n not in PROXY: return OBJ[n].Shape
    sh = PROXY[n].copy(); sh.Placement = OBJ[n].Placement; return sh
BASE_OBJ = ["Stand_Base", "Stand_TE", "Stand_Slider", "Stand_Screw", "Stand_Ferrule"]
HEAD_OBJ = ["Tip_Holder", "Tip_Probe", "Tip_Clamp_Screw", "Tip_Ferrule"] if TIP_PROBE else ["Tip_TE", "Tip_Slider", "Tip_Screw", "Tip_Ferrule"]                   
COLL_BASE = ["Stand_Base", "Stand_TE", "Stand_Slider", "Stand_Screw"]; COLL_HEAD = ["Tip_Holder", "Tip_Probe"] if TIP_PROBE else ["Tip_TE", "Tip_Slider", "Tip_Screw"]       # parts that take part in the collision tests

# ============================== LINKS (ball - rod - ball) AND LOOSE BALLS ==============================
def ring_stop(R, c, dirn):
    """raised ring (collar) on the neck side of a link ball = mechanical STOP for the tilt. Seen from the neck axis the plane of the cup's top face (ZG below the ball centre,
    on the cup side) is the cone  z = (rho * sin(a) - ZG) / cos(a)  when the joint is tilted a = RING_LIMIT + RING_PLAY. That cone is the underside of the ring, so the top face of the
    cup comes to rest FLAT against it at a, in every tilt direction, and stays clear below a. Profile (rho, z): underside cone, vertical outer wall RING_WALL, flat top (perpendicular
    to the neck axis). dirn = +1: neck points up (+z), -1: down."""
    a = math.radians(RING_LIMIT + RING_PLAY); s, k = math.sin(a), math.cos(a)
    m, q = s / k, ZG / k
    zf = lambda r: m * r - q
    rs = (2 * m * q + math.sqrt(4 * m * m * q * q - 4 * (1 + m * m) * (q * q - R * R))) / (2 * (1 + m * m))        # underside cone leaves the sphere here
    rc = rs + RING_H; z2 = zf(rc); z3 = z2 + RING_WALL
    ri = min(0.88 * R, math.sqrt(max(0.0, 0.9 * R * R - z3 * z3)))                  # inner edge of the profile: inside the ball, so the ring fuses with it
    pts = [V(ri, 0, zf(ri)), V(rc, 0, z2), V(rc, 0, z3), V(ri, 0, z3)]
    sol = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon(pts + [pts[0]])).revolve(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360)
    if dirn < 0: sol.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0), 180)
    sol.translate(V(*c))
    return sol
def ring_top(R):
    """outer radius rc and height z3 (above the ball centre, neck side) of the top face of the stop ring of ring_stop(R, ...): where the rounded spindle of the M links starts"""
    a = math.radians(RING_LIMIT + RING_PLAY); s, k = math.sin(a), math.cos(a); m, q = s / k, ZG / k
    rs = (2 * m * q + math.sqrt(4 * m * m * q * q - 4 * (1 + m * m) * (q * q - R * R))) / (2 * (1 + m * m)); rc = rs + RING_H
    return rc, (m * rc - q) + RING_WALL
def make_link(Rlo, Rhi, c, D):
    """lower ball (flare down) + rod + upper ball (flare up); the wire runs through the axis"""
    top = (c[0], c[1], c[2] + D)
    lo = Part.makeSphere(Rlo, V(*c)).cut(cone_cut(Rlo, c, -1))
    hi = Part.makeSphere(Rhi, V(*top)).cut(cone_cut(Rhi, top, +1))
    rnd = M_ROUND and RING_ON and abs(Rlo - Rhi) < 1e-6 and BALL_BORE > HOLE_R + 1.5 and HOLE_R < 4 and D > 20
    if rnd:                                                                   # spindle = arc through the outer top edge of the ring on the lower ball, (M_WAIST, middle) and the outer top edge of the ring on the upper ball
        rc, z3 = ring_top(Rlo); zm = D / 2.0; hl = zm - z3; dd = rc - M_WAIST
        Ra = (hl * hl + dd * dd) / (2.0 * dd); cx = M_WAIST + Ra                     # outer arc: circle of radius Ra, centre at radius cx
        A = lambda r, z: V(c[0] + r, c[1], c[2] + z)
        ed = [Part.LineSegment(A(0, z3), A(rc, z3)).toShape(), Part.Arc(A(rc, z3), A(M_WAIST, zm), A(rc, D - z3)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(A(rc, D - z3), A(0, D - z3)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(A(0, D - z3), A(0, z3)).toShape()]
        m = fuse(lo, hi, Part.Face(Part.Wire(Part.__sortEdges__(ed))).revolve(V(c[0], c[1], 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360))
    else:
        m = fuse(lo, hi, cyl(R_NECK, D, c))
    m = m.cut(cyl(HOLE_R, D, c))
    z0 = c[2] + Rlo + 3; z1 = top[2] - Rhi - 3
    if rnd:                                                                   # one smooth inner void: bore through both balls (vertical), 45 deg cone out to M_CAVE, then the inner surface follows the spindle at the distance M_WALL (concentric arc)
        bb = min(BALL_BORE, 13.0 * math.sin(math.radians(FLARE_EDGE))); rv = max(bb + 1.0, min(M_CAVE, Rlo - 3.0)); Ri = Ra + M_WALL; zc = zm - math.sqrt(Ri * Ri - (cx - rv) ** 2); zk = rv - bb
        B = lambda r, z: V(c[0] + r, c[1], c[2] + z)
        ed = [Part.LineSegment(B(0, -Rlo - 1), B(bb, -Rlo - 1)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(B(bb, -Rlo - 1), B(bb, 0)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(B(bb, 0), B(rv, zk)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(B(rv, zk), B(rv, zc)).toShape(),
              Part.Arc(B(rv, zc), B(M_WAIST - M_WALL, zm), B(rv, D - zc)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(B(rv, D - zc), B(rv, D - zk)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(B(rv, D - zk), B(bb, D)).toShape(),
              Part.LineSegment(B(bb, D), B(bb, D + Rhi + 1)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(B(bb, D + Rhi + 1), B(0, D + Rhi + 1)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(B(0, D + Rhi + 1), B(0, -Rlo - 1)).toShape()]
        m = m.cut(Part.Face(Part.Wire(Part.__sortEdges__(ed))).revolve(V(c[0], c[1], 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360))
    elif z1 - z0 > 12 and HOLE_R < 4: m = m.cut(cyl(4, z1 - z0, (c[0], c[1], z0)))        # hollow rod, wire runs free inside
    if BALL_BORE > HOLE_R + 1.5 and HOLE_R < 4 and D > 20 and not rnd:                  # one inner void: bore of radius BALL_BORE through both balls (vertical walls), 45 deg cones down to the 4 mm bore of the rod
        bb, rt = min(BALL_BORE, 13.0 * math.sin(math.radians(FLARE_EDGE))), min(ROD_BORE, R_NECK - 1.6); zl = min(8.0, Rlo - 5.0); zh = min(8.0, Rhi - 5.0); a0, a1 = c[2] + zl, top[2] - zh
        pts = [(0, c[2] - Rlo - 1), (bb, c[2] - Rlo - 1), (bb, a0), (rt, a0 + bb - rt), (rt, a1 - bb + rt), (bb, a1), (bb, top[2] + Rhi + 1), (0, top[2] + Rhi + 1)]
        void = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(c[0] + r, c[1], z) for r, z in pts] + [V(c[0], c[1], c[2] - Rlo - 1)])).revolve(V(c[0], c[1], 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360)
        m = m.cut(void)
    if RING_ON: m = fuse(m, ring_stop(Rlo, c, +1), ring_stop(Rhi, top, -1))      # stop rings
    return m
def loose_ball(R, c):
    s = Part.makeSphere(R, V(*c)).cut(cone_cut(R, c, 1)).cut(cone_cut(R, c, -1))
    return s.cut(cyl(HOLE_R + 0.05, 2 * R + 2, (c[0], c[1], c[2] - R - 1)))
def make_dc(c_lo, c_hi):
    """double-cup connector = end piece version with two cups back to back. The lower cup opens down and holds the top ball of M0 (centre c_lo),
    the upper cup opens up and holds the lower ball of M1 (centre c_hi). Both rims lie ZG from the ball centres, like the cups of the boom."""
    zb = -seat_depth(RB); rrim = 2.0 + (-ZG - zb) * T30; rho = rrim + 3.0
    L = (c_hi[2] - ZG) - (c_lo[2] + ZG)
    if DC_LIGHT:                                                  # outer surface = the cavity cones moved out by the wall (rho - rrim = 3 mm at the rim): a collar, then a 30 deg double cone down to DC_CORE round the wire hole
        P3 = lambda r, z: V(c_lo[0] + r, c_lo[1], c_lo[2] + ZG + z)
        if DC_FIL > 0:                                            # waist = an arc of radius DC_FIL tangent to both cones (30 deg from the axis): it is the neck, rounder and thicker than the straight core
            Rf = min(DC_FIL, 2.0 * (L / 2.0 - DC_COLLAR - 1.0)); zm = L / 2.0; s30, c30 = 0.5, math.sqrt(0.75)
            rn = rho - (zm - 0.5 * Rf - DC_COLLAR) * T30 - Rf * (1.0 - c30)                  # radius of the neck: the cone through the collar corner meets the arc tangentially
            rc = rn + Rf; q1 = (rc - Rf * c30, zm - Rf * s30); q2 = (rc - Rf * c30, zm + Rf * s30)
            ed = [Part.LineSegment(P3(0, 0), P3(rho, 0)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P3(rho, 0), P3(rho, DC_COLLAR)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P3(rho, DC_COLLAR), P3(*q1)).toShape(),
                  Part.Arc(P3(*q1), P3(rn, zm), P3(*q2)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P3(*q2), P3(rho, L - DC_COLLAR)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P3(rho, L - DC_COLLAR), P3(rho, L)).toShape(),
                  Part.LineSegment(P3(rho, L), P3(0, L)).toShape(), Part.LineSegment(P3(0, L), P3(0, 0)).toShape()]
            prof = Part.Face(Part.Wire(Part.__sortEdges__(ed)))
        else:
            z1 = min(L / 2.0, DC_COLLAR + (rho - DC_CORE) / T30); rm = rho - (z1 - DC_COLLAR) * T30
            pts = [(0, 0), (rho, 0), (rho, DC_COLLAR), (rm, z1), (rm, L - z1), (rho, L - DC_COLLAR), (rho, L), (0, L)]
            prof = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([P3(r, z) for r, z in pts] + [P3(0, 0)]))
        blk = prof.revolve(V(c_lo[0], c_lo[1], 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360)
    else: blk = cyl(rho, L, (c_lo[0], c_lo[1], c_lo[2] + ZG))
    lo = seat(RB, c_lo)[0]; lo.rotate(V(*c_lo), V(1, 0, 0), 180)         # the cone of the lower cup opens downward
    blk = blk.cut(lo).cut(seat(RB, c_hi)[0])
    return blk.cut(cyl(HOLE_R, c_hi[2] - c_lo[2], (c_lo[0], c_lo[1], c_lo[2])))
if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2:
    add("M0", make_link(R1, RB, C0a, LINK_D), PRINT); add("DC", make_dc(C0b, C1a), PRINT)
add("M1", make_link(RB, RB, C1a, D1), PRINT)
_SH_M = make_link(RB, RB, CH, LINK_T)
_SH_DC = make_dc((0, 0, HZI5a), (0, 0, HZ4a)) if any(STK_FULL(_s) for _s in STACKS) else None
_SH_M2 = make_link(RB, RB, (0, 0, HZI5b), LINK_T) if _SH_DC is not None else None
for _s in STACKS:                                                                      # the stacks hang from the far cups of the booms (the last one is the tip side); every part is built once and reused
    _mn, _dn, _m2 = SN(_s)
    add(_mn, _SH_M.copy(), PRINT, placement=SPL[_s - 1])
    if STK_FULL(_s): add(_dn, _SH_DC.copy(), PRINT, placement=SPL[_s - 1]); add(_m2, _SH_M2.copy(), PRINT, placement=SPL[_s - 1])
for _k in range(1, NBOOM):
    if not INTER: add("Ball_S%d" % (_k + 1), loose_ball(RB, (0, 0, 0)), PRINT, placement=App.Placement(BALL[_k], App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), upz(dvec(ANG_F[_k - 1])))))
# ============================== THE BOOM (rod + 2 identical end pieces; the boom is printed 3 times) ==============================
def bend_tube(r, rb, z_top, x_end, off=30.0):
    """like bend_bore, but the seam of the quarter torus is turned by `off` deg (the boolean operations of the windows fail silently with the seam in the plane of the bend)"""
    parts = []
    if z_top > rb: parts.append(cyl(r, z_top - rb, (0, 0, rb)))
    f = Part.Face(Part.Wire([Part.makeCircle(r, V(0, 0, rb), V(0, 0, 1), off, off + 360.0)]))
    parts.append(f.revolve(V(rb, 0, rb), V(0, -1, 0), 90))
    if x_end > rb: parts.append(cyl(r, x_end - rb, (rb, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
    return fuse(*parts)
def ep_cavity(zb, rho, er):
    """hollow of the end piece (tool solid, local frame of make_ep): the cavity of the cup block as in the tensioner end (roof = the seat cone offset by EP_VOID_W, 30 deg from vertical, outer wall vertical) continues
    down through the base of the block as an annulus (wall EP_VOID_W under the outer wall of the elbow, a column of radius ra round the wire) and follows the elbow for EP_VOID_TILT degrees; a 45 deg cone widens it
    from the elbow wall to the wall of the block. Nothing in it is steeper than 45 deg from the vertical (the roof of the elbow part is, at most 45 deg of tilt), its lower end is a floor. The wire tube stays. With EP_WIN open windows
    (radial hexagons through the wall of the block, one hexagon through each side wall of the elbow) connect it to the outside."""
    W = EP_VOID_W; ra = 2.0 + W / math.cos(math.radians(30.0)); rc = rho - W; rcs = RS - W
    zapex = A + zb; zk = A + zb + (rc - ra) / T30
    zs = er + 0.5
    pts = [(ra, er), (rcs, er), (rcs, zs)] + ([(rc, zs + (rc - rcs))] if rc > rcs else []) + [(rc, zk), (ra, zapex), (ra, er)]
    rev = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(r, 0, z) for r, z in pts])).revolve(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), 360)
    tilt = max(5.0, min(45.0, float(EP_VOID_TILT)))
    tor = Part.Face(Part.Wire([Part.makeCircle(rcs, V(0, 0, er), V(0, 0, 1), 30.0, 390.0)])).revolve(V(er, 0, er), V(0, -1, 0), tilt)
    pipe = bend_tube(ra, BEND_R, zapex + 0.3, XF - 4.0)                                                  # the wire tube stays (radius ra round the wire path)
    cav = fuse(rev, tor).cut(pipe)
    if EP_WIN:
        tools = []
        b = EP_WIN_B; rs = rc - 0.6
        zr = zapex + (rs - ra) / T30                                                                     # roof of the cavity at the inner end of the windows
        zsill = max(zs + (rc - rcs) + 0.2, zr - 0.6 - 2.0 * b - 1.0)
        for ang in EP_WIN_ANG:
            w = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(rs, -b, zsill), V(rs, b, zsill), V(rs, b, zsill + 1.0 + b), V(rs, 0, zsill + 2.0 * b + 1.0), V(rs, -b, zsill + 1.0 + b), V(rs, -b, zsill)])).extrude(V(6.0, 0, 0))
            w.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 1), ang); tools.append(w)
        a, hv = EP_WIN_A, 2.0
        th = math.radians(tilt * 0.5); xc = er - er * math.cos(th) + 1.0; zc = er - er * math.sin(th) - 1.0         # hexagon through both side walls, in the middle of the cavity of the elbow
        hexp = [(xc - a, zc - hv / 2.0), (xc - a, zc + hv / 2.0), (xc, zc + hv / 2.0 + a), (xc + a, zc + hv / 2.0), (xc + a, zc - hv / 2.0), (xc, zc - hv / 2.0 - a), (xc - a, zc - hv / 2.0)]
        side = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(x, -20.0, z) for x, z in hexp])).extrude(V(0, 40.0, 0)).cut(pipe)
        tools.append(side)
        cav = cav.fuse(fuse(*tools))
    return cav
def make_ep():
    """end piece, local frame: rod axis = x axis, cup centre at (0,0,A) opening up, rod flange at x = XF. Used at both ends of every boom.
    The wire runs down the cup axis, turns 90 deg on a smooth arc of radius BEND_R and leaves along the rod axis. The bore is
    open to the rod socket, so the wire is threaded through it from there after the rod is plugged on."""
    zb = -seat_depth(RB); rrim = 2.0 + (-ZG - zb) * T30; rho = rrim + 3.0
    er = max(RS + 0.5, min(float(ELBOW_R), XF - 0.5))                      # centre-line radius of the rounded elbow (a torus needs er > RS)
    chm = max(0.0, min(float(EP_CHAMFER), rho - RS - 0.2))                  # chamfer of the cup block's outer edge on the elbow side
    blk = cyl(rho, -ZG - (zb - 2), (0, 0, A + zb - 2)) if chm <= 0 else fuse(Part.makeCone(rho - chm, rho, chm, V(0, 0, A + zb - 2), V(0, 0, 1)), cyl(rho, -ZG - (zb - 2) - chm, (0, 0, A + zb - 2 + chm)))
    ep = fuse(blk, cyl(RS, A + zb + 1 - er, (0, 0, er)),                                               # cup block (chamfered), straight stem,
              bend_bore(RS, er, er, er),                                                               # quarter torus: the rounded elbow (same bend construction as the bore)
              cyl(RS, XF - er, (er, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))                                                 # short straight part up to the rod flange
    ep = ep.cut(seat(RB, (0, 0, A))[0])
    if ROD_CH > 0:
        ep = ep.cut(Part.makeCone(R_SOCK - 0.5, R_SOCK + ROD_CH, ROD_CH + 0.5, V(XF - ROD_CH - 0.5, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0)))      # conical socket (45 deg), 0.5 mm deeper than the rod end
        if ROD_ST > 0:                                                                                                                  # pocket for the stub: round below, 45 deg roof (teardrop) so the horizontal bore needs no support
            rr, q, x_a = R_SOCK, 0.70710678, XF - ROD_CH - ROD_ST - 0.5
            ep = ep.cut(fuse(cyl(rr, ROD_ST + 1.0, (x_a, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)), Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(x_a, -rr * q, rr * q), V(x_a, 0, rr * 1.41421356), V(x_a, rr * q, rr * q), V(x_a, -rr * q, rr * q)])).extrude(V(ROD_ST + 1.0, 0, 0))))
    else: ep = ep.cut(cyl(R_SOCK, 4.5, (XF - 4.5, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
    if EP_VOID and HOLE_R < 3.0:                                                                         # (skipped on a small model: the wire channel is then too wide for a hollow with 3 mm walls)
        ep = ep.cut(ep_cavity(zb, rho, er))
    ep = ep.cut(bend_bore(HOLE_R, BEND_R, A + zb + HOLE_UP, XF - 4.0))          # wire path (bare channel), up into the cup apex
    return ep
def make_rod():
    """boom rod, local frame: rod axis = x axis, flange faces at x0 = XF and x1 = L - XF. Turned profile: round spigot with a 45 deg fillet cone (ROD_CH) into the flange (R = ROD_RF, 3 mm) at both ends, concave 45 deg cone from the flange down to the core
    (R_ROD) on a longer rod. Printed standing on a spigot end every surface is at most 45 deg from the vertical (only the 2.5 mm rim of the flange is flat), so no supports."""
    x0, x1, fl = XF, L - XF, 3.0
    if x1 - x0 < 1.0:                # no rod: a short coupler peg joins the two end pieces, flange to flange
        return cyl(R_SPIG, 8.0, (XF - 4.0, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)).cut(cyl(HOLE_R, 8.0, (XF - 4.0, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
    if ROD_CH <= 0:
        rod = fuse(cyl(R_ROD, x1 - x0, (x0, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)), cyl(RS, fl, (x0, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)), cyl(RS, fl, (x1 - fl, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)),
                   cyl(R_SPIG, 4.0, (x0 - 4.0, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)), cyl(R_SPIG, 4.0, (x1, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
        rod = rod.cut(cyl(HOLE_R, (x1 - x0) + 8.0, (x0 - 4.0, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
        if x1 - x0 - 2 * fl > 14 and HOLE_R < 4: rod = rod.cut(cyl(4, x1 - x0 - 2 * fl - 2, (x0 + fl + 1, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
        return rod
    ch, nc = ROD_CH, ROD_RF - R_ROD
    st = ROD_ST
    p = [(x0 - ch - st, 0.0), (x0 - ch - st, R_SPIG), (x0 - ch, R_SPIG), (x0, R_SPIG + ch), (x0, ROD_RF), (x0 + fl, ROD_RF)]
    if x1 - x0 >= 2 * (fl + nc) + 0.2: p += [(x0 + fl + nc, R_ROD), (x1 - fl - nc, R_ROD), (x1 - fl, ROD_RF)]
    elif x1 - x0 > 2 * fl + 0.1: p += [(x1 - fl, ROD_RF)]
    p += [(x1, ROD_RF), (x1, R_SPIG + ch), (x1 + ch, R_SPIG), (x1 + ch + st, R_SPIG), (x1 + ch + st, 0.0)]
    p = [q for i, q in enumerate(p) if i == 0 or abs(q[0] - p[i - 1][0]) + abs(q[1] - p[i - 1][1]) > 1e-6]      # no zero-length edges
    rod = Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(x, r, 0) for x, r in p] + [V(p[0][0], p[0][1], 0)])).revolve(V(0, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0), 360)
    rod = rod.cut(cyl(HOLE_R, (x1 - x0) + 2 * (ch + st) + 2.0, (x0 - ch - st - 1.0, 0, 0), (1, 0, 0)))
    xa, xb = x0 + fl + 1.0, x1 - fl - 1.0
    if xb - xa > 14 and HOLE_R < 4:                 # hollow core with 45 deg cone ends
        d = 4.0 - HOLE_R
        rod = rod.cut(Part.Face(Part.makePolygon([V(xa, 0, 0), V(xa, HOLE_R, 0), V(xa + d, 4.0, 0), V(xb - d, 4.0, 0), V(xb, HOLE_R, 0), V(xb, 0, 0), V(xa, 0, 0)])).revolve(V(0, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0), 360))
    return rod
def ep_place(k, end):
    th = ANG_N[k] if end == "n" else ANG_F[k]
    rot = App.Rotation(V(1, 0, 0), th)
    if end == "f": rot = rot.multiply(App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), 180))
    return App.Placement(AXIS[k] + (V(L, 0, 0) if end == "f" else V(0, 0, 0)), rot)
EP = make_ep(); ROD = make_rod()
if EP_VOID and HOLE_R < 3.0:                    # collision proxy of the hollow end piece (solid inside): same outer shape and seats, simpler faces
    EP_VOID = False
    try: _EP_PROXY = make_ep()
    finally: EP_VOID = True
    for _k in range(NBOOM): PROXY["Boom%d_EPn" % (_k + 1)] = _EP_PROXY.copy(); PROXY["Boom%d_EPf" % (_k + 1)] = _EP_PROXY.copy()
for _k in range(NBOOM):
    add("Boom%d_EPn" % (_k + 1), EP.copy(), PRINT, placement=ep_place(_k, "n"))
    add("Boom%d_Rod" % (_k + 1), ROD.copy(), PRINT, placement=App.Placement(AXIS[_k], App.Rotation()))
    add("Boom%d_EPf" % (_k + 1), EP.copy(), PRINT, placement=ep_place(_k, "f"))
# ============================== WIRE ==============================
add("Stand_Base", BASE_SHAPE, PRINT, "printed", BASE_PL); add("Stand_TE", TE_STAND, PRINT, "printed", STAND_TE_PL); add("Tip_TE", TE_TIP, PRINT, "printed", TIP_PL) if not TIP_PROBE else None
if TIP_PROBE:
    add("Tip_Holder", TIP_HOLDER, PRINT, "printed", TIP_PL); add("Tip_Probe", PROBE_REF, (0.30, 0.32, 0.38), "ref", TIP_PL); add("Tip_Clamp_Screw", CLAMP_SCREW, TEAL, "printed", TIP_PL); add("Tip_Ferrule", FER_P, (0.8, 0.5, 0.2), "hw", TIP_PL)
for _tag, _pl in ((("Stand", STAND_TPL),) if TIP_PROBE else (("Stand", STAND_TPL), ("Tip", TIP_TAIL_PL))):
    add(_tag + "_Slider", TIP_SLIDER, PRINT, "printed", _pl); add(_tag + "_Screw", SCREW, TEAL, "printed", _pl)
    add(_tag + "_Ferrule", FERRULE, (0.8, 0.5, 0.2), "hw", _pl)
def arc_pts(cx, cz, r, a0, a1, n=9):
    return [V(cx + r * math.cos(math.radians(a0 + (a1 - a0) * i / n)), 0, cz + r * math.sin(math.radians(a0 + (a1 - a0) * i / n))) for i in range(n + 1)]
EPW = [V(0, 0, A), V(0, 0, BEND_R)] + arc_pts(BEND_R, BEND_R, BEND_R, 180, 270, 12)[1:]   # wire inside one end piece: cup centre -> rod axis
# the wire is built in pieces, one for every moving part it runs through (it kinks at the ball centres), so it follows the pose
WSEG = []      # (start, end, name of the frame that carries this piece of wire)
def _wire(pts, frame):
    for a, b in zip(pts[:-1], pts[1:]):
        if (b - a).Length > 1e-6: WSEG.append((a, b, frame))
_BWP = [V(XT, 0, TZ0 + TE_XF), V(XT, 0, zB)] + arc_pts(XB, zB, RW, 0, -90, 12)[1:] + arc_pts(RW, zB, RW, 270, 180, 12) + [V(0, 0, MAST_TOP)]      # slider -> drum B -> floor -> drum A -> straight up to the cup centre
_wire([BASE_PL.multVec(p) for p in _BWP], "BASE")
if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2: _wire([V(*C0a), V(*C0b)], "M0"); _wire([V(*C0b), V(*C1a)], "DC")
_wire([V(*C1a), V(*C1b)], "M1")
for _k in range(NBOOM):
    _wn = [ep_place(_k, "n").multVec(p) for p in EPW]; _wf = [ep_place(_k, "f").multVec(p) for p in reversed(EPW)]
    _wire(_wn + _wf[:1], "B%dn" % (_k + 1)); _wire(_wf, "B%df" % (_k + 1))      # the stretch along the rod axis stays with the near end piece
    if _k + 1 in STACKS:                                                          # the stack that hangs from the far cup of this boom: far cup centre -> M -> DC -> M (-> the near cup of the next boom)
        _P0, _P1, _P2, _P3 = STK[_k]; _mn, _dn, _m2 = SN(_k + 1)
        _wire([_wf[-1], V(*_P1)], _mn)
        if STK_FULL(_k + 1): _wire([V(*_P1), V(*_P2)], _dn); _wire([V(*_P2), V(*_P3)], _m2)
_wire([V(*CT), HEADPL.multVec(V(0, 0, HZT + (PH_ZCEIL - 4.5) if TIP_PROBE else HZT - (TD + TE_XF)))], "Head")                           # tip: straight down from the head pivot into the ferrule
WPTS = [WSEG[0][0]] + [_b for _a, _b, _f in WSEG]
WIRE_LEN = sum((_b - _a).Length for _a, _b, _f in WSEG)
WBODY = {}                                                           # frame -> wire piece that moves with it
for _fr in dict.fromkeys(_f for _a, _b, _f in WSEG):
    _off = V(0, 0, 0)
    _sg = []
    for _a, _b, _f in WSEG:
        if _f != _fr: continue
        _d = _b - _a; _sg += [Part.makeCylinder(WIRE_D / 2, _d.Length, _a + _off, _d), Part.makeSphere(WIRE_D / 2, _a + _off), Part.makeSphere(WIRE_D / 2, _b + _off)]
    add("Wire_" + _fr, Part.makeCompound(_sg), (0.9, 0.62, 0.1), "wire", None)
    if _fr != "BASE": WBODY[_fr] = ["Wire_" + _fr]
doc.recompute()
# ============================== POSE / DEGREES OF FREEDOM ==============================
def _bn(k): return ["Boom%d_EPn" % k, "Boom%d_Rod" % k]
def _bf(k): return ["Boom%d_EPf" % k]
BODY = {"M1": ["M1"]}
if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2: BODY["M0"] = ["M0"]; BODY["DC"] = ["DC"]
for _k in range(1, NBOOM + 1):
    BODY["B%dn" % _k] = _bn(_k); BODY["B%df" % _k] = _bf(_k) + (["Ball_S%d" % (_k + 1)] if (_k < NBOOM and not INTER) else [])
BODY["Head"] = list(HEAD_OBJ)
TC = [tp(AXIS[_k] + V(L / 2.0, 0, 0)) for _k in range(NBOOM)]      # a point on every rod axis; twist joints Tk turn the far end piece about the rod axis through it
if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2:
    CHAIN = [("M0", "BASE", C0a, "J0a"), ("DC", "M0", C0b, "J0b"), ("M1", "DC", C1a, "J1a"), ("B1n", "M1", C1b, "J1b")]
else:
    CHAIN = [("M1", "BASE", C1a, "J1a"), ("B1n", "M1", C1b, "J1b")]
def _add_stack(s):
    """stack s (hanging from the far cup of boom s): chain entries; returns (last frame, centre of its lower joint, name of that joint)"""
    mn, dn, m2 = SN(s); P0, P1, P2, P3 = STK[s - 1]; jn = ["J%d%s" % (s + 1, _c) for _c in "abcd"]
    BODY[mn] = [mn]; CHAIN.append((mn, "B%df" % s, P0, jn[0]))                    # a = boom cup / first link
    if STK_FULL(s):
        BODY[dn] = [dn]; BODY[m2] = [m2]
        CHAIN.append((dn, mn, P1, jn[1])); CHAIN.append((m2, dn, P2, jn[2]))     # b = first link / DC, c = DC / second link
        return m2, P3, jn[3]                                                     # d = second link / what follows
    return mn, P1, jn[1]
for _k in range(1, NBOOM + 1):
    CHAIN.append(("B%df" % _k, "B%dn" % _k, TC[_k - 1], "T%d" % _k))
    if _k < NBOOM and not INTER: CHAIN.append(("B%dn" % (_k + 1), "B%df" % _k, CB[_k], "J%d" % (_k + 1)))
    elif _k < NBOOM:
        _lf, _lc, _lj = _add_stack(_k); CHAIN.append(("B%dn" % (_k + 1), _lf, _lc, _lj))       # M - DC - M between boom k and boom k+1
HJ = ["J%d%s" % (NBOOM + 1, _c) for _c in ("a", "b", "c", "d")[:2 * TIP_LINKS]]      # tip side joint names: a = boom cup / first link, b = first link / DC, c = DC / second link, d = second link / tip end (with one link: a, b)
_lf, _lc, _lj = _add_stack(NBOOM); CHAIN.append(("Head", _lf, _lc, _lj))
assert _lj == HJ[-1]
JAX = {"J0a": V(0, 0, 1), "J0b": V(0, 0, 1), "J1a": V(0, 0, 1), "J1b": V(0, 0, 1)}
for _hj in HJ: JAX[_hj] = upz(dvec(ANG_F[-1]))
for _s in range(1, NBOOM):
    if INTER:
        for _c in "abcd": JAX["J%d%s" % (_s + 1, _c)] = upz(dvec(ANG_F[_s - 1]))
for _k in range(1, NBOOM + 1):
    JAX["T%d" % _k] = V(1, 0, 0)
    if _k < NBOOM and not INTER: JAX["J%d" % (_k + 1)] = upz(dvec(ANG_F[_k - 1]))
# ============================== SCALE: the finished model is shrunk so that the balls have the diameter BALL_D ==============================
# Everything is built at the design size (RB = 13 mm) and then scaled once about the origin: shapes, placements, joint centres, wire path.
# Forces scale with the cross-section (K^2: same wire stress), masses with the volume (K^3), the test weight like the forces.
def _sv(v): return V(v.x * KS, v.y * KS, v.z * KS)
def _st(t): return (t[0] * KS, t[1] * KS, t[2] * KS)
def _spl(pl): return App.Placement(_sv(pl.Base), pl.Rotation)
def _ssh(sh):                                     # scale the geometry, keep the orientation (print shapes carry a rotation in their placement)
    pl = sh.Placement; c = sh.copy(); c.Placement = App.Placement(); c.scale(KS); c.Placement = _spl(pl); return c
if abs(KS - 1.0) > 1e-9:
    for _n, _o in OBJ.items():
        _pl = _o.Placement; _o.Shape = _ssh(_o.Shape); _o.Placement = _spl(_pl)
    for _n in list(NEUT): NEUT[_n] = _spl(NEUT[_n])
    for _n in list(PROXY): PROXY[_n] = _ssh(PROXY[_n])
    for _n in ("EP", "ROD", "TE_TIP", "TE_STAND", "TIP_SLIDER", "SCREW", "FERRULE", "BASE_SHAPE", "TIP_SLIDER_PRINT", "SCREW_PRINT") + (("TIP_HOLDER", "PROBE_REF", "FER_P", "CLAMP_SCREW") if TIP_PROBE else ()): globals()[_n] = _ssh(globals()[_n])
    CHAIN[:] = [(_f, _p, _st(_c), _j) for _f, _p, _c, _j in CHAIN]
    TC[:] = [_st(_c) for _c in TC]; CB[:] = [_st(_c) for _c in CB]; BALL[:] = [_sv(_c) for _c in BALL]; AXIS[:] = [_sv(_c) for _c in AXIS]; FARB[:] = [_sv(_c) for _c in FARB]
    STK[:] = [tuple(_st(_p) for _p in _t) for _t in STK]
    WSEG[:] = [(_sv(_a), _sv(_b), _f) for _a, _b, _f in WSEG]; WPTS[:] = [_sv(_p) for _p in WPTS]; WIRE_LEN *= KS
    C0a = _st(C0a) if C0a else C0a; C0b = _st(C0b) if C0b else C0b; C1a = _st(C1a); C1b = _st(C1b); C4a = _st(C4a); C4b = _st(C4b); CT = _st(CT); C5a = _st(C5a) if C5a else C5a; C5b = _st(C5b) if C5b else C5b; CBASE = _st(CBASE); CH = _st(CH)
    XH *= KS; YH *= KS; XP *= KS; YP *= KS; ZTIP *= KS; WIRE_D *= KS; RB *= KS; R1 *= KS; WIRE_T *= KS * KS
    doc.recompute()
PROBE_G = 100.0 * KS * KS        # test weight at the end wall of the tip end (g): 100 g at full size, scaled like the forces
CRIMP = 20.0 * KS                # wire allowance for the two crimps (mm)
MARGINS = {}
def joint_rot(jn, phi, beta, psi):
    if jn[0] == "T": return App.Rotation(JAX[jn], psi)        # twist about the rod axis (phi, beta unused)
    a = V(-math.sin(math.radians(phi)), math.cos(math.radians(phi)), 0)
    q = App.Rotation(a, beta).multiply(App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), psi))
    Rj = App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), JAX[jn])                 # tilt is measured from the axis of the joint's cups
    return Rj.multiply(q).multiply(Rj.inverted())
def set_pose(P=None):
    """P = {"J1a": (tilt_azimuth_deg, tilt_deg, spin_deg), ...}; missing joints stay neutral. The wire follows the pose."""
    P = P or {}; pl = {"BASE": App.Placement()}
    for frame, parent, c, jn in CHAIN:
        phi, beta, psi = P.get(jn, (0, 0, 0))
        if jn[0] != "T" and abs(beta) > TILT_MAX + 1e-6: print("WARNING %s tilt %.1f exceeds the ball limit %.0f deg" % (jn, beta, TILT_MAX))
        pl[frame] = pl[parent].multiply(App.Placement(V(0, 0, 0), joint_rot(jn, phi, beta, psi), V(*c)))
        for o in BODY[frame] + WBODY.get(frame, []): OBJ[o].Placement = pl[frame].multiply(NEUT.get(o, App.Placement()))
    doc.recompute()
def check_pose(P=None, tol=None):
    """pose the stand and list every pair of parts that overlap by more than tol mm3"""
    tol = 0.5 * KS ** 3 if tol is None else tol
    set_pose(P)
    names = list(COLL_BASE) + (["M0", "DC"] if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2 else []) + ["M1"]
    for k in range(1, NBOOM + 1):
        names += ["Boom%d_EPn" % k, "Boom%d_Rod" % k, "Boom%d_EPf" % k]
        if k < NBOOM and not INTER: names.append("Ball_S%d" % (k + 1))
        if k in STACKS: names += STACK_PARTS(k)
    names += list(COLL_HEAD)
    bad = []
    for i, a in enumerate(names):
        for b in names[i + 1:]:
            if a.startswith(("Stand_", "Tip_")) and b.startswith(a.split("_")[0] + "_"): continue          # parts of one tensioner end move together
            if frozenset((a, b)) in SKIP_PAIRS: continue
            sa, sb = _located(a), _located(b)
            if not sa.BoundBox.intersect(sb.BoundBox): continue
            v = sa.common(sb).Volume
            if v > tol: bad.append((a, b, round(v, 1)))
    print("pose %s -> %s" % (P, bad if bad else "no interference"))
    return bad
def export_stl(folder):
    """one STL per printed part; end piece (print 6x) and rod (print 3x) are written once"""
    import MeshPart
    _base_print = BASE_SHAPE.copy(); _base_print.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0), 180); _base_print.translate(V(0, 0, -_base_print.BoundBox.ZMin))        # upside down: deck on the bed
    _stand_te_print = TE_STAND.copy(); _stand_te_print.translate(V(0, 0, -TE_STAND.BoundBox.ZMin))                                  # the stand end: standing on its end wall too, the column up
    _tip_print = TE_TIP.copy(); _tip_print.translate(V(0, 0, -TE_TIP.BoundBox.ZMin))
    _holder_print = TIP_HOLDER.copy() if TIP_PROBE else None
    if _holder_print is not None: _holder_print.translate(V(0, 0, -_holder_print.BoundBox.ZMin))
    _clamp_print = None
    if TIP_PROBE:
        _clamp_print = CLAMP_SCREW.copy(); _clamp_print.rotate(V(0, 0, 0), V(1, 0, 0), 90.0); _clamp_print.translate(V(0, 0, -_clamp_print.BoundBox.ZMin))        # standing on its knob, thread up               # printed standing on its end wall, cup up
    os.makedirs(folder, exist_ok=True)
    jobs = [(n + ".stl", o.Shape) for n, o in OBJ.items() if ROLE[n] == "printed" and not n.startswith(("Boom", "Stand_", "Tip_"))]
    jobs += [("End_piece_x%d.stl" % (2 * NBOOM), EP), ("Rod_x%d.stl" % NBOOM, ROD), ("Stand_base_x1.stl", _base_print), ] + ([("Stand_end_x1.stl", _stand_te_print), ("Probe_holder_x1.stl", _holder_print), ("Clamp_screw_x1.stl", _clamp_print), ("Slider_x1.stl", TIP_SLIDER_PRINT), ("Tension_screw_x1.stl", SCREW_PRINT)] if TIP_PROBE else ([("Tip_end_x2.stl", _tip_print)] if SAME_END else [("Stand_end_x1.stl", _stand_te_print), ("Tip_end_x1.stl", _tip_print)]) + [("Slider_x2.stl", TIP_SLIDER_PRINT), ("Tension_screw_x2.stl", SCREW_PRINT)])
    for fn, shp in jobs:
        MeshPart.meshFromShape(Shape=shp, LinearDeflection=0.05 * KS, AngularDeflection=0.3).write(os.path.join(folder, fn))
    print("STL files written to", folder)

def torque_margins(tension=None, mu=0.25, samples=4000, probe_g=None):
    """worst-case holding margin of every joint over random poses (every ball tilted 0..TILT_MAX, any direction),
    with the weight of everything beyond the joint + a 1 N push down and 1 N sideways at the probe tip.
    hold torque = mu * R * (T / cos60) * mean(sqrt(1 - (sin60 cos(phi))^2));  T = wire tension at that joint"""
    import random
    tension = tension or WIRE_T
    if probe_g is None: probe_g = PROBE_G
    PET = 1.27e-3; STL = 7.85e-3; steel = ("Tip_Ferrule", "Stand_Ferrule")
    def mass_com(names):
        m = 0.0; mo = V(0, 0, 0)
        for n in names:
            dens = STL if n in steel else PET
            for so in OBJ[n].Shape.Solids:
                mm = so.Volume * dens / 1000.0; m += mm; mo = mo + so.CenterOfMass * mm
        return m, mo
    jn = [c[3] for c in CHAIN]; grp = []
    for frame, parent, c, name in CHAIN:
        m, mo = mass_com([n for n in BODY[frame] if n not in ("DummyProbe", "Tip_Probe")])
        if frame == CHAIN[-1][0]:
            m += probe_g / 1000.0; mo = mo + V(XP, YP, ZTIP) * (probe_g / 1000.0)
        grp.append((len(grp), m, mo * (1.0 / m)))
    tipn = V(XP, YP, ZTIP)          # test load: 100 g (probe_g) and 1 N pushes at the tail end of the tip fixture
    RAD = {"J0a": R1, "J0b": RB, "J1a": RB, "J1b": RB}
    for _j in range(2, NBOOM + 2): RAD["J%d" % _j] = RB
    eb = math.exp(-MU_W * math.pi / 2)            # tension kept after one sliding 90 deg bend of the end pieces (capstan)
    TRANS = {"J0a": 0.952, "J0b": 0.952, "J1a": 0.952, "J1b": 0.952}                  # 0.952 = seat transmission; every boom adds two bends in front of the next ball
    for _j in range(2, NBOOM + 2): TRANS["J%d" % _j] = 0.952 * eb ** (2 * (_j - 1))
    for _hj in HJ: RAD[_hj] = RB; TRANS[_hj] = 0.952 * eb ** (2 * NBOOM)       # head joints: after all the booms
    if INTER:
        for _s in range(1, NBOOM):                                                  # the stacks between the booms: after s booms (two bends each)
            for _c in "abcd": RAD["J%d%s" % (_s + 1, _c)] = RB; TRANS["J%d%s" % (_s + 1, _c)] = 0.952 * eb ** (2 * _s)
    def hold(T, R):
        N = 720; a = math.radians(60)
        av = sum(math.sqrt(1 - (math.sin(a) * math.cos(2 * math.pi * i / N)) ** 2) for i in range(N)) / N
        return mu * (R / 1000.0) * (T / math.cos(a)) * av
    worst = {j: 0.0 for j in jn}; random.seed(5)
    for _ in range(samples):
        pls = []; pl = App.Placement()
        for frame, parent, c, name in CHAIN:
            t = TILT_MAX if random.random() < 0.5 else random.uniform(0, TILT_MAX); phi = random.uniform(0, 360)
            pl = pl.multiply(App.Placement(V(0, 0, 0), joint_rot(name, phi, t, 0), V(*c))); pls.append(pl)
        cps = [pls[k].multVec(V(*CHAIN[k][2])) for k in range(len(CHAIN))]
        pg = [(o, m, pls[o].multVec(com)) for (o, m, com) in grp]; ptip = pls[-1].multVec(tipn)
        for k in range(len(CHAIN)):
            tau = V(0, 0, 0)
            for o, m, p in pg:
                if o >= k: tau = tau + (p - cps[k]).cross(V(0, 0, -m * 9.81))
            best = 0.0
            for ang in range(0, 360, 90):
                F = V(math.cos(math.radians(ang)), math.sin(math.radians(ang)), -1.0) * (KS * KS)     # 1 N pushes at full size
                best = max(best, (tau + (ptip - cps[k]).cross(F)).Length / 1000.0)
            worst[jn[k]] = max(worst[jn[k]], best)
    print("Holding margin, wire %.1f N at the knob (x%.2f after the two bends of the base), test weight %.1f g at the tip end, seat friction %.2f (x2 with TPU seats), wire-in-bend friction %.2f:" % (tension, BASE_EFF, probe_g, mu, MU_W))
    for j in jn:
        if j[0] == "T": continue
        h = hold(tension * BASE_EFF * TRANS[j], RAD[j]); MARGINS[j] = h / worst[j]
        print("  %s need %.2f N*m | hold %.2f N*m | margin x%.2f" % (j, worst[j], h, h / worst[j]))
    return worst
# ============================== REPORT ==============================
def report():
    PET = 1.27e-3; tot = 0
    print("---- ProbeStand OneBoom (%d boom%s%s, %d tip link%s): COMBINED: base with top tensioner (H %.1f mm), tip side points %d deg (TIP_ANG), end wall face of the tip end at z=%.1f, x=%.1f, y=%.1f mm; cup directions near/far: %s ----" %
          (NBOOM, "s" if NBOOM > 1 else "", " joined by M-DC-M stacks" if INTER else "", TIP_LINKS, "s" if TIP_LINKS == 2 else "", BASE_H * KS, TIP_ANG, ZTIP, XP, YP, [(ANG_N[k], ANG_F[k]) for k in range(NBOOM)]))
    for n, o in OBJ.items():
        if ROLE[n] == "printed":
            m = o.Shape.Volume * PET; tot += m
            print("  %-12s %8.3f cm3  %7.2f g PETG  %s" % (n, o.Shape.Volume / 1000, m, "valid" if o.Shape.isValid() else "INVALID"))
    print("  printed total %.1f g.  Wire: cut %.0f mm (path %.0f mm + %.0f mm for the two crimps)." % (tot, WIRE_LEN + CRIMP, WIRE_LEN, CRIMP))
def wire_clearance(step=None):
    step = 3.0 * KS if step is None else step
    solids = [o.Shape for n, o in OBJ.items() if ROLE[n] == "printed"]
    hits = 0; n = 0; r = WIRE_D / 2 - 0.03 * KS       # 0.03 mm less: the wire lies ON the two drums of the base (tangent) and the arcs are drawn as chords
    for a, b in zip(WPTS[:-1], WPTS[1:]):
        d = b - a; Ld = d.Length
        if Ld < 1e-6: continue
        u = d * (1.0 / Ld); h = V(0, 1, 0) if abs(u.y) < 0.9 else V(0, 0, 1)
        n1 = u.cross(h); n1.normalize(); n2 = u.cross(n1); kk = max(1, int(Ld / step))
        for i in range(kk + 1):
            c = a + d * (i / float(kk))
            for off in (V(0, 0, 0), n1 * r, n1 * -r, n2 * r, n2 * -r):
                p = c + off; n += 1
                for s in solids:
                    if s.BoundBox.isInside(p) and s.isInside(p, 1e-4, True): hits += 1; break
    print("wire clearance: %d of %d sample points lie inside printed material" % (hits, n))
    return hits
if RUN_CHECKS:
    report(); torque_margins()
if CHECK_WIRE:
    wire_clearance(1.5 * KS)
if App.GuiUp:
    try:
        import FreeCADGui as Gui
        Gui.activeDocument().activeView().viewIsometric(); Gui.SendMsgToActiveView("ViewFit")
    except Exception as e:
        print("view not adjusted:", e)

# ============================== COLLISION GUARD: a move may not create a new collision ==============================
CN = list(COLL_BASE) + (["M0", "DC"] if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2 else []) + ["M1"]
for _k in range(1, NBOOM + 1):
    CN += ["Boom%d_EPn" % _k, "Boom%d_Rod" % _k, "Boom%d_EPf" % _k]
    if _k < NBOOM and not INTER: CN.append("Ball_S%d" % (_k + 1))
    if _k in STACKS: CN += STACK_PARTS(_k)
CN += list(COLL_HEAD)
SKIP_PAIRS = set()
for _k in range(1, NBOOM + 1):
    _t = ["Boom%d_EPn" % _k, "Boom%d_Rod" % _k, "Boom%d_EPf" % _k]
    for _i in range(3):
        for _j in range(_i + 1, 3): SKIP_PAIRS.add(frozenset((_t[_i], _t[_j])))

class Guard:
    """Part-against-part overlap test. While a joint turns, only (moving part, fixed part) pairs can change, so only those are tested.
    Overlaps that already exist when a drag starts are tolerated but may not grow."""
    TOL = 0.5 * KS ** 3     # mm3 (0.5 at full size)
    def __init__(self):
        self.fr = {n: "BASE" for n in BASE_OBJ}
        for fr, lst in BODY.items():
            for n in lst: self.fr[n] = fr
        self.idx = {c[0]: i for i, c in enumerate(CHAIN)}; self.idx["BASE"] = -1
        self.tp = {}
        for n in CN:
            s = PROXY[n].copy() if n in PROXY else OBJ[n].Shape.copy(); s.Placement = App.Placement(); self.tp[n] = s
    def placements(self, P):
        pl = {"BASE": App.Placement()}
        for frame, parent, c, jn in CHAIN:
            phi, beta, psi = P.get(jn, (0, 0, 0))
            pl[frame] = pl[parent].multiply(App.Placement(V(0, 0, 0), joint_rot(jn, phi, beta, psi), V(*c)))
        return pl
    def located(self, pl, names):
        out = {}
        for n in names:
            s = self.tp[n].copy(); s.Placement = pl[self.fr[n]].multiply(NEUT.get(n, App.Placement())); out[n] = s
        return out
    def prepare(self, P, i0):
        """everything from chain position i0 on moves; the rest is fixed"""
        pl = self.placements(P)
        ctx = {"mv": [n for n in CN if self.idx[self.fr[n]] >= i0], "B": self.located(pl, [n for n in CN if self.idx[self.fr[n]] < i0])}
        ctx["base"] = self.check(ctx, P, raw=True)
        return ctx
    hot = []        # pairs that blocked a move last time: tried first (a blocked drag then costs one boolean operation instead of dozens)
    def check(self, ctx, P, raw=False, first=False):
        """raw: every overlapping pair. Otherwise only pairs that overlap MORE than they did at the start of the drag; first=True stops at the first such pair (all that a verdict needs)"""
        A = self.located(self.placements(P), ctx["mv"]); out = {}; base = ctx.get("base", {}); B = ctx["B"]
        if first and not raw:
            for a, b in list(self.hot):
                if frozenset((a, b)) in SKIP_PAIRS: continue
                if a in A and b in B and A[a].BoundBox.intersect(B[b].BoundBox):
                    v = A[a].common(B[b]).Volume
                    if v > self.TOL and v > base.get((a, b), 0.0) + self.TOL: return {(a, b): v}
        for a, sa in A.items():
            ba = sa.BoundBox
            for b, sb in B.items():
                if not ba.intersect(sb.BoundBox) or frozenset((a, b)) in SKIP_PAIRS: continue
                v = sa.common(sb).Volume
                if v > self.TOL:
                    out[(a, b)] = v
                    if first and not raw and v > base.get((a, b), 0.0) + self.TOL:
                        Guard.hot = [(a, b)] + [h for h in Guard.hot if h != (a, b)][:5]; return {(a, b): v}
        if raw: return out
        return {k: v for k, v in out.items() if v > base.get(k, 0.0) + self.TOL}
    def all_overlaps(self, P):
        S = self.located(self.placements(P), CN); out = {}
        for i, a in enumerate(CN):
            for b in CN[i + 1:]:
                if self.fr[a] == self.fr[b] or frozenset((a, b)) in SKIP_PAIRS or not S[a].BoundBox.intersect(S[b].BoundBox): continue
                v = S[a].common(S[b]).Volume
                if v > self.TOL: out[(a, b)] = v
        return out

# ============================== POSE CONTROLLER (shared by the gizmo and the panel) ==============================
JOINTS = [c[3] for c in CHAIN]
if SHOULDER_LINKS == 2:
    JOINT_TEXT = {"J0a": "J0a  stand cup, lower ball of M0", "J0b": "J0b  top ball of M0 in the connector DC",
                  "J1a": "J1a  lower ball of M1 in the connector DC", "J1b": "J1b  top ball of M1 (boom cup)"}
else:
    JOINT_TEXT = {"J1a": "J1a  shoulder ball in the base cup", "J1b": "J1b  top of the shoulder link"}
for _k in range(1, NBOOM + 1):
    JOINT_TEXT["T%d" % _k] = "T%d  boom%s twist about its rod" % (_k, (" %d" % _k) if NBOOM > 1 else "")
    if _k < NBOOM and not INTER: JOINT_TEXT["J%d" % (_k + 1)] = "J%d  loose ball between boom %d and %d" % (_k + 1, _k, _k + 1)
for _s in STACKS:
    _mn, _dn, _m2 = SN(_s); _n = _s + 1 if INTER else NBOOM + 1; _full = STK_FULL(_s)
    _bm = "boom" if NBOOM == 1 else "boom %d" % _s
    JOINT_TEXT["J%da" % _n] = "J%da  %s, upper ball in the end cup of %s" % (_n, _mn, _bm if _s == NBOOM and NBOOM == 1 else ("the " + _bm if _s == NBOOM else _bm))
    if _full:
        JOINT_TEXT["J%db" % _n] = "J%db  lower ball of %s in the connector %s" % (_n, _mn, _dn)
        JOINT_TEXT["J%dc" % _n] = "J%dc  upper ball of %s in the connector %s" % (_n, _m2, _dn)
        JOINT_TEXT["J%dd" % _n] = ("J%dd  lower ball of %s in the cup of the tip end" % (_n, _m2)) if _s == NBOOM else ("J%dd  lower ball of %s in the near cup of boom %d" % (_n, _m2, _s + 1))
    else:
        JOINT_TEXT["J%db" % _n] = "J%db  lower ball of %s in the cup of the tip end" % (_n, _mn)
RING_TEXT = {"X": "tilt about the X ring axis", "Y": "tilt about the Y ring axis", "Z": "spin about the cup axis"}

class Ctrl:
    def __init__(self):
        self.guard = Guard(); self.idx = {j: i for i, j in enumerate(JOINTS)}
        self.pose = {j: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0] for j in JOINTS}      # tilt direction, tilt, spin (deg); twist joints use the last one only
        self.sel = DEFAULT_JOINT if DEFAULT_JOINT in JOINTS else JOINTS[0]; self.step = 1.0; self.gizmo = None; self.panel = None; self.obs = None; self.st = None
    def pdict(self): return {j: tuple(v) for j, v in self.pose.items()}
    def apply(self, P, i0=0, final=False):
        pl = self.guard.placements(P)
        for frame, parent, c, jn in CHAIN[i0:]:
            for o in BODY[frame] + WBODY.get(frame, []): OBJ[o].Placement = pl[frame].multiply(NEUT.get(o, App.Placement()))
        if final: doc.recompute()
    def say(self, text):
        print("ProbeStand:", text)
        if self.panel is not None: self.panel.set_status(text)
        try: Gui.getMainWindow().statusBar().showMessage(text, 6000)
        except Exception: pass
    # --- rotations: pose <-> rotation in the joint frame (tilt measured from the cup axis, like joint_rot)
    @staticmethod
    def q_of(p):
        a = V(-math.sin(math.radians(p[0])), math.cos(math.radians(p[0])), 0)
        return App.Rotation(a, p[1]).multiply(App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), p[2]))
    @staticmethod
    def to_pose(q, prev):
        v = q.multVec(V(0, 0, 1)); beta = math.degrees(math.acos(max(-1.0, min(1.0, v.z))))
        phi = prev[0] if beta < 1e-6 else math.degrees(math.atan2(v.y, v.x))
        qt = App.Rotation(V(-math.sin(math.radians(phi)), math.cos(math.radians(phi)), 0), beta)
        r = qt.inverted().multiply(q).multVec(V(1, 0, 0))
        return [phi % 360.0, beta, math.degrees(math.atan2(r.y, r.x))]
    def frame_of(self, jn):
        """where the gizmo sits: at the joint centre, z = cup axis (rod axis for a twist), fixed to the part that does not move"""
        pl = self.guard.placements(self.pdict()); frame, parent, c, _ = CHAIN[self.idx[jn]]
        return App.Placement(pl[parent].multVec(V(*c)), pl[parent].Rotation.multiply(App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), JAX[jn])))
    def ring_text(self, jn, ax): return "twist about the rod axis" if jn[0] == "T" else RING_TEXT[ax]
    def describe(self, jn):
        p = self.pose[jn]
        return "%s: twist %.1f deg" % (jn, p[2]) if jn[0] == "T" else "%s: tilt %.1f deg toward %.0f deg, spin %.1f deg" % (jn, p[1], p[0], p[2])
    # --- one drag of a ring
    def begin_drag(self):
        jn = self.sel; i = self.idx[jn]
        self.st = {"jn": jn, "i": i, "p0": list(self.pose[jn]), "ok": list(self.pose[jn]), "ok_deg": 0.0, "why": None,
                   "twist": jn[0] == "T", "ctx": self.guard.prepare(self.pdict(), i)}
        return lambda axis, deg, st=self.st: self.preview(st, axis, deg)
    def candidate(self, st, axis, deg):
        p0 = st["p0"]
        if st["twist"]:
            newp = [0.0, 0.0, p0[2] + deg]; return newp, App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), newp[2])
        q = App.Rotation(V(*axis), deg).multiply(self.q_of(p0))
        return self.to_pose(q, p0), q
    def verdict(self, st, newp):
        if not st["twist"] and newp[1] > TILT_MAX + 1e-6: return "tilt limit of %.0f deg" % TILT_MAX
        P = self.pdict(); P[st["jn"]] = tuple(newp)
        bad = self.guard.check(st["ctx"], P, first=True)
        if bad:
            (a, b), v = max(bad.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]); return "%s would hit %s" % (a, b)
        return None
    def preview(self, st, axis, deg):
        newp, q = self.candidate(st, axis, deg); okp = newp; key = (tuple(axis), deg > 0); blk = st.get("blk")
        if blk is not None and blk[0] == key and abs(deg) >= blk[1] - 1e-9 and st.get("why"): problem = st["why"]; okp = st["ok"]        # known blocked from here on: keep the last clear angle
        else:
            problem = self.verdict(st, newp)
            st["blk"] = None if problem is None else ((key, min(abs(deg), blk[1]) if (blk is not None and blk[0] == key) else abs(deg)))
        if blk is not None and blk[0] == key and abs(deg) >= blk[1] - 1e-9 and st.get("why"): pass
        elif problem is None: st["ok_deg"] = deg
        else:                                    # stop at the last clear angle (bisection between the last clear one and the request)
            lo, hi, okp = st["ok_deg"], deg, st["ok"]
            for _ in range(4):
                mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi); np_, _q = self.candidate(st, axis, mid)
                if self.verdict(st, np_) is None: lo, okp = mid, np_
                else: hi = mid
            st["ok_deg"] = lo
        st["ok"] = okp; st["why"] = problem
        P = self.pdict(); P[st["jn"]] = tuple(okp); self.apply(P, st["i"])
        if st["twist"]:
            d0 = self.twist_dir(st["jn"]); heading = App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), newp[2]).multVec(d0)
            note = "twist %.1f deg" % okp[2]
        else:
            heading = q.multVec(V(0, 0, 1)); note = "tilt %.1f of %.0f deg, spin %.1f" % (okp[1], TILT_MAX, okp[2])
        if heading.Length < 1e-9: heading = V(0, 0, 1)
        return {"heading": heading, "path": None, "problem": problem, "note": note}
    def twist_dir(self, jn):
        """direction from the rod axis to the far cup, in the gizmo frame of the twist joint"""
        k = int(jn[1]) - 1; w = FARB[k] - V(*TC[k]); w = V(0, w.y, w.z)
        d = App.Rotation(V(0, 0, 1), JAX[jn]).inverted().multVec(w); d.normalize(); return d
    def commit(self, deg=0.0):
        st = self.st; self.st = None
        if st is None: return
        self.pose[st["jn"]] = list(st["ok"]); self.apply(self.pdict(), st["i"], final=True)
        txt = self.describe(st["jn"])
        if st["why"]: txt += "   - stopped: %s" % st["why"]
        self.say(txt); self.refresh()
    def restore(self):
        st = self.st; self.st = None
        self.apply(self.pdict(), st["i"] if st else 0, final=True)
    # --- panel fields, buttons
    def set_value(self, jn, k, val):
        new = list(self.pose[jn]); new[k] = val
        st = {"twist": jn[0] == "T", "jn": jn}; st["ctx"] = self.guard.prepare(self.pdict(), self.idx[jn])
        why = self.verdict(st, new)
        if why:
            self.say("%s not changed: %s" % (jn, why))
        else:
            self.pose[jn] = new; self.apply(self.pdict(), self.idx[jn], final=True); self.say(self.describe(jn))
        self.refresh()
    def reset(self, jn=None):
        for j in ([jn] if jn else JOINTS): self.pose[j] = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        self.apply(self.pdict(), 0, final=True); self.say("%s back to neutral" % (jn or "all joints")); self.refresh()
    def check_all(self):
        bad = self.guard.all_overlaps(self.pdict())
        self.say("no overlaps in this pose" if not bad else "OVERLAPS: " + "; ".join("%s x %s %.0f mm3" % (a, b, v) for (a, b), v in bad.items()))
        return bad
    def select(self, jn):
        self.sel = jn; self.refresh(); self.say(self.describe(jn))      # the panel has no value boxes: the status line shows the pose of the selected joint
    def set_step(self, s):
        self.step = s
        if self.gizmo is not None: self.gizmo.set_angle_step(s)
    def refresh(self):
        if self.panel is not None: self.panel.sync()
        self.show_gizmo()
    def picked(self, obj_name, pos):
        fr = self.guard.fr.get(obj_name)
        if fr is None: return
        i = self.guard.idx[fr]
        cands = JOINTS[:i + 1] if i >= 0 else JOINTS[:1]
        if pos is None or abs(pos[0]) + abs(pos[1]) + abs(pos[2]) < 1e-9: best = cands[-1]      # chosen in the tree (no click point): the joint that carries the part
        else:
            p = V(*pos); best = min(cands, key=lambda j: (self.frame_of(j).Base - p).Length)
        if best != self.sel: self.select(best)
    def show_gizmo(self):
        if not App.GuiUp or "ProbeGizmo" not in globals(): return
        if self.gizmo is None: self.gizmo = ProbeGizmo(Gui.ActiveDocument.ActiveView, self)
        self.gizmo.set_joint(self.frame_of(self.sel), ("Z",) if self.sel[0] == "T" else ("X", "Y", "Z"), self.sel)
    def teardown(self):
        try:
            if self.gizmo is not None: self.gizmo.destroy()
        except Exception as e: print("gizmo:", e)
        try:
            if self.obs is not None: Gui.Selection.removeObserver(self.obs)
        except Exception: pass
        try:
            if self.panel is not None: self.panel.close(); self.panel.deleteLater()
        except Exception: pass
        self.gizmo = self.panel = self.obs = None

# ============================== GIZMO + PANEL (GUI only) ==============================
NEUTRAL_BAD = {}
if App.GuiUp:
    import FreeCADGui as Gui
    from PySide import QtCore, QtWidgets
    try:
        import wire_harness as _wh        # the rotate gizmo of the Wire Harness Designer (same folder as this macro)
    except Exception as _e:
        _wh = None; print("ProbeStand: wire_harness.py not found, the gizmo is off (the panel still works):", _e)

    if _wh is not None:
        class ProbeGizmo(_wh.DragGizmo):
            """The Wire Harness gizmo, reduced to rings and placed in the frame of the selected joint: z = cup axis (spin ring),
            x and y = tilt rings. A twist joint only has the ring about its rod. Every turn is checked by the Ctrl (no new collisions)."""
            def __init__(self, view, ctrl):
                super().__init__(view, lambda *a: None, self._turned, self._factory, None)
                self.ctrl = ctrl; self.local = App.Placement(); self.enabled = ("X", "Y", "Z"); self.jn = ""
                self.xf = self._coin.SoTransform(); self.sep.insertChild(self.xf, 2)         # everything after it is drawn in the joint frame
                for k in ("move:X", "move:Y", "move:Z", "center"): self.sep.removeChild(self.handles[k])
                self.set_angle_step(ctrl.step)
            def _factory(self): return self.ctrl.begin_drag()
            def _turned(self, axis, deg): self.ctrl.commit(deg)
            def set_joint(self, frame, enabled, jn):
                self.local, self.enabled, self.jn = frame, tuple(enabled), jn
                q = frame.Rotation.Q
                self.xf.translation = tuple(frame.Base); self.xf.rotation = self._coin.SbRotation(q[0], q[1], q[2], q[3])
                self.rings.removeAllChildren()
                for ax in self.enabled: self.rings.addChild(self.handles["turn:" + ax])
                self.set_target((0, 0, 0), rings=True)
            # the geometry of the base class works in the joint frame: convert what the camera sees
            def _ray(self, x, y):
                o, d = _wh._ViewMath._ray(self, x, y); inv = self.local.inverse()
                return inv.multVec(o), inv.Rotation.multVec(d)
            def project(self, point): return _wh._ViewMath.project(self, self.local.multVec(point))
            def project_all(self, points): return _wh._ViewMath.project_all(self, [self.local.multVec(p) for p in points])
            def _cam_axes(self):
                r, u = _wh._ViewMath._cam_axes(self); inv = self.local.Rotation.inverted()
                return inv.multVec(r), inv.multVec(u)
            def _pick(self, x, y):
                grab = _wh._GRAB_PIXELS * self._dpr(); c, s = self.center, self._s
                best, best_score = None, 0.0
                for ax in self.enabled:
                    _, u, v = (V(*q) for q in _wh._GIZMO_AXES[ax]); n = 48
                    pts = self.project_all([c + (u * math.cos(2 * math.pi * k / n) + v * math.sin(2 * math.pi * k / n)) * (_wh._GIZMO_RING * s) for k in range(n + 1)])
                    score = min(_wh._seg_dist((x, y), pts[k], pts[k + 1]) for k in range(n)) - grab
                    if score < best_score: best, best_score = "turn:" + ax, score
                return best
            def _hint(self, hid):
                return "%s: %s. Drag the ring (Shift = fine, arrow keys = one step, Esc cancels)." % (self.jn, self.ctrl.ring_text(self.jn, hid.partition(":")[2]))
            def _cancel(self):
                super()._cancel(); self.ctrl.restore()
            def _abort(self):
                super()._abort(); self.ctrl.restore()

    def _macro_path():
        for p in (globals().get("__file__"), os.path.join(App.getUserMacroDir(True), "ProbeStand_OneBoom_Combined.FCMacro")):
            if p and os.path.isfile(p) and "probestand" in os.path.basename(p).lower(): return p
        raise RuntimeError("macro file not found")
    def _rebuild_with(ov):
        """run this macro again with other values (ov: name -> value for the parameters the panel may change); the old model and panel are closed first, the pose is carried over"""
        try:
            QtWidgets.QApplication.setOverrideCursor(QtCore.Qt.WaitCursor)
            try: Gui.getMainWindow().statusBar().showMessage("ProbeStand: rebuilding with M length %g mm ..." % ov.get("M_LEN", 0), 0)
            except Exception: pass
            p = _macro_path(); src = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read(); keep = CTRL.pdict() if CTRL is not None else None; old = doc.Name
            if CTRL is not None: CTRL.teardown()
            try: App.closeDocument(old)
            except Exception as e: print("ProbeStand: old model not closed:", e)
            g = globals(); g["PS_OVERRIDE"] = dict(ov); g["_POSE_KEEP"] = keep
            exec(compile(src, p, "exec"), g)
        except Exception:
            import traceback; traceback.print_exc()
        finally:
            QtWidgets.QApplication.restoreOverrideCursor()
    class SelObs:
        """Clicking a part in the 3D view selects the nearest joint that moves it."""
        def __init__(self, ctrl): self.ctrl = ctrl
        def addSelection(self, document, obj, sub, pos):
            try:
                if document == globals()["doc"].Name: self.ctrl.picked(obj, pos)
            except Exception as e: print("ProbeStand selection:", e)

    class Panel(QtWidgets.QDockWidget):
        def __init__(self, ctrl):
            mw = Gui.getMainWindow()
            for w in mw.findChildren(QtWidgets.QDockWidget):
                if w.objectName() == "ProbeStandPanel": w.close(); w.deleteLater()
            super().__init__("Probe stand", mw)
            self.setObjectName("ProbeStandPanel"); self.ctrl = ctrl; self._syncing = False
            self.setWidget(self._pose_tab())
            mw.addDockWidget(QtCore.Qt.RightDockWidgetArea, self); self.show()
            def _fit():          # the dock area keeps the width of the previous panel until the layout has settled: set the compact width afterwards
                try: mw.resizeDocks([self], [self.widget().sizeHint().width() + 12], QtCore.Qt.Horizontal)
                except Exception: pass
            _fit(); QtCore.QTimer.singleShot(0, _fit); QtCore.QTimer.singleShot(300, _fit)
            self.visibilityChanged.connect(self._vis)
        def _vis(self, shown):
            try:
                if not shown and self.ctrl.gizmo is not None: self.ctrl.gizmo.hide()
                elif shown: self.ctrl.show_gizmo()
            except Exception: pass
        # ---- pose tab
        def _pose_tab(self):
            HINT = "Click a part or pick a joint, then drag a ring of the gizmo.\nA turn that would create a new collision stops at the last clear angle."
            w = QtWidgets.QWidget(); lay = QtWidgets.QVBoxLayout(w); lay.setContentsMargins(4, 4, 4, 4); lay.setSpacing(3); w.setToolTip(HINT)
            g = QtWidgets.QGridLayout(); g.setContentsMargins(0, 0, 0, 0); g.setHorizontalSpacing(4); g.setVerticalSpacing(1); g.setColumnStretch(0, 1); g.setColumnStretch(1, 1)
            def cap(text, tip, r, c, span=1):
                lb = QtWidgets.QLabel(text); lb.setToolTip(tip); lb.setAlignment(QtCore.Qt.AlignHCenter | QtCore.Qt.AlignBottom); g.addWidget(lb, r, c, 1, span); return lb
            # row 0: joint chooser (long joint texts only in the drop-down list) with previous / next
            self.combo = QtWidgets.QComboBox()
            for j in JOINTS: self.combo.addItem(JOINT_TEXT[j], j)
            self.combo.setSizeAdjustPolicy(QtWidgets.QComboBox.AdjustToMinimumContentsLengthWithIcon); self.combo.setMinimumContentsLength(8)
            self.combo.view().setMinimumWidth(self.combo.view().sizeHintForColumn(0) + 24)
            self.combo.currentIndexChanged.connect(lambda _i: None if self._syncing else self.ctrl.select(self.combo.currentData()))
            g.addWidget(self.combo, 0, 0, 1, 2)
            # row 1: previous / next joint, the same buttons as the reset buttons
            b1, b2 = QtWidgets.QPushButton("<"), QtWidgets.QPushButton(">")
            for b, tip in ((b1, "previous joint"), (b2, "next joint")): b.setToolTip(tip)
            b1.clicked.connect(lambda: self._step(-1)); b2.clicked.connect(lambda: self._step(1))
            g.addWidget(b1, 1, 0); g.addWidget(b2, 1, 1)
            # (no direction / tilt / spin boxes: the pose is set with the gizmo; the values of the selected joint are shown in the status line; CTRL.set_value(joint, k, deg) remains for the console)
            # rows 2-3: gizmo step | gizmo size
            self.stepbox = QtWidgets.QComboBox()
            for v in (0.1, 0.5, 1, 5, 15, 45): self.stepbox.addItem("%g deg" % v, float(v))
            self.stepbox.setCurrentIndex(max(0, self.stepbox.findData(float(self.ctrl.step))))
            self.stepbox.currentIndexChanged.connect(lambda _i: self.ctrl.set_step(self.stepbox.currentData()))
            self.size = QtWidgets.QSpinBox(); self.size.setRange(50, 300); self.size.setSuffix(" %")
            self.size.setValue(_wh._gizmo_percent() if _wh else 100)
            self.size.valueChanged.connect(lambda v: self.ctrl.gizmo.set_size(v) if self.ctrl.gizmo is not None else None)
            self.stepbox.setToolTip("Gizmo step: angle of one arrow-key step (and the snap of a ring drag)"); self.size.setToolTip("Gizmo size in the 3D view")
            cap("Gizmo step", self.stepbox.toolTip(), 2, 0); cap("Gizmo size", self.size.toolTip(), 2, 1); g.addWidget(self.stepbox, 3, 0); g.addWidget(self.size, 3, 1)
            # row 4: the two reset buttons (no overlap check button: every move is checked by the Ctrl, the neutral pose at the start; CTRL.check_all() still exists for the console)
            for k, (txt, tip, fn) in enumerate((("Reset joint", "Reset the selected joint to neutral", lambda: self.ctrl.reset(self.ctrl.sel)), ("Reset all", "Reset every joint to neutral", lambda: self.ctrl.reset()))):
                bt = QtWidgets.QPushButton(txt); bt.setToolTip(tip); bt.clicked.connect(lambda _c=False, fn=fn: fn()); g.addWidget(bt, 4, k)
            # rows 5-6: length of the M links (rebuilds the model; the pose is kept when it is still free of collisions)
            cap("M length", "Ball-centre distance of the %d M links (M0 .. M%d): 36 .. 120 mm. Rebuilds the whole model (about 20 s); the pose is kept when it is still free of collisions." % (NMLINK, NMLINK - 1), 5, 0, 2)
            self.mlen = QtWidgets.QSpinBox(); self.mlen.setRange(36, 120); self.mlen.setSuffix(" mm"); self.mlen.setValue(int(round(M_LEN)))
            self.mlen.setToolTip("Length of the %d M links (M0 .. M%d), ball centre to ball centre" % (NMLINK, NMLINK - 1))
            bm = QtWidgets.QPushButton("Rebuild"); bm.setToolTip("Rebuild the model with this M length (about 20 s)"); bm.clicked.connect(lambda _c=False: self._rebuild_m())
            g.addWidget(self.mlen, 6, 0); g.addWidget(bm, 6, 1)
            lay.addLayout(g)
            lay.addStretch(1)         # no status line and no results box in the panel: messages go to the FreeCAD status bar and the Report view
            return w
        def _rebuild_m(self):
            v = self.mlen.value()
            if abs(v - float(M_LEN)) < 1e-9 and M_LEN_TIP <= 0: self.ctrl.say("the M links are already %d mm long" % v); return
            QtCore.QTimer.singleShot(0, lambda: _rebuild_with({"M_LEN": float(v), "M_LEN_TIP": 0}))      # after this click: the panel is replaced
        def _step(self, d):
            i = (JOINTS.index(self.ctrl.sel) + d) % len(JOINTS); self.ctrl.select(JOINTS[i])
        def sync(self):
            c = self.ctrl; self._syncing = True
            try:
                self.combo.setCurrentIndex(self.combo.findData(c.sel)); self.combo.setToolTip(self.combo.currentText())
            finally: self._syncing = False
        def set_status(self, text): pass                      # Ctrl.say already prints it and shows it in the FreeCAD status bar
        def set_results(self, text): print("ProbeStand:\n  " + text.replace("\n", "\n  "))

    if OPEN_PANEL:
        try:
            NEUTRAL_BAD = Guard().all_overlaps({})
            CTRL = Ctrl()
            _pk = globals().pop("_POSE_KEEP", None)                       # pose of the model that was replaced (rebuild from the panel)
            if _pk and set(_pk) == set(JOINTS):
                if not CTRL.guard.all_overlaps(_pk): CTRL.pose = {j: list(v) for j, v in _pk.items()}; CTRL.apply(CTRL.pdict(), 0, final=True)
                else: print("ProbeStand: the old pose collides with the new link length, all joints back to neutral")
            elif START_POSE:                                              # first start: the pose of START_POSE (if it is free of collisions)
                _sp = {j: tuple(START_POSE.get(j, (0.0, 0.0, 0.0))) for j in JOINTS}
                if not CTRL.guard.all_overlaps(_sp): CTRL.pose = {j: list(v) for j, v in _sp.items()}; CTRL.apply(CTRL.pdict(), 0, final=True)
                else: print("ProbeStand: START_POSE collides, all joints neutral")
            if not MARGINS: torque_margins()
            CTRL.panel = Panel(CTRL); CTRL.obs = SelObs(CTRL); Gui.Selection.addObserver(CTRL.obs)
            _mass = sum(o.Shape.Volume for n, o in OBJ.items() if ROLE[n] == "printed") * 1.27e-3
            CTRL.panel.set_results("tip end wall face x %.1f y %.1f z %.1f | wire cut %.0f mm | printed %.1f g\nholding margins (%.1f g at the tip end): %s\nneutral pose: %s" % (
                XP, YP, ZTIP, WIRE_LEN + CRIMP, _mass, PROBE_G, "  ".join("%s %.1f" % (j, m) for j, m in MARGINS.items()),
                "no overlaps" if not NEUTRAL_BAD else "OVERLAPS " + "; ".join("%s x %s" % k for k in NEUTRAL_BAD)))
            CTRL.panel.sync(); CTRL.show_gizmo()
        except Exception:
            import traceback; traceback.print_exc()
if START_POSE and not (App.GuiUp and OPEN_PANEL):                    # without the panel: just pose the model
    try: set_pose({j: tuple(START_POSE.get(j, (0.0, 0.0, 0.0))) for j in JOINTS})
    except Exception: import traceback; traceback.print_exc()
